  {t="A", seg=9, q={2841}, names={"Rig Wars"}, text="Nogg in the Valley of Honor. The Rig Blueprints are on an elite robot, the safe combination on Mekgineer Thermaplugg, the last boss.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=76.0, y=25.4, dg=9},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={2842}, names={"Chief Engineer Scooty"}, text="Sovik, next to Nogg. It sends you to Scooty in Booty Bay.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=75.5, y=25.4, dg=9},
  {t="N", seg=9, arg="Leave Orgrimmar by the main gate and take the zeppelin to the Undercity", text="Frezza's platform, on the tower just outside the gate. The zeppelin lands at the tower in Tirisfal Glades", zone="Durotar", map=1411, x=50.8, y=13.5},
  {t="FLY", seg=9, arg="The Sepulcher", text="Walk south from the tower into the Undercity. Bat handler Michael Garrett stands by the west elevator in the Trade Quarter", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=63.3, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={1013}, names={"The Book of Ur"}, zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=53.7, y=54.5, dg=4},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={63}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Ride west from the Sepulcher (Ghost Wolf) to the shrine on the coast. Kill the Corrupt Minor Manifestation of Water (level 22) at the pool for its bracers. The Corrupt Water Spirits (19) around it are easy. Check that you still have the Water Sapta Islen gave you for the vial: you need it at the brazier", zone="Silverpine Forest", map=1421, x=38.8, y=44.3},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={63}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Click the Brazier of Everfount to place the bracers and the Remaining Drops of Purest Water", zone="Silverpine Forest", map=1421, x=38.3, y=44.6},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={100}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="The brazier gives the next part right away", zone="Silverpine Forest", map=1421, x=38.3, y=44.6},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={100}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Drink the Water Sapta: it lets you see the Minor Manifestation of Water beside the brazier. Talk to it before the effect wears off. If it runs out, Tiev Mordune (37.3, 44.1) has a backup quest, but it needs a new sapta from Islen", zone="Silverpine Forest", map=1421, x=38.3, y=44.6},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={96}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Keep the Shard of Water for Islen Waterseer (next segment): that hand-in gives your Water Totem", zone="Silverpine Forest", map=1421, x=38.3, y=44.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=9, arg="Tarren Mill", text="Back to Karos Razok at the Sepulcher"},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={509}, names={"Elixir of Agony"}, text="Apothecary Lydon", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.4, y=19.1},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={98094}, names={"Scout Support"}, text="Deathstalker Masoj, on the high ground straight south of Tarren Mill, above Nethander Stead", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=64.0, y=53.8},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98095}, names={"Valuable Vantages"}, text="Three vials to place (south, north and west). At each spot look for a crushed empty vial on the ground", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=64.0, y=53.8},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={509}, names={"Elixir of Agony"}, text="Mudsnout Blossoms grow in the fields of Nethander Stead, just south of Masoj. Mudsnout Gnolls and Shamans (26-28) walk among them: Earth Shock the Shamans when they cast", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=64.4, y=61.3},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={98095}, obj={3}, names={"Valuable Vantages"}, text="Southern vial: on the hills bordering Dun Garok, the dwarf fort southeast of Nethander Stead. Search the hilltops and slopes around the fort from outside its walls for the crushed empty vial and place yours. Do not go inside or up its gate road: the Dun Garok Mountaineers, Riflemen and Priests (28-30) are ELITE and stand in groups. Feral Mountain Lions (27-28) roam the slopes: pull them one at a time and heal between fights"},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={98095}, obj={2}, names={"Valuable Vantages"}, text="Northern vial: on the plateau overlooking Durnholde Keep, the Syndicate castle east of Masoj, on your way back north. The Syndicate around the keep are only level 20-24"},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={509}, names={"Elixir of Agony"}, text="Back in Tarren Mill", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.4, y=19.1},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={513}, names={"Elixir of Agony"}, text="Keep the Mudsnout Composite for Faranell in the Undercity at the end of this segment", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.4, y=19.1},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={529}, names={"Battle of Hillsbrad"}, text="Ride west along the road to Hillsbrad Fields (Ghost Wolf), keeping clear of Southshore and its guards to the south. Blacksmith Verringtan (26) and his 4 apprentices work at the smithy; the Shipment of Iron crate is by the forge. Already done on your first visit? Go on. Every human here can drop a skull for Souvenirs of Death", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=31.8, y=45.3},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={567}, obj={2}, names={"Dangerous!"}, text="Citizen Wilkes walks the north side of the town", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=32.6, y=39.8},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={567}, obj={4}, names={"Dangerous!"}, text="Farmer Kalaba works the fields east of the town (already done if you killed her on the last visit)", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=35.9, y=46.6},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={529}, names={"Battle of Hillsbrad"}, text="Back to High Executor Darthalia, Tarren Mill", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.3, y=20.4},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={532}, names={"Battle of Hillsbrad"}, zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.3, y=20.4},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={532}, names={"Battle of Hillsbrad"}, text="Town hall: kill Magistrate Burnside (level 30) and 4 Hillsbrad Councilmen, destroy the Proclamation and take the Town Registry, both inside. Pull one at a time; if two come, drop a Stoneclaw Totem and Earth Shock the extra. Heal up between pulls", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=30.3, y=42.3, path={{63.6,22.9},{66.0,23.8},{66.0,25.6},{63.4,28.3},{62.8,32.2},{60.0,31.3},{57.2,26.2},{43.2,29.5},{38.6,34.9},{35.0,34.9}}},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={567}, obj={1}, names={"Dangerous!"}, text="Clerk Horrace Whitesteed is in the town hall", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=29.5, y=42.4},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={532}, names={"Battle of Hillsbrad"}, text="Darthalia, Tarren Mill", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.3, y=20.4, path={{29.4,40.9},{31.4,40.3},{35.0,34.9},{38.6,34.9},{42.4,29.8},{50.6,28.6},{54.0,26.2},{57.2,26.2},{60.0,31.3},{62.8,32.2},{63.4,28.3},{66.0,25.6},{66.0,23.8},{63.6,22.9}}},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={539}, names={"Battle of Hillsbrad"}, text="Skip the next part (541) later: it is elite", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.3, y=20.4},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={98095}, obj={1}, names={"Valuable Vantages"}, text="Western vial: on the ridge of the Headland above Hillsbrad Fields, on the way to the mine. Run past the bears and moss creepers on the slopes; no need to fight them"},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={539}, names={"Battle of Hillsbrad"}, text="Azurelode Mine, south of Hillsbrad Fields: Foreman Bonds (30) and 10 Hillsbrad Miners. Miners and Foremen stand close together: pull one and put down an Earthbind Totem if it runs", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=29.9, y=55.6, path={{27.1,58.5}}, cave=true},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={567}, obj={3}, names={"Dangerous!"}, text="Miner Hackett (29), deep in the mine", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=31.1, y=58.6, path={{27.1,58.5}}, cave=true},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={546}, names={"Souvenirs of Death"}, text="Finish the 30 skulls on the miners if you still need them", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=29.9, y=55.5},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={546}, names={"Souvenirs of Death"}, text="Deathguard Samsa, Tarren Mill", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.1, y=19.7},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={539}, names={"Battle of Hillsbrad"}, text="Darthalia", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.3, y=20.4},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={567}, names={"Dangerous!"}, zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.3, y=20.5},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={98095}, names={"Valuable Vantages"}, text="Ride south to Deathstalker Masoj once more", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=64.0, y=53.8},
  {t="L", seg=9, lvl=29, text="Not 29 yet? Kill Mudsnout Gnolls and Shamans (26-28) at Nethander Stead, just south of Masoj", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.8, y=62.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=9, arg="Undercity", text="Ride back north to Tarren Mill and fly from Zarise"},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={513}, names={"Elixir of Agony"}, text="Master Apothecary Faranell, in the Apothecarium", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.8, y=69.3},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={515}, names={"Elixir of Agony"}, text="Keep it for your next Hillsbrad visit. Its follow-up (517) is elite: skip it later", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.8, y=69.3},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={1109}, names={"Going, Going, Guano!"}, text="Master Apothecary Faranell in the Apothecarium. Kraul Guano drops from the bats inside. Needs level 30.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.8, y=69.3, dg=8},
  {t="N", seg=9, arg="Open Elixir of Agony (515) in your quest log and buy the troll's blood potion it lists at the Auction House in the Trade Quarter", text="Forever's quest page lists a Lesser Troll's Blood Elixir, the old quest text a Strong Troll's Blood Potion: buy whichever your log shows. If none is for sale, you drop 515 later"},
  {t="H", seg=9, arg="Crossroads", text="Hearth back to the Crossroads"},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1145}, names={"The Swarm Grows"}, text="Korran, next to the Crossroads flight master. Keep his sealed note for your next Orgrimmar visit. Not offered yet (needs 29)? Then fly Freewind Post -> Crossroads at the end of this segment, take it, and fly on to Ratchet", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=51.1, y=29.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=10, arg="Ratchet", text="You start at the Crossroads, hearthed back from the Undercity"},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={96}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Islen Waterseer, on the beach south of Ratchet next to Mahren Skyseer. You get the Water Totem and learn Healing Stream Totem; your other water totems (Mana Spring, Poison Cleansing) now work too", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=65.8, y=43.8},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1221}, names={"Blueleaf Tubers"}, text="Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet. Take the crate, the command stick and the manual next to him. In the kraul, let the gopher out near the blueleaf trail and use the stick to make it dig up 6 tubers.", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.4, y=37.6, dg=8},
  {t="FLY", seg=10, arg="Thunder Bluff", text="Run back to the Ratchet flight master. The flight goes through the Crossroads"},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1130}, names={"Melor Sends Word"}, text="Melor Stonehoof, Hunter Rise (the south mesa)", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=61.5, y=80.9},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1131}, names={"Steelsnap"}, text="Steelsnap is a hyena in the far west of Thousand Needles", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=61.5, y=80.9},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={5062}, names={"Sacred Fire"}, text="Magatha Grimtotem, Elder Rise (the east mesa). Do not take Arikara (elite)", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=69.8, y=30.9},
  {t="G", seg=10, text="Take the path north out of the city", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=51.1, y=31.8},
  {t="G", seg=10, text="Follow it to the new plateau north of Thunder Bluff, then head west to the camp on Skywatcher Plateau", zone="Mulgore", map=1412, x=40.0, y=17.2},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={96260}, names={"Stronger than Steel"}, text="Yorn Grimtotem", zone="Mulgore", map=1412, x=32.4, y=20.0},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={96241}, names={"Talkin' bout Toxins, Mon"}, text="Mazu'kon, beside Yorn. He gives you a Toxin Extractor", zone="Mulgore", map=1412, x=32.5, y=20.6},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={96259}, names={"Defending the Dead"}, text="Muln Earthfury, in the same camp. If someone in the camp offers nothing, skip that quest", zone="Mulgore", map=1412, x=33.5, y=22.5},
  {t="N", seg=10, arg="Optional: this camp takes cloth donations (60 Wool Cloth or 60 Silk Cloth; Oura Stormspinner, 34.2,22.4) for a little extra XP. Skip it if you have no spare cloth"},
  {t="C", seg=10, q={96259,96241,96260}, names={"Defending the Dead","Talkin' bout Toxins, Mon","Stronger than Steel"}, text="Gloomrise burial ground, north of the camp: kill Hatchlings and Soldiers, use the Toxin Extractor on Gnawed Corpses, and loot Crystalline Silk from Spinners. Leave Broodmother Valraxx (elite, north end) alone. Fight next to Healing Stream Totem; drop Poison Cleansing Totem if the bites poison you", zone="Mulgore", map=1412, x=33.4, y=10.0},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={96260}, names={"Stronger than Steel"}, text="Yorn Grimtotem", zone="Mulgore", map=1412, x=32.5, y=20.1},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={96241}, names={"Talkin' bout Toxins, Mon"}, text="Mazu'kon. Skip his Drowned City idol quest (level 40)", zone="Mulgore", map=1412, x=32.5, y=20.6},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={96259}, names={"Defending the Dead"}, text="Muln Earthfury. If anyone offers The Broodmother (elite), skip it", zone="Mulgore", map=1412, x=33.5, y=22.5},
  {t="FLY", seg=10, arg="Freewind Post", text="Walk back into Thunder Bluff to Tal, the wind rider master on the central mesa"},
  {t="S", seg=10, arg="Freewind Post", text="Innkeeper Abeqwa. Your hearth stays here for the rest of this segment"},
  {t="C", seg=10, q={1131}, names={"Steelsnap"}, text="Steelsnap (level 30) roams the north-west end of the canyon (17.8,19.8). Ghost Wolf west along the road toward Whitereach Post, then north. Pull him away from other hyenas; if one joins, drop Stoneclaw Totem and Earth Shock Steelsnap first", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=17.8, y=19.8},
  {t="H", seg=10, arg="Freewind Post", text="Saves the long run back east. If the hearthstone is still on cooldown, Ghost Wolf back along the road"},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1104}, names={"Salt Flat Venom"}, text="From Freewind Post follow the canyon road east and down onto the Shimmering Flats to the Mirage Raceway. Fizzle Brassbolts (gnome side)", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1105}, names={"Hardened Shells"}, text="Wizzle Brassbolts, next to Fizzle", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1110}, names={"Rocket Car Parts"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={5762}, names={"Hemet Nesingwary"}, text="Kravel's crate for Hemet Nesingwary in Stranglethorn; keep it until you get there", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1176}, names={"Load Lightening"}, text="Pozzik (goblin side)", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1175}, names={"A Bump in the Road"}, text="Trackmaster Zherin, east end of the goblin camp", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=81.6, y=78.0},
  {t="C", seg=10, q={1104,1105,1175}, obj={0,0,1}, names={"Salt Flat Venom","Hardened Shells","A Bump in the Road"}, text="North half of the flats first: Scorpid Reavers (31-32) for venom, Sparkleshell Tortoises (30-31) for shells, and Saltstone Basilisks (30-31). Leave the look-alike Sparkleshell Snappers (34-35) alone: they drop shells too but are five levels higher, and most roam the east edge, so take your tortoises on the west side. Also kill Crystalhides (32-33) and Salt Flats Scavengers (bones) and loot every Rocket Car Rubble pile you pass. Basilisks often come in pairs: Stoneclaw Totem holds one, Earthbind Totem stops runners, Healing Wave between pulls", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=76.0, y=60.0},
  {t="C", seg=10, q={1110,1176,1175}, names={"Rocket Car Parts","Load Lightening","A Bump in the Road"}, text="Then the south half, around and below the race track: Saltstone Gazers (34-35, the hardest: pull them one at a time from the edges), the rest of the Crystalhides, Salt Flats Vultures for the remaining bones and the rest of the rubble. Avoid Vile Sting, a rare elite scorpid", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.0, y=83.0},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1104}, names={"Salt Flat Venom"}, text="Fizzle Brassbolts. Leave his letter for Martek (Badlands) for a later visit", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1105}, names={"Hardened Shells"}, text="Wizzle Brassbolts. Skip his next quest, Encrusted Tail Fins (elite)", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1110}, names={"Rocket Car Parts"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1176}, names={"Load Lightening"}, text="Pozzik", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1178}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Pozzik: a message for Gazlowe in Ratchet", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1175}, names={"A Bump in the Road"}, text="Trackmaster Zherin", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=81.6, y=78.0},
  {t="L", seg=10, lvl=30, text="Only if you are not 30 yet (the step ticks by itself otherwise): Kravel's next quest, Call of Air and Astral Recall all need level 30. Go back to the west side of the north half and kill Saltstone Basilisks and Sparkleshell Tortoises (30-31) and Scorpid Reavers (31-32). Skip the Scorpid Terrors and Snappers (33-35) around the race track. Then come back to Kravel", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=74.0, y=60.0},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1111}, names={"Wharfmaster Dizzywig"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard: his parts order for Ratchet", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="G", seg=10, text="Leave the flats south along the race track into Tanaris; Gadgetzan's flight master is on the north side of town", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=25.4},
  {t="F", seg=10, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Bulkrek Ragefist"},
  {t="FLY", seg=10, arg="Thunder Bluff"},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=10, text="Shaman trainers in the Pools of Vision under Spirit Rise, beside Apothecary Zamah: learn your level 30 spells, including Astral Recall (a second hearthstone to your bind point, 15 min cooldown), Windfury Weapon and Reincarnation. The new air totems only work once you have the Air Totem", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=22.8, y=21.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1532}, names={"Call of Air"}, text="Xanis Flameweaver, beside the shaman trainers", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=25.2, y=20.5},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1131}, names={"Steelsnap"}, text="Melor Stonehoof, Hunter Rise. Skip his next quest, Frostmaw: this route does not go after it", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=61.5, y=80.9},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1102}, names={"A Vengeful Fate"}, text="Auld Stonespire. Razorflank's Heart drops from Charlga Razorflank, the last boss. Needs level 29.", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=36.0, y=59.9, dg=8},
  {t="N", seg=10, arg="Optional dungeon: Razorfen Kraul, levels 29-38", text="The entrance is in the far south-west of the Barrens, south of Camp Taurajo, where the road turns towards the Great Lift. Inside: Willix the Importer, near the end, gives an escort quest that also ends with him. Quests you picked up for it: Blueleaf Tubers, A Vengeful Fate, Going, Going, Guano!.", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=42.9, y=90.2, dg=8, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1102}, names={"A Vengeful Fate"}, zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=36.0, y=59.9, dg=8},
  {t="N", seg=10, arg="Cast Astral Recall (back to Freewind Post)", text="Or fly to Freewind Post from Tal"},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1532}, names={"Call of Air"}, text="Prate Cloudseer sits in a small hut on the mesa north-east of Freewind Post, just south of Dorn Plainstalker (the Test of Faith planks): take the same way up you used for Dorn. You get the Air Totem, so your air totems now work", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=53.5, y=42.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=10, arg="Ratchet", text="From Nyse at Freewind Post"},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1178}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Gazlowe, in the middle of Ratchet", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.7, y=36.2},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1180}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Gazlowe: keep it for Booty Bay", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.7, y=36.2},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1111}, names={"Wharfmaster Dizzywig"}, text="Wharfmaster Dizzywig, on the dock", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=63.4, y=38.5},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1221}, names={"Blueleaf Tubers"}, zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.4, y=37.6, dg=8},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1112}, names={"Parts for Kravel"}, text="Keep Kravel's parts; you take them back to the Shimmering Flats in a later segment", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=63.4, y=38.5},
  {t="N", seg=10, arg="Take the boat from the Ratchet dock to Booty Bay. Keep 515 for Tarren Mill; your hearth stays at Freewind Post"},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={1180}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Wharfmaster Lozgil, on the dock where the boat from Ratchet lands", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.4, y=73.6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={1181}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Wharfmaster Lozgil", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.3, y=73.6},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={1181}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Baron Revilgaz, top floor of the inn building", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=76.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={1182}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Keep it; the blueprints are for a later Stranglethorn visit", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=76.9},
  {t="F", seg=11, arg="Booty Bay", text="Gringer, the wind rider master by the inn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.1},
  {t="S", seg=11, arg="Booty Bay", text="Innkeeper Skindle. Your hearthstone still points at Freewind Post, which is no use on this continent; you hearth back here at the end of the jungle loop"},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={201}, names={"Investigate the Camp"}, text="Krazek, in the inn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={605}, names={"Singing Blue Shards"}, text="Crank Fizzlebub, in the inn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.1, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={189}, names={"Bloodscalp Ears"}, text="Kebok, in the inn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={575}, names={"Supply and Demand"}, text="Drizzlik, in the shop next to the inn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.3, y=77.6},
  {t="F", seg=11, arg="Grom'gol", text="Leave Booty Bay by the tunnel and follow the main road north in Ghost Wolf (about 5 minutes) to Grom'gol Base Camp. Do not leave the road: the jungle beside it is level 37-44 (gorillas near Booty Bay, then stealthed Shadowmaw Panthers, Jungle Stalkers and Cold Eye Basilisks), and Tethis, an elite raptor (43), prowls beside the road just north of the arena (28-32,43-45). Thysta, the wind rider master, is in the camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.5, y=29.4},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={581}, names={"Hunt for Yenniku"}, text="Nimboya", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.7},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={596}, names={"Bloody Bone Necklaces"}, text="Kin'weelay", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.3, y=27.7},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Take any new quest a Grom'gol NPC offers that is not red; the logger records it", text="Forever adds a few undocumented Stranglethorn quests. Commander Aggro'gosh and Far Seer Mok'thardin only have quests from level 33: leave them"},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={201}, names={"Investigate the Camp"}, text="Keep following the road north to Nesingwary's camp (35.7,10.9); arriving there completes it", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.6, y=11.0},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={5762}, names={"Hemet Nesingwary"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={583}, names={"Welcome to the Jungle"}, text="Barnil Stonepot", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.5},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={583}, names={"Welcome to the Jungle"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={185}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, text="Ajeck Rouack", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.6, y=10.6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={190}, names={"Panther Mastery"}, text="Sir S. J. Erlgadin", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.5, y=10.6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={194}, names={"Raptor Mastery"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={185,190,575}, names={"Tiger Mastery","Panther Mastery","Supply and Demand"}, text="Young tigers around and west of the camp, young panthers to the east, River Crocolisks along the river beside the camp. Cats often come in pairs: drop a Stoneclaw Totem to hold the second one, or Frost Shock it while you finish the first. The few Stone Maw Basilisks (31-32) just north of the camp (31-37,2-8) drop Singing Crystal Shards for Crank's quest: kill them while you are here", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.3, y=12.5},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={185}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, text="Ajeck Rouack", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.6, y=10.6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={186}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.6, y=10.6},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={190}, names={"Panther Mastery"}, text="Sir S. J. Erlgadin", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.5, y=10.6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={191}, names={"Panther Mastery"}, zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.5, y=10.6},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={186,191}, names={"Tiger Mastery","Panther Mastery"}, text="Panthers roam the hills west of the camp (28-31,9-17), with only 7 Stranglethorn Tigers among them. If the tigers run out before you have 10, wait for respawns while you kill panthers, or finish them east of the camp (43-48,11-18): stay in the middle there, between the Kurzen camp to the north and the Venture Co. camp to the south", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=29.5, y=12.5},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={194,605}, names={"Raptor Mastery","Singing Blue Shards"}, text="Stranglethorn Raptors (33-34) and Crystal Spine Basilisks (34-35) share the open ground further west (24-27,15-18); the basilisks drop the rest of the Singing Crystal Shards. At about 30 they are 3-5 levels above you: pull one at a time from the edge with Stoneclaw Totem down, and rest to full after each fight. Raptors run in pairs too: Earthbind Totem slows the second, Healing Wave between pulls", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=25.5, y=16.5},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Optional new quests at the Ruins of Zul'Kunda (24,10), just north of the raptors: zeppelin crash debris and a caged goblin, Zimmix Sputterspark, start NEW level 35 quests that end in Booty Bay. Take them only if the 34-37 trolls there are manageable; the logger records them", text="Every Bloodscalp there also drops the ears, tusks and necklaces you need next"},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={186}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, text="Back east to Ajeck Rouack at Nesingwary's camp. Do not take the next tier yet; you get it on the next Stranglethorn visit", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.6, y=10.6},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={191}, names={"Panther Mastery"}, text="Sir S. J. Erlgadin. Leave the next tier for the next Stranglethorn visit", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.5, y=10.6},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={194}, names={"Raptor Mastery"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary. Leave the next tier for the next Stranglethorn visit", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={581,596,189}, names={"Hunt for Yenniku","Bloody Bone Necklaces","Bloodscalp Ears"}, text="Head back south toward Grom'gol through the Bloodscalp camps: first 31-34,12-17 just south-west of the hunters' camp, then 29-31,17-21. Any Bloodscalp can drop ears, tusks and necklaces. Kill the axe throwers first and Earth Shock the shamans' heals and bolts", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=33.5, y=15.5},
  {t="L", seg=11, lvl=31, text="Drizzlik's next quest in Booty Bay needs 31. If you are short, keep killing Bloodscalps at these camps (33-34) before going on to Grom'gol", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=29.8, y=19.5},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={581}, names={"Hunt for Yenniku"}, text="Nimboya, Grom'gol", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.7},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={582}, names={"Headhunting"}, text="Keep it for your next Stranglethorn visit", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.7},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={596}, names={"Bloody Bone Necklaces"}, text="Kin'weelay", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.3, y=27.7},
  {t="H", seg=11, arg="Booty Bay", text="Hearthstone, or cast Astral Recall. If both are on cooldown, fly from Grom'gol"},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={201}, names={"Investigate the Camp"}, text="Krazek", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={605}, names={"Singing Blue Shards"}, text="Crank Fizzlebub", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.1, y=77.2},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={2842}, names={"Chief Engineer Scooty"}, zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.6, y=77.5, dg=9, req=2842},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={2843}, names={"Gnomer-gooooone!"}, text="Scooty gives you the Goblin Transponder: it lets you use the teleporter pad next to him.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.6, y=77.5, dg=9, req=2842},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={2843}, names={"Gnomer-gooooone!"}, zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.6, y=77.5, dg=9, req=2843},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={189}, names={"Bloodscalp Ears"}, text="Kebok.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={213}, names={"Hostile Takeover"}, text="Kebok: Hostile Takeover (needs level 31). Do not go now: the Venture Co. geologists are 34-36 and the route is at their camp at level 39 (segment 15). Not offered? Press Skip: the later steps for it then pass by themselves", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={575}, names={"Supply and Demand"}, text="Drizzlik", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.3, y=77.6},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={577}, names={"Some Assembly Required"}, text="Keep it; Snapjaw Crocolisks are 35-36, so it waits for a later visit", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.3, y=77.6},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Optional dungeon: Gnomeregan, levels 29-38", text="For the Horde the way in is the teleporter pad next to Scooty in Booty Bay (you need his Goblin Transponder). It drops you inside Gnomeregan, close to the dungeon portal. Inside: Kernobee gives an escort quest, A Fine Mess, that ends at Scooty. Quests you picked up for it: Rig Wars.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.6, y=77.5, dg=9, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={2904}, names={"A Fine Mess"}, text="A Fine Mess, if you escorted Kernobee.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.6, y=77.5, dg=9},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Hand in any Zul'Kunda NEW quests you took (the goblin escort ends at Wharfmaster Lozgil on the dock)"},
  {t="FLY", seg=11, arg="Grom'gol", text="Gringer, Booty Bay"},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Take the zeppelin to the Undercity from the tower at Grom'gol's west edge", text="Nez'raz on the platform runs the Undercity zeppelin; the other one goes to Orgrimmar. It lands at the tower outside the Undercity in Tirisfal: walk into the city and down the elevator"},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={1164}, names={"To Steal From Thieves"}, text="Genavie Callow, beside the bat handler near the west elevator. The Dabyrie heads come from Arathi; you hand them in at the start of the next segment", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=63.8, y=49.5},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={96988}, names={"Source of Power"}, text="Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium. 6 Cracked Sentry Cores from the Fragmented Sentries; a run has only 12 to 15 of them and cores are not shared.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=46.6, y=74.4, dg=7},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={1109}, names={"Going, Going, Guano!"}, zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.8, y=69.3, dg=8},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Elixir of Agony (515) needs a troll's blood potion. If it is not in your bags yet, buy the one your quest log names at the Undercity Auction House now", text="Forever's page lists a Lesser Troll's Blood Elixir, the old text a Strong Troll's Blood Potion. If none is for sale, skip the two Hillsbrad coast steps and abandon 515"},
  {t="FLY", seg=11, arg="Tarren Mill", text="Bat handler Michael Garrett, next to Genavie Callow"},
  {t="S", seg=11, arg="Tarren Mill", text="Bind at the Tarren Mill inn (Innkeeper Shay). You hearth back here after the coast run"},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={556}, names={"Stone Tokens"}, text="Keeper Bel'varil", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.5, y=20.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={544}, names={"Prison Break In"}, text="Magus Wordeen Voidglare", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.6, y=20.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={93680}, names={"Key to the City"}, text="Magus Wordeen Voidglare (new in Forever). Ignore his later Blood in the Streets: it leads into the City of Dalaran instance", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.6, y=20.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={552}, names={"Helcular's Revenge"}, text="Novice Thaivand", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.9, y=19.7},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={533}, names={"Infiltration"}, text="Krusk. Leave his Regthar Deathgate for your last visit here; Tallow's Hammer May Fall also waits until you are back from the coast", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.2, y=20.7},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={533}, names={"Infiltration"}, text="The Syndicate camp just north of Tarren Mill. Kill Syndicate Footpads and Thieves until a Syndicate Missive drops. Skip Henchman Valik: his quest needs Southshore Stout from the Alliance town. If a Singed Note drops, keep it: it starts Strahnbrad Mystery at the end of this segment", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=58.3, y=68.0},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={552}, names={"Helcular's Revenge"}, text="Head south-west to the yeti cave in the hills west of Tarren Mill. Kill Cave and Ferocious Yetis until Helcular's Rod drops", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=44.5, y=30.0, path={{46.3,31.6}}, cave=true},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={544,556,93680}, names={"Prison Break In","Stone Tokens","Key to the City"}, text="Go west to the Lordamere Internment Camp, south of the Dalaran dome. Kill Ricter, Alina, Dermot and Kegan Darkmar for the four Bloodstone pieces; every Dalaran mob here drops Worn Stone Tokens. Search the camp for the Grimy Key (new quest, no map data yet). Most of them are casters: Earth Shock their spells and drop a Stoneclaw Totem when two pull together", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=19.5, y=84.5},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={533}, names={"Infiltration"}, text="Krusk. He offers Gol'dir (503) next: leave it until you come back from Arathi", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.2, y=20.7},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={544}, names={"Prison Break In"}, text="Magus Wordeen Voidglare", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.6, y=20.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={545}, names={"Dalaran Patrols"}, text="Magus Wordeen Voidglare", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.6, y=20.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={93680}, names={"Key to the City"}, text="Magus Wordeen Voidglare. No key yet? Leave this step for now: search the Lordamere camp again when you kill the Dalaran Summoners just north of it on the next loop, and hand the key in with Dalaran Patrols after you hearth back", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.6, y=20.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={556}, names={"Stone Tokens"}, text="Keeper Bel'varil", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.5, y=20.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={557}, names={"Bracers of Binding"}, text="Keeper Bel'varil", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.5, y=20.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={552}, names={"Helcular's Revenge"}, text="Novice Thaivand", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.9, y=19.7},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={553}, names={"Helcular's Revenge"}, text="Novice Thaivand", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.9, y=19.7},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={553,553}, obj={1,2}, names={"Helcular's Revenge","Helcular's Revenge"}, text="Back in the same yeti cave: with the rod in your bags, click the Flame of Azel and the Flame of Veraz deeper inside", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=44.0, y=27.4, path={{46.3,31.6}}, cave=true},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={553}, obj={3}, names={"Helcular's Revenge"}, text="Go north to the yeti cave in Alterac and click the Flame of Uzel. Giant Yetis (33-34) guard it: pull them one at a time. Do not wander north of the cave: the ruins just above it (35-41,49-60) are full of elite Crushridge Warmongers and Enforcers (38-40)", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=37.5, y=66.2},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={557,545}, obj={0,2}, names={"Bracers of Binding","Dalaran Patrols"}, text="Head due west from the cave to the edge of the Dalaran crater, staying south of that ogre camp: kill Elemental Slaves for Bracers of Earth Binding and the Dalaran Patrols count", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=21.0, y=58.5},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={545}, obj={1}, names={"Dalaran Patrols"}, text="Kill 6 Dalaran Summoners south of the dome. Earth Shock interrupts them; when a summoner and its elemental come together, Stoneclaw Totem holds the elemental. Still no Grimy Key (93680)? Search the Lordamere camp just south of them (17-22,82-88) again", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=16.0, y=76.0},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={515}, obj={3}, names={"Elixir of Agony"}, text="Head south-east across Hillsbrad to the coast. Torn Fin Oracles and Tidehunters drop Torn Fin Eyes; Earth Shock the Oracles' heals", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=41.2, y=69.0},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={553}, names={"Helcular's Revenge"}, text="Helcular's Grave is in the Southshore graveyard on the north-east side of town. Alliance guards patrol: come in from the hills, click the grave, leave in Ghost Wolf", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=52.8, y=53.4},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={515}, obj={2}, names={"Elixir of Agony"}, text="Daggerspine Shorehunters and Sirens along the Eastern Strand drop Daggerspine Scales", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=57.4, y=69.5},
  {t="H", seg=11, arg="Tarren Mill", text="Hearthstone, or cast Astral Recall"},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={545}, names={"Dalaran Patrols"}, text="Magus Wordeen Voidglare. Hand in Key to the City (93680) too if you found the key on this loop", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.6, y=20.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={557}, names={"Bracers of Binding"}, text="Keeper Bel'varil", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.5, y=20.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={515}, names={"Elixir of Agony"}, text="Apothecary Lydon. Do not take 517 (elite)", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.4, y=19.1},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={676}, names={"The Hammer May Fall"}, text="Tallow, standing next to Lydon", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.9, y=19.6},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={676}, names={"The Hammer May Fall"}, text="Take the road east out of Tarren Mill into Arathi Highlands. Kill Boulderfist Ogres and Enforcers at Boulder'gor, south of the road on the west side of Arathi. They hit hard: pull one at a time, Stoneclaw Totem if a second wanders in, Healing Wave between fights", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.6, y=44.9},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={1164}, names={"To Steal From Thieves"}, text="Follow the road east to Dabyrie's Farmstead, staying clear of Refuge Pointe (Alliance) in the middle of the zone. Kill Fardel, Marcel and Kenata Dabyrie for their heads. Pull the farm guards one at a time", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=55.7, y=37.6},
  {t="F", seg=11, arg="Hammerfall", text="Urda, the wind rider master in Hammerfall", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=73.0, y=32.6},
  {t="S", seg=11, arg="Hammerfall", text="Bind at the Hammerfall inn"},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={676}, names={"The Hammer May Fall"}, text="Drum Fel", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.2, y=33.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={677}, names={"Call to Arms"}, text="Drum Fel", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.2, y=33.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={655}, names={"Hammerfall"}, text="Gor'mul", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=72.6, y=33.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={655}, names={"Hammerfall"}, text="Tor'gan", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={672,671}, names={"Raising Spirits","Foul Magics"}, text="Tor'gan", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={97539}, names={"Silky Sutures"}, text="Doctor Gregory Victor (new in Forever), at the infirmary", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=73.4, y=36.8},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={672}, names={"Raising Spirits"}, text="Highland Striders roam the hills all around Hammerfall; they drop Highland Raptor Eyes", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=64.3, y=41.4},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={97539}, names={"Silky Sutures"}, text="Plains Creepers (spiders, 32-33) drop Surgical Spidersilk. Try the ones south of Hammerfall first, but Forever's quest page has only recorded drops in west and central Arathi (16-42,26-76). If 6-8 kills here give no silk, stop: collect it on the run west instead (around 38-42,43-61, Northfold Manor and Boulder'gor)", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=66.0, y=50.0},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={677}, names={"Call to Arms"}, text="Witherbark Village in the south-east: Axe Throwers, Witch Doctors and Headhunters. Earth Shock the Witch Doctors' casts and fight at the edge of the village so you only pull one at a time", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=65.4, y=70.2, path={{66.4,60.6},{61.8,67.2},{61.8,69.3},{63.8,72.3},{65.0,72.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={92707}, names={"The Giant in the Den"}, text="New in Forever. Kill the goliath in its den south of Witherbark Village; its Goliath's Wristguards start the quest. Witherbark Shadow Hunters (35-36) and Headhunters stand around the den, and Zalas Witherbark (a level 40 rare) can walk through: pull them one at a time from the edge, and skip the goliath if its level shows a skull or it is elite", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=69.0, y=81.0},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={672}, names={"Raising Spirits"}, text="Tor'gan", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={674}, names={"Raising Spirits"}, text="Tor'gan", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={674}, names={"Raising Spirits"}, text="Gor'mul", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=72.6, y=33.9},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={675}, names={"Raising Spirits"}, text="Gor'mul", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=72.6, y=33.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={675}, names={"Raising Spirits"}, text="Tor'gan. He now offers Guile of the Raptor (701): leave it. Highland Fleshstalkers are level 36-37, and you come back to Hammerfall at 37", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={95663}, names={"Dragonmaw Rumors"}, text="Zaruk in Hammerfall. It sends you to the Deathstalker Agent in the Wetlands.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.5, y=35.6, dg=6},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={677}, names={"Call to Arms"}, text="Drum Fel. Leave the second Call to Arms (678) for your next Hammerfall visit too: its Brutes and Magi are level 35-37", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.2, y=33.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={92707}, names={"The Giant in the Den"}, text="Drum Fel", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.2, y=33.9},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={97539}, names={"Silky Sutures"}, text="Doctor Gregory Victor. Silk not done yet? Skip this step and Ward Restocking (92519); you hand the silk in when you hearth back here at the end", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=73.4, y=36.8},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={92519}, names={"Ward Restocking"}, text="Doctor Gregory Victor should offer Ward Restocking now (new in Forever). Skip the Go'shek step if he does not", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=73.4, y=36.8},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Optional dungeon: Excavation Site: Wetlands, levels 26-31", text="It is in the Wetlands, in the hills above Whelgar's Excavation. From Hammerfall ride west across Arathi and south over the Thandol Span. Before going in, hand Dragonmaw Rumors in to the Deathstalker Agent near the entrance (Wetlands 51.4, 59.2) and take Open the Maw from her; hand it back to her after the run. Inside: the last boss, the Relic Guardian, drops a Titan Relic that starts Elder Knowledge. Quests you picked up for it: Changing Tastes, Dragonmaw Rumors.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=47.8, y=56.2, dg=6, run=true},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={92519}, names={"Ward Restocking"}, text="Go'shek Farm, south-west of Hammerfall. Pick up the case of Packaged Tonics in Apothecary Jorell's shack", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=60.1, y=59.3, path={{73.0,38.5},{70.6,38.5},{68.8,41.2},{68.8,45.4},{66.0,51.0},{60.0,51.0},{58.0,53.1},{58.0,59.1},{58.8,60.3}}},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={671}, names={"Foul Magics"}, text="Go north-west to Northfold Manor. The Syndicate Highwaymen, Mercenaries and Pathstalkers drop Bloodstone Amulets. You hand them in when you hearth back to Hammerfall at the end. Still short of Surgical Spidersilk? Kill the Plains Creepers you pass on the way", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.0, y=28.5},
  {t="L", seg=11, lvl=33, text="Quest XP runs short here, and Strahnbrad (next) is level 34-37. Grind the Boulderfist Ogres and Enforcers (32-34) at Boulder'gor, just south of Northfold Manor, until you are 33. The Syndicate at Northfold Manor (30-33) are an easier but slower fallback", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.5, y=46.5},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={1361,503}, names={"Regthar Deathgate","Gol'dir"}, text="Run west in Ghost Wolf along the road through Thoradin's Wall into Hillsbrad to Tarren Mill (closer than going back to Hammerfall to fly). Krusk: keep Regthar Deathgate for the Barrens (next segment); Gol'dir is done in Strahnbrad now", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.2, y=20.7},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={503}, names={"Gol'dir"}, text="Take the road north out of Tarren Mill to Strahnbrad. Kill Jailor Borhuin (level 37) for the Rusted Iron Key. Syndicate Spies, Wizards and Argus Shadow Mages (34-36) fill the town: clear his surroundings first, Earth Shock the casters, then pull him alone at full mana with Stoneclaw Totem down and Healing Wave when he gets you low. If he is still too strong, abandon 503 and skip ahead to the hearth step (Perenolde, 507, then drops out later too)", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=63.1, y=43.4},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={503}, names={"Gol'dir"}, text="Free Gol'dir from his cell", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=60.0, y=43.7},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={506}, names={"Blackmoore's Legacy"}, text="Gol'dir", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=60.0, y=43.7},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={95534}, names={"Strahnbrad Mystery"}, text="New in Forever. A Singed Note drops from the Syndicate in and around Strahnbrad (also at the camp north of Tarren Mill). Right-click it to start the quest. No note by the time the town is cleared? Skip the 95534 steps", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=61.0, y=44.5},
  {t="C", seg=11, q={95534}, names={"Strahnbrad Mystery"}, text="Go to the old bellows by the smithy (about 61.3,44.4) and clear the Syndicate around them. Stand next to them out of combat and click them; something fiery may come to life, so kill it. If nothing happens within 2-3 minutes, abandon 95534 and skip its steps. The logger records what you saw", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=61.3, y=44.4},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={506}, names={"Blackmoore's Legacy"}, text="Krusk in Tarren Mill. He then offers Lord Aliden Perenolde (507): leave it. Perenolde is level 41; take it from Krusk when you come back for him at 39-40", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.2, y=20.7},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={95534}, names={"Strahnbrad Mystery"}, text="Report your findings in Tarren Mill. The turn-in NPC is not known yet; try High Executor Darthalia first, then the other quest givers", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.3, y=20.4},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={96986}, names={"The Grave Knight"}, text="Melisara in Tarren Mill. Kill Atrexis the Grave Knight.", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.5, y=20.6, dg=7},
  {t="A", seg=11, q={92434}, names={"Blood in the Streets"}, text="Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill, after Dalaran Patrols and Key to the City. It leads you through the sewers on the north side of Dalaran to the Image of Archmage Modera.", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.6, y=20.8, dg=7},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Optional dungeon: City of Dalaran, levels 28-33", text="You get in through Dalaran's sewers, on the north side of the city by Lordamere Lake, then a portal at the end of a long pipe. The Image of Archmage Modera there ends Blood in the Streets, gives Heart of Disruption and turns your Grimy Key into the Dalaran Sewer Key. One player with the key lets the whole group in. Rexxie Copperclutch at the sewer entrance gives Opportunistic Education (a book on the back wall past the portal room). Many enemies here are immune to Arcane damage. Quests you picked up for it: Source of Power, The Grave Knight, Blood in the Streets.", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=8.5, y=59.2, dg=7, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={96986}, names={"The Grave Knight"}, zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.5, y=20.6, dg=7},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={96984}, names={"Heart of Disruption"}, text="Heart of Disruption: bring the Arcane Mote to Magus Wordeen Voidglare.", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=61.6, y=20.8, dg=7},
  {t="H", seg=11, arg="Hammerfall", text="Hearthstone or Astral Recall. Or fly from Tarren Mill if both are on cooldown"},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={671}, names={"Foul Magics"}, text="Tor'gan. If you finished Silky Sutures (97539) only on the run west, hand it in to Doctor Gregory Victor now and do not take Ward Restocking", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3},
  {t="T", seg=11, q={92519}, names={"Ward Restocking"}, text="Doctor Gregory Victor", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=73.4, y=36.8},
  {t="N", seg=11, arg="Segment done. Keep Regthar Deathgate (1361) and To Steal From Thieves (1164) in the log. Next: fly from Hammerfall to the Undercity for Genavie Callow, then the zeppelin to Orgrimmar, where you train 32", text="Your hearthstone stays at Hammerfall. There is no shaman trainer on this trip; your next one is in Orgrimmar"},
  {t="FLY", seg=12, arg="Undercity", text="Urda, the wind rider master in Hammerfall. Your hearthstone stays at Hammerfall until Shadowprey Village."},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1164}, names={"To Steal From Thieves"}, text="Genavie Callow, right next to the bat handler by the west elevator", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=63.8, y=49.5},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={96988}, names={"Source of Power"}, zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=46.6, y=74.4, dg=7},
  {t="G", seg=12, text="Ride the elevator up, leave the ruins and climb the zeppelin tower just outside. Take the zeppelin to Orgrimmar (Zapetta), not the Grom'gol one.", zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=60.7, y=58.8},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={92422}, names={"The Wrath of Rath'mael"}, zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=65.2, y=60.2, dg=2},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Ride the zeppelin to Durotar, then run into Orgrimmar through the front gate", text="This is the trip back to Kalimdor. The rest of the Eastern Kingdoms work waits for segment 14."},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1145}, names={"The Swarm Grows"}, text="Belgrom Rockmaul in the Valley of Honor", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=75.2, y=34.2},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={2841}, names={"Rig Wars"}, zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=76.0, y=25.4, dg=9},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1146}, names={"The Swarm Grows"}, text="Belgrom Rockmaul. Keep it: Moktar Krin in Thousand Needles takes it in the next segment.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=75.2, y=34.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1431}, names={"Alliance Relations"}, text="Craven Drok in the Cleft of Shadow", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=45.7, y=49.9},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={95697}, names={"Changing Tastes"}, zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=57.4, y=53.4, dg=6},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1431}, names={"Alliance Relations"}, text="Keldran, on the west side of the city", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=22.6, y=52.6},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1432}, names={"Alliance Relations"}, text="Keldran. You hand it in at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=22.6, y=52.6},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=12, text="Valley of Wisdom: learn your level 32 spells (Chain Lightning and Windfury Totem among them). Your level 34 ranks come from the Thunder Bluff trainers at the start of the next segment.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=38.8, y=36.4},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Ask Searn Firewarder and the shaman trainers here for any new shaman quest and take it", text="Forever lists a new Call of Air (96136) with no known giver; it is written for Zephras Isle shaman, so you will most likely get nothing. You already have your Air Totem. If a quest is offered, take it so the logger records it."},
  {t="FLY", seg=12, arg="Crossroads", text="Doras, on top of the tower in the Valley of Strength"},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1361}, names={"Regthar Deathgate"}, text="Regthar Deathgate, a short run west of the Crossroads", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=45.3, y=28.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1362}, names={"The Kolkar of Desolace"}, text="Regthar Deathgate", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=45.3, y=28.4},
  {t="FLY", seg=12, arg="Thunder Bluff", text="Run back to the Crossroads flight master"},
  {t="G", seg=12, text="Take the path north out of the city, the same way you went to the Gloomrise camp at 30. Use Ghost Wolf.", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=51.1, y=31.8},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={95664}, names={"Elder Knowledge"}, text="Elder Knowledge: Bashana Runetotem on Elder Rise.", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=70.9, y=33.8, dg=6},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={98823}, names={"Earthen Echo"}, text="Earthen Echo: take the relic to Muln Earthfury at the Skywatcher Plateau in north-west Mulgore.", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=70.9, y=33.8, dg=6, req=95664},
  {t="G", seg=12, text="Keep going to the new plateau north of Thunder Bluff, then follow the new path west into Desolace and on to Kormek's Hut. If there is no path into Desolace, go back to the Thunder Bluff flight master, fly to Sun Rock Retreat and take the road south into Desolace to Kormek's Hut.", zone="Mulgore", map=1412, x=40.0, y=17.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5501}, names={"Bone Collector"}, text="Bibbly F'utzbuckle at Kormek's Hut", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=62.3, y=39.0},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5821}, names={"Bodyguard for Hire"}, text="Cork Gizelton, only if the Gizelton caravan is stopped here. If it is not, skip both caravan quests (5821 and 5943). If Rigger Gizelton offers Gizelton Caravan (5943) here too, take it now.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.4, y=38.1},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={5821}, names={"Bodyguard for Hire"}, text="Walk with the caravan south past Kolkar Village and kill the centaur that attack the kodos.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=64.0, y=50.0},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5943}, names={"Gizelton Caravan"}, text="Rigger Gizelton. If he had no quest at Kormek's Hut, he offers it when the caravan stops again after the Kolkar leg, before Mannoroc Coven; take it there or skip it. Optional: demons up to level 38 attack on this leg.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.3, y=38.2},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={5943}, names={"Gizelton Caravan"}, text="Stay with the caravan through Mannoroc Coven and kill the demons that attack the kodos. Drop Stoneclaw Totem beside the kodos to pull attackers onto it, and Earth Shock the casters.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.0, y=72.0},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={5821,5943}, names={"Bodyguard for Hire","Gizelton Caravan"}, text="Smeed Scrabblescrew at Scrabblescrew's Camp", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.9, y=61.9},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5561}, names={"Kodo Roundup"}, text="Smeed Scrabblescrew", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.9, y=61.9},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={5561,5501}, names={"Kodo Roundup","Bone Collector"}, text="Kodo Graveyard: use the Kodo Kombobulator on Aged, Dying or Ancient Kodos and walk each tamed kodo back to Smeed, one at a time. The kodos on the east edge are closest to the camp. Loot Kodo Bones from the bone piles as you go.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=53.0, y=59.5},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={5561}, names={"Kodo Roundup"}, text="Smeed Scrabblescrew", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=60.9, y=61.9},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1362}, names={"The Kolkar of Desolace"}, text="Felgur Twocuts", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.2, y=59.6},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1365}, names={"Khan Dez'hepah"}, text="Felgur Twocuts", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.2, y=59.6},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1368}, names={"Gelkis Alliance"}, text="Gurda Wildmane. Gelkis and Magram reputations are exclusive. This route sides with the Gelkis: kill Magram, never Gelkis.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.3, y=59.7},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={93225}, names={"Carved Centaur Totems"}, text="Gurda Wildmane (new in Forever). The quest says any centaur can drop the 5 Carved Centaur Totems, but so far they have only been recorded from the Maraudine in the Valley of Spears. Keep any that drop from Kolkar or Magram.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.2, y=59.6},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1432}, names={"Alliance Relations"}, text="Takata Steelblade", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.6, y=54.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1433}, names={"Alliance Relations"}, text="Takata Steelblade", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.6, y=54.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1433}, names={"Alliance Relations"}, text="Maurin Bonesplitter, next to Takata", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.2, y=53.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1435}, names={"The Burning of Spirits"}, text="Maurin Bonesplitter. He gives you the Burning Gem.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.2, y=53.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1434}, names={"Befouled by Satyr"}, text="Takata Steelblade", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.6, y=54.4},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={1365}, names={"Khan Dez'hepah"}, text="Kolkar Village, northeast of Ghost Walker Post. Khan Dez'hepah stands at the north end. Kolkar come in groups: pull from the edge, drop Stoneclaw Totem when two come at once, and Earth Shock the Windchasers' casts.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=73.4, y=41.6},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={5501}, names={"Bone Collector"}, text="Bibbly F'utzbuckle at Kormek's Hut", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=62.3, y=39.0},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={1435}, names={"The Burning of Spirits"}, text="Thunder Axe Fortress, northwest of Kormek's Hut: bring each Burning Blade orc to low health, then use the Burning Gem on it to get an Infused Burning Gem. Used at high health it does nothing, so stop shocking once they are low. Get 15, and keep the Burning Gem: it goes back to Maurin with them.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=54.8, y=27.8},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1480}, names={"The Corrupter"}, text="The Flayed Demon Skin drops from Burning Blade orcs here. Right-click it to start the quest.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=54.8, y=27.8},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1365}, names={"Khan Dez'hepah"}, text="Felgur Twocuts", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.2, y=59.6},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1366}, names={"Centaur Bounty"}, text="Felgur Twocuts", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.2, y=59.6},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1435}, names={"The Burning of Spirits"}, text="Maurin Bonesplitter. Takata now offers Alliance Relations (1436). Leave it for later to save log space.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.2, y=53.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1480}, names={"The Corrupter"}, text="Maurin Bonesplitter", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.2, y=53.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1481}, names={"The Corrupter"}, text="Maurin Bonesplitter", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.2, y=53.4},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={1366,93225}, names={"Centaur Bounty","Carved Centaur Totems"}, text="Magram Village, southeast of Ghost Walker Post: kill Magram centaur for 15 Centaur Ears, and keep any totems that drop. Pull singles away from the huts; Earthbind Totem stops the ones that run, and Earth Shock interrupts Windchasers and Stormers.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=69.5, y=75.0},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={1368}, names={"Gelkis Alliance"}, text="Do not leave Magram Village until you are Friendly with the Gelkis (check the reputation tab). Every Magram kill raises it, and these are the same kills as the grind below. Do not count on Gurda's totem reward to finish it.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=69.5, y=75.0},
  {t="L", seg=12, lvl=34, text="Keep killing Magram centaur here (levels 32-36) until you reach 34. Keep Lightning Shield up and pull them one or two at a time."},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1366}, names={"Centaur Bounty"}, text="Felgur Twocuts", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.2, y=59.6, path={{66.6,70.5},{63.8,70.8},{62.4,73.8},{59.0,73.5},{56.0,66.3}}},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={93225}, names={"Carved Centaur Totems"}, text="Fewer than 5 totems? Kill Maraudine Scouts and Wranglers (36-38) on the south-east edge of the Valley of Spears, on the way from Ghost Walker Post to Gelkis Village. Pull them one at a time and keep Stoneclaw Totem ready. If they are too strong, abandon 93225 and skip its hand-in later.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.5, y=65.5},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1368}, names={"Gelkis Alliance"}, text="Uthek the Wise, at the edge of Gelkis Village in the southwest", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.2, y=79.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1370}, names={"Stealing Supplies"}, text="Uthek the Wise. Keep it: you loot the meat at Magram Village at the end of this segment.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.2, y=79.2},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Take any new quests offered here if you have log space; the logger records them", text="Forever adds several Gelkis quests at this village (crafted-item turn-ins and more). Skip Ongeku (1373): its shard is in the Swamp of Sorrows."},
  {t="F", seg=12, arg="Shadowprey Village", text="Thalon, the wind rider master in Shadowprey Village", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=21.6, y=74.0},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={6142}, names={"Clam Bait"}, text="Mai'Lahii on the docks, just north of the flight master", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=22.6, y=72.0},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={6143}, names={"Other Fish to Fry"}, text="Drulzegar Skraghook, also on the docks", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=23.3, y=72.9},
  {t="S", seg=12, arg="Shadowprey Village", text="Walk north up to the inn and make it your home (Innkeeper Sikewa)"},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5381}, names={"Hand of Iruxos"}, text="Taiga Wisemane, just east of the inn. She gives you the Demon Pick.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=25.8, y=68.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={97265}, names={"Hate the Hatefury"}, text="Aka'rai (new in Forever), just north of the inn", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=25.2, y=67.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={6161}, names={"Claim Rackmore's Treasure!"}, text="Follow the coast north to the shipwreck. Rackmore's Log lies on the beach next to it.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.1, y=30.4},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={6161}, obj={1}, names={"Claim Rackmore's Treasure!"}, text="Kill Drysnap crabs around the wreck until Rackmore's Silver Key drops. They also drop Soft-shelled Clam Meat.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=33.0, y=32.0},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5741}, names={"Sceptre of Light"}, text="Azore Aldamort, at the top of the tower at Ethel Rethor, just northeast of the wreck", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=38.9, y=27.2},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={6143,6142,6161}, obj={0,0,2}, names={"Other Fish to Fry","Clam Bait","Claim Rackmore's Treasure!"}, text="Slitherblade naga on the shore north of Ethel Rethor, from about 36,28 up to 31,15: 7 Myrmidons, 7 Naga and 5 Sorceresses. Any naga can drop Rackmore's Golden Key and clam meat. Stay on the mainland; Ranazjar Isle comes later. Save Earth Shock for the Sorceresses' casts; they hit hard.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=35.0, y=22.0},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={5741}, names={"Sceptre of Light"}, text="Burning Blade Seer at the top of the tower in Thunder Axe Fortress. He has the Sceptre of Light.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=55.2, y=30.1, path={{39.0,31.9},{45.2,31.3},{47.4,34.0},{55.0,34.0}}},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={5381}, names={"Hand of Iruxos"}, text="Use the Demon Pick on the red Hand of Iruxos Crystal inside Thunder Axe Fortress. Kill the Demon Spirit (37) that appears and loot the Demon Box.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=55.0, y=26.7},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={1434,1481,97265}, names={"Befouled by Satyr","The Corrupter","Hate the Hatefury"}, text="Sargeron, the satyr camp in the northeast: 7 each of Hatefury Rogues, Felsworn, Betrayers and Hellcallers, plus 2 each of Tricksters, Hellcallers, Shadowstalkers, Felsworn and Rogues for Aka'rai. Shadowstalkers are stealthed; one drops the Shadowstalker Scalp. Earth Shock the Hellcallers' casts.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=75.5, y=19.5},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1434}, names={"Befouled by Satyr"}, text="Takata Steelblade", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.6, y=54.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1481}, names={"The Corrupter"}, text="Maurin Bonesplitter", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.2, y=53.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1482}, names={"The Corrupter"}, text="Maurin Bonesplitter", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.2, y=53.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={93225}, names={"Carved Centaur Totems"}, text="Gurda Wildmane. If she then offers a Totem Tote quest, take Buying Friendship: Gelkis (not the Magram one) and give the tote to the Gelkis Quartermaster when you hand in Stealing Supplies in Gelkis Village at the end of this segment.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=56.2, y=59.6},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5386}, names={"Catch of the Day"}, text="Nataka Longhorn", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=55.4, y=55.8},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={5741}, names={"Sceptre of Light"}, text="Azore Aldamort", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=38.9, y=27.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={6027}, names={"Book of the Ancients"}, text="Azore Aldamort. He gives you the Gem of the Serpent.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=38.9, y=27.2},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={6161}, names={"Claim Rackmore's Treasure!"}, text="Rackmore's Chest on Ranazjar Isle: follow the naga shore north and swim across (needs both keys)", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=30.0, y=8.7},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={6027,1482}, names={"Book of the Ancients","The Corrupter"}, text="Ranazjar Isle: put the Gem of the Serpent on the Serpent Statue's hand and kill Lord Kragaru (level 38) for the book. Clear the naga near the statue first, then fight him with Stoneclaw and Searing Totem down and Healing Wave when you drop low. Slitherblade Oracles here drop the Oracle Crystal.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=30.0, y=9.5},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={6027}, names={"Book of the Ancients"}, text="Azore Aldamort", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=38.9, y=27.2},
  {t="H", seg=12, arg="Shadowprey Village", text="Or cast Astral Recall if the hearthstone is on cooldown: both take you to Shadowprey."},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={97265}, names={"Hate the Hatefury"}, text="Aka'rai, a few steps from the inn where the hearth lands you", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=25.2, y=67.2},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={5381}, names={"Hand of Iruxos"}, text="Taiga Wisemane", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=25.8, y=68.2},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5581}, names={"Portals of the Legion"}, text="Taiga Wisemane. She gives you the Hand of Iruxos.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=25.8, y=68.2},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={6142}, names={"Clam Bait"}, text="Mai'Lahii, down on the docks", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=22.6, y=72.0},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={6143}, names={"Other Fish to Fry"}, text="Drulzegar Skraghook", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=23.3, y=72.9},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5421}, names={"Fish in a Bucket"}, text="Jinar'Zillen, next to Drulzegar on the docks. This is how you get the Bloodbelly Fish for Catch of the Day.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=22.4, y=73.1},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={5421}, names={"Fish in a Bucket"}, text="Loot the Shellfish Traps on the sea floor under and around the docks. Get 10: each 5 Shellfish buy one fish.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=21.6, y=79.3},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={5421}, names={"Fish in a Bucket"}, text="Jinar'Zillen. Take the quest again and hand in the other 5 Shellfish for the second Bloodbelly Fish.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=22.4, y=73.1},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1482}, names={"The Corrupter"}, text="Maurin Bonesplitter. It is a long run east from Shadowprey: use Ghost Wolf.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.2, y=53.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1484}, names={"The Corrupter"}, text="Maurin Bonesplitter", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.2, y=53.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1484}, names={"The Corrupter"}, text="Takata Steelblade", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.6, y=54.4},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={1436}, names={"Alliance Relations"}, text="Takata Steelblade. You hand this in to Keldran in Orgrimmar in the next segment.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=52.6, y=54.4},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={5386}, names={"Catch of the Day"}, text="Nataka Longhorn", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=55.4, y=55.8},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={1370}, names={"Stealing Supplies"}, text="Magram Village: loot 6 Sacks of Meat by the huts. Kill the Magram that get in the way.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=70.2, y=77.5},
  {t="L", seg=12, lvl=35, text="Short of 35? Keep killing Magram here first: the Demon Portal Guardians in the next step are 38-39."},
  {t="C", seg=12, q={5581}, names={"Portals of the Legion"}, text="Mannoroc Coven, on the way west: use the Hand of Iruxos at a demon portal and kill the Demon Portal Guardian (38-39) that comes out. Do 6. Clear the Doomwarders around a portal first, keep Stoneclaw Totem and Healing Wave for the Guardian. Only do this if the Guardians are not red to you; otherwise abandon 5581 and skip its hand-in at Shadowprey.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=53.0, y=79.0, path={{68.4,73.2},{65.6,70.5},{63.8,70.8},{62.0,74.4},{59.4,74.4},{58.4,76.5},{54.6,76.5}}},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={1370}, names={"Stealing Supplies"}, text="Uthek the Wise, Gelkis Village. Give the Totem Tote to the Gelkis Quartermaster here if you have it.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=36.2, y=79.2},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Shen'dralas check", text="Shen'dralas is Forever's new area around the Valley of Bones (east of Gelkis Village, south of Magram Village, quests 38-43). Its Gelkis line continues after Ongeku (1373). Note any givers you see as a 37-43 filler; don't start it now."},
  {t="T", seg=12, q={5581}, names={"Portals of the Legion"}, text="Taiga Wisemane", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=25.8, y=68.2, path={{31.2,79.8},{29.8,77.7},{30.2,70.5},{28.8,68.4}}},
  {t="A", seg=12, q={5763}, names={"Hunting in Stranglethorn"}, text="Roon Wildmane. You hand it in to Hemet Nesingwary in Stranglethorn later in the route.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=25.0, y=72.3},
  {t="N", seg=12, arg="Buy 3 Soothing Spices before you leave Shadowprey", text="Lah'Mawhani (trade supplies) sells them. They are for Jarl's quest in Dustwallow Marsh in the next segment. Your hearthstone stays at Shadowprey Village.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=23.1, y=71.6},
  {t="N", seg=13, arg="Have 3 Soothing Spices in your bags before you leave", text="They are for Jarl's quest in Dustwallow, so you can hand it in on the spot. Missed them at the end of the last segment? Lah'Mawhani (trade supplies) sells them here; Wulan the cook at 26.2,69.6 does too.", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=23.1, y=71.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=13, arg="Thunder Bluff", text="Thalon, the Shadowprey wind rider master (21.6,74.1). A short stop to train on the way to Dustwallow."},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=13, text="Shaman trainers in the Pools of Vision under Spirit Rise, beside Apothecary Zamah: learn your level 34 spells. You last trained at 32, and the next trainer stop is at the end of this segment.", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=22.8, y=21.1},
  {t="FLY", seg=13, arg="Camp Taurajo", text="Tal, the wind rider master on the central mesa"},
  {t="G", seg=13, text="In Ghost Wolf, follow the road east out of Camp Taurajo into Dustwallow Marsh to the burned-out Shady Rest Inn.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=29.7, y=47.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1251}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Pull the black shield off the inn's chimney", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=29.6, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1268}, names={"Suspicious Hoofprints"}, text="Click the hoofprints in the mud beside the inn", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=29.7, y=47.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1269}, names={"Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}, text="Pick up the badge in the inn's rubble", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=29.8, y=48.2},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1177}, names={"Hungry!"}, text="Mudcrush Durtfeet, the big ogre beside the road a little south of Brackenwall Village", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.1, y=38.3},
  {t="G", seg=13, text="Brackenwall Village, north up the road", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.6, y=31.8},
  {t="F", seg=13, arg="Brackenwall Village", text="Shardi, the wind rider master"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1251,1268,1269}, names={"The Black Shield","Suspicious Hoofprints","Lieutenant Paval Reethe"}, text="Krog", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.4, y=31.9},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1321}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Krog", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.4, y=31.9},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1321}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Do'gol, next to Krog", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.5, y=30.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1322}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Do'gol. The venom sacs drop from the Darkmist spiders you kill for Jarl later, so leave this for now.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.5, y=30.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1201}, names={"Theramore Spies"}, text="Nazeer Bloodpike", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.2, y=30.7},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1273}, names={"Questioning Reethe"}, text="Ogron, south-east of the village", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=41.0, y=36.7},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1273}, names={"Questioning Reethe"}, text="Follow Ogron to Reethe's hideout. Theramore men ambush you there: drop Stoneclaw Totem to pull them off Ogron, kill them one by one and heal Ogron with Healing Wave if he gets low.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=42.6, y=38.1},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1201}, names={"Theramore Spies"}, text="The Theramore Infiltrators (35-36) are stealthed and prowl the grass east and north-east of Brackenwall. Keep Lightning Shield up so they hurt themselves when they open on you.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=40.1, y=25.1},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1201}, names={"Theramore Spies"}, zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.2, y=30.7},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1202}, names={"The Theramore Docks"}, zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.2, y=30.7},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1273}, names={"Questioning Reethe"}, text="Krog", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.4, y=31.9},
  {t="G", seg=13, text="Ghost Wolf east across the marsh to the coast north of Theramore and get into the sea here. Stay out of the long lake south-east of Brackenwall (Murk Threshers, 41-43), keep well north of Sentry Point (the tower at 60,41, guards 38) and never take the bridge into Theramore (guards 53-57). Mudrock turtles (37-38) walk this shore: slip past them.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=64.6, y=39.1},
  {t="G", seg=13, text="Swim east, well out from the shore, until you are past the north-east corner of Theramore. Do not cut across the town.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=72.0, y=45.5},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1202}, names={"The Theramore Docks"}, text="Swim south to the Captain's Footlocker on the sea floor beside the Theramore docks and loot the documents. Stay off the pier and the beach (guards 53-57). Young Murk Threshers (40-41) circle the footlocker, one almost on top of it: do not fight them at your level, wait until it swims clear and keep your distance from the others.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=71.5, y=51.2},
  {t="G", seg=13, text="Swim back north the way you came before you turn toward Jarl, so you stay clear of the town.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=72.0, y=45.5},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1218}, names={"Soothing Spices"}, text="\"Swamp Eye\" Jarl at Swamplight Manor, north-west of Theramore", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=26.3},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1218}, names={"Soothing Spices"}, text="Hand over the 3 Soothing Spices", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=26.3},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1206}, names={"Jarl Needs Eyes"}, zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=26.3},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1238}, names={"The Lost Report"}, text="The Loose Dirt mound just outside the manor", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=25.9},
  {t="G", seg=13, text="Head west past the north side of North Point Tower (46,24). About twenty Theramore Sentries (35-36) stand packed around the tower, so do not go near it.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=47.0, y=21.0},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1206,1322}, names={"Jarl Needs Eyes","The Black Shield"}, text="Darkmist Cavern, north-west of Brackenwall. Every Darkmist spider in and around the cave can drop both the eyes and the venom sacs. Most are Spiders and Recluses (35-37), but Silkspinners (38-39) are mixed in everywhere, the outer edge too: pull one at a time and use Healing Wave between pulls. Leave the Darkmist Widow (40, rare) at 31,20 alone. These spiders give more XP than the silithids where this segment's grind is, so extra kills here are never wasted.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=31.5, y=21.5},
  {t="L", seg=13, lvl=36, text="Not 36 yet? Keep killing Darkmist Spiders and Recluses (35-37) here before you leave: they give about a fifth more XP per kill than the level 32-35 silithids at the Swarm hive, where the rest of this segment's grind waits. Leave the Silkspinners (38-39) alone if they are too much for you", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=31.5, y=21.5},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1238,1202}, names={"The Lost Report","The Theramore Docks"}, text="Nazeer Bloodpike, Brackenwall", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.2, y=30.7},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1322}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Do'gol", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.5, y=30.8},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1323}, names={"The Black Shield"}, zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.5, y=30.8},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1323}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Krog", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.4, y=31.9},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1276}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Krog. Keep it for Mosarn in Thunder Bluff later in this segment.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.4, y=31.9},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1206}, names={"Jarl Needs Eyes"}, text="Back to Jarl. Skip Jarl Needs a Blade (it needs a crafted Moonsteel Broadsword).", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=26.3},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1239}, names={"The Severed Head"}, text="Dig at the Loose Dirt again", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.4, y=25.9},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1177}, names={"Hungry!"}, text="Mirefin murlocs on the north coast, north-east of Jarl, drop the heads. They run when hurt: Earthbind Totem or Frost Shock keeps them from bringing friends.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=59.5, y=11.5},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1270}, names={"Stinky's Escape"}, text="\"Stinky\" Ignatz, north-west of Swamplight Manor", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=46.9, y=17.5},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1270}, names={"Stinky's Escape"}, text="Escort Stinky on his short loop through the bog while he picks bogbean leaves; kill whatever jumps him and keep him healed.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=46.9, y=17.5},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1177}, names={"Hungry!"}, text="Mudcrush Durtfeet, on the road just south of Brackenwall", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.1, y=38.3},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1239}, names={"The Severed Head"}, text="Nazeer Bloodpike, Brackenwall", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.2, y=30.7},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1240}, names={"The Troll Witchdoctor"}, text="Keep the head for Kin'weelay in Grom'gol (Stranglethorn, a later segment)", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.2, y=30.7},
  {t="FLY", seg=13, arg="Ratchet", text="Shardi, the Brackenwall wind rider master"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1270}, names={"Stinky's Escape"}, text="Mebok Mizzyrix", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.4, y=37.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=13, arg="Gadgetzan"},
  {t="G", seg=13, text="Ghost Wolf north out of Gadgetzan to the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.0, y=77.0},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1112}, names={"Parts for Kravel"}, text="Kravel Koalbeard", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1114}, names={"Delivery to the Gnomes"}, zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1114}, names={"Delivery to the Gnomes"}, text="Fizzle Brassbolts, a few steps away", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1115}, names={"The Rumormonger"}, text="Kravel. Keep it for Krazek in Booty Bay.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1106}, names={"Martek the Exiled"}, text="Fizzle. Keep the letter for Martek the Exiled in the Badlands (next segment).", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1146}, names={"The Swarm Grows"}, text="Moktar Krin, north-west across the flats at their western edge, where the canyon road from Freewind Post comes down", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=67.6, y=63.9},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1147}, names={"The Swarm Grows"}, zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=67.6, y=63.9},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1148}, names={"Parts of the Swarm"}, text="Silithid hive south of Moktar Krin. Kill silithids until a Cracked Silithid Carapace drops and right-click it at once, so the parts start dropping.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=67.7, y=82.5, path={{67.8,62.1},{69.0,62.1},{69.4,65.7},{71.0,68.7},{70.4,77.4},{67.4,81.6}}},
  {t="C", seg=13, q={1147,1148}, names={"The Swarm Grows","Parts of the Swarm"}, text="Same hive: 5 Searchers, 5 Hive Drones, 5 Invaders, plus 1 Heart, 5 Talons and 3 Intact Carapaces from any of them. Searchers (32-33) are on the north and east edge, Drones (33-34) fill the middle, Invaders (34-35) hold the west edge (64,86). They stand in groups: pull from the edge, drop Stoneclaw Totem when two come, Earthbind any that run. The Silithid Ravager (37, rare) walks the north side: fight it only when it is alone.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=68.5, y=85.5},
  {t="L", seg=13, lvl=37, text="Not 37 yet? Keep killing silithids here; the Invaders (34-35) on the west edge give the most XP. The five turn-ins still ahead add about 11k XP, so you can stop that far short of 37.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=68.5, y=85.5},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1147}, names={"The Swarm Grows"}, text="Back north to Moktar Krin", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=67.6, y=63.9},
  {t="G", seg=13, text="Ghost Wolf west up the canyon road to Freewind Post (wind rider master Nyse)", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=45.1, y=49.1},
  {t="FLY", seg=13, arg="Thunder Bluff"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1276}, names={"The Black Shield"}, text="Mosarn", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=54.0, y=80.8},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=13, text="Shaman trainers in the Pools of Vision under Spirit Rise, beside Apothecary Zamah: learn your level 36 spells (and any level 34 ones you skipped at the start of this segment)", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=22.8, y=21.1},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1049}, names={"Compendium of the Fallen"}, text="Sage Truthseeker. The Compendium of the Fallen is in the Library wing. Not offered to Undead.", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=34.4, y=46.9, dg=10},
  {t="FLY", seg=13, arg="Crossroads"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1148}, names={"Parts of the Swarm"}, text="Korran", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=51.1, y=29.6},
  {t="A", seg=13, q={1184}, names={"Parts of the Swarm"}, text="Korran. For Belgrom in Orgrimmar.", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=51.1, y=29.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=13, arg="Orgrimmar"},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1184}, names={"Parts of the Swarm"}, text="Belgrom Rockmaul, Valley of Honor (east side of the city)", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=75.2, y=34.2},
  {t="T", seg=13, q={1436}, names={"Alliance Relations"}, text="Keldran, on the west side of the city", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=22.6, y=52.6},
  {t="N", seg=13, arg="Start saving gold for your mount", text="At 40 (first step of segment 16) you learn Wolf Riding from Kildar and buy a wolf from Ogunaro in the Valley of Honor: roughly 90-100 gold at Classic prices. Keep about that much from here on; sell greys and skip pricey upgrades."},
  {t="N", seg=13, arg="Take the zeppelin to the Undercity", text="Leave by the main gate; the zeppelin tower is just outside. Board the zeppelin to Tirisfal Glades (Undercity), not the one to Grom'gol. Your hearthstone stays on Shadowprey Village.", zone="Durotar", map=1411, x=50.8, y=13.5},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="You arrive at the zeppelin tower outside the Undercity", text="Your hearthstone stays set to Shadowprey Village for this whole trip: do not use it or Astral Recall until a later segment says so. Keep saving gold for Wolf Riding and a wolf at 40 (roughly 90-100g)."},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Optional: get ready for the dives at Faldir's Cove", text="Some of those quests are underwater and an orc runs out of breath fast. If you have Water Breathing, carry a few Shiny Fish Scales for it (reagent vendors sell them, and the naga at the cove drop them). An Elixir of Water Breathing from the Auction House works too. Without either, just surface for air between dives."},
  {t="FLY", seg=14, arg="Hammerfall", text="Walk south from the tower into the ruined city and ride an elevator down. Bat handler Michael Garrett stands by the west elevator.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=63.2, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1113}, names={"Hearts of Zeal"}, text="Master Apothecary Faranell. 20 Hearts of Zeal from any Scarlet enemies in the monastery.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.8, y=69.3, dg=10, req=1109},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1048}, names={"Into The Scarlet Monastery"}, text="Varimathras in the Royal Quarter. Kill Houndmaster Loksey (Library), Herod (Armory), and Mograine and Whitemane (Cathedral). Needs level 33.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=56.2, y=92.2, dg=10},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Optional dungeon: Scarlet Monastery, levels 30-46", text="The monastery is in the north-east corner of Tirisfal Glades; from Undercity ride east past Brill and north at the Bulwark road. It has four wings, each its own run: Graveyard (30-38), Library (33-41), Armory (36-44) and Cathedral (38-46). Inside the Graveyard wing, Vorrel Sengutz gives Vorrel's Revenge (the ring drops in the Graveyard wing; hand in to Monika Sengutz in Tarren Mill). Quests you picked up for it: Compendium of the Fallen, Hearts of Zeal, Into The Scarlet Monastery.", zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=82.6, y=33.8, dg=10, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1048}, names={"Into The Scarlet Monastery"}, zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=56.2, y=92.2, dg=10},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1113}, names={"Hearts of Zeal"}, zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.8, y=69.3, dg=10},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={701}, names={"Guile of the Raptor"}, text="Tor'gan. He offered it after Raising Spirits in segment 11.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={678}, names={"Call to Arms"}, text="Drum Fel. The second Call to Arms, left with him in segment 11.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.2, y=33.9},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={701,678}, names={"Guile of the Raptor","Call to Arms"}, text="Boulderfist Hall, south-west of Hammerfall. Highland Fleshstalker raptors (36-37) roam the hills around it; a heart drops about one kill in three. The Brutes and Magi (35-37) are in and around the ogre cave: Earth Shock the Magi's casts and drop Stoneclaw Totem if a second ogre joins.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=52.0, y=75.0, path={{73.4,30.7},{70.8,31.9},{70.6,35.8},{68.8,38.5},{68.8,45.4},{66.0,51.0},{60.0,51.0},{58.0,53.1},{57.8,57.3},{54.0,63.0},{53.9,76.8}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={701}, names={"Guile of the Raptor"}, text="Tor'gan", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3, path={{54.6,61.5},{57.8,56.7},{58.0,53.1},{59.4,51.0},{66.0,51.0},{68.8,46.9},{68.8,41.2},{70.4,38.5},{71.6,30.7},{76.7,32.8},{76.7,35.8}}},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={702}, names={"Guile of the Raptor"}, text="Tor'gan", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={702}, names={"Guile of the Raptor"}, text="Gor'mul", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=72.6, y=33.9},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={847}, names={"Guile of the Raptor"}, text="Gor'mul", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=72.6, y=33.9},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={847}, names={"Guile of the Raptor"}, text="Back to Tor'gan", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.7, y=36.3},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={678}, names={"Call to Arms"}, text="Drum Fel. Skip the follow-ups 679 and 680: both are elite.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=74.2, y=33.9},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={663}, names={"Land Ho!"}, text="Ghost Wolf south-west across Arathi to Faldir's Cove on the coast; Lolo the Lookout stands at the camp. These quests are level 40.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=31.8, y=82.7},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={663}, names={"Land Ho!"}, text="Shakes O'Breen", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.3, y=81.4},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={662,664,665}, names={"Deep Sea Salvage","Drowned Sorrows","Sunken Treasure"}, text="First Mate Nilzlix, Captain Steelgut and Professor Phizzlethorpe, all in the camp", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.8, y=81.5},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={665}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Escort the professor to the cave up the hill and back. Vengeful Surge water elementals (40) ambush you at the cave: drop Stoneclaw Totem, kill them one at a time and throw him a Healing Wave if he gets low.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.5},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={665}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Doctor Draxlegauge", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.4},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={666}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Doctor Draxlegauge. He lends you the Goggles of Gem Hunting: they are not worn. Right-click them in your bags to make the calcified gems on the sea floor visible, and use them again if the gems disappear.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.5},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={662,664,666}, names={"Deep Sea Salvage","Drowned Sorrows","Sunken Treasure"}, text="West of the cove. The charts and logs are inside the two wrecks (Maiden's Folly and Spirit of Silverpine), the gems lie on the sea floor around them, and the Daggerspine Raiders and Sorceresses (38-40) are on the reef and shore. Watch your breath bar and surface between dives, or cast Water Breathing. Pull the naga one at a time and Earth Shock the Sorceresses' casts.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=21.5, y=86.0},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={662}, names={"Deep Sea Salvage"}, text="Nilzlix", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.8, y=81.5},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={664}, names={"Drowned Sorrows"}, text="Steelgut", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=34.0, y=80.8},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={666}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Draxlegauge, return the goggles", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.5},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={668}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Draxlegauge", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=33.9, y=80.4},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={668}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Shakes O'Breen", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.3, y=81.4},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={669}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Shakes O'Breen. Keep the gem for Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay (segment 15).", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=32.3, y=81.4},
  {t="G", seg=14, text="Ghost Wolf east to Thandol Span, the great bridge at the south edge of Arathi. Dark Iron dwarves stand on it: keep moving.", zone="Arathi Highlands", map=1417, x=48.5, y=87.5},
  {t="G", seg=14, text="Cross the bridge into the Wetlands, keep clear of the Dark Iron fort of Dun Modr just past the bridge and follow the road south to the Dun Algaz pass.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=54.2, y=70.3},
  {t="G", seg=14, text="Go through Dun Algaz into Loch Modan. The Alliance mountaineers at the gates are level 30. Head south down the west side of the zone, keeping Thelsamar well to your left (east), to the pass into the Badlands. Mountaineer Pebblebitty (44) stands at the pass: run past him.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=18.5, y=85.0},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1106}, names={"Martek the Exiled"}, text="Martek the Exiled, south along the road from the pass. Shadowforge dwarves dig near the pass: don't stray.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.2, y=52.7},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1108}, names={"Indurium"}, text="Martek", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.2, y=52.7},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={703}, names={"Barbecued Buzzard Wings"}, text="Rigglefuzz, next to Martek. Skip Pearl Diving (705, elite-flagged).", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.4, y=52.9},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={710}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil Veriatus, west along the road", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="F", seg=14, arg="Kargath", text="Gorrik, the wind rider master at the west edge of the Badlands", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=4.0, y=44.8, path={{25.6,47.8},{24.5,49.6},{16.1,49.3},{14.3,46.6},{14.5,43.3},{12.1,41.8},{3.9,41.2},{3.3,43.6}}},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={2258,1419}, names={"Badlands Reagent Run","Coyote Thieves"}, text="Jarkal Mossmeld and Neeka Bloodscar. Gorn's Broken Alliances (782) needs level 40: leave it.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.4, y=46.1},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={710,2258}, obj={0,3}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock","Badlands Reagent Run"}, text="Lesser rock elementals (37-39) between Kargath and Lotwil's camp. Rock Elemental Shards drop from them too.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=18.8, y=43.0},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={710}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={711}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1419,2258,703}, names={"Coyote Thieves","Badlands Reagent Run","Barbecued Buzzard Wings"}, text="South-west of Lotwil's camp. Giant Buzzards (39-41) circle here, around 16,60, and a few more around 12,70. They drop the wings, but only about 1 in 5 drops a gizzard, so kill every buzzard you see and check back for respawns. Elder Crag Coyotes (38-40) on the same hills drop the jawbones and fangs (4 kills in 5 give each). 30 jawbones take a while: finish them on the coyotes further east and south-east, on your way to the Rock Elementals at 41,79.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=18.0, y=60.0},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={711}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Rock Elementals (39-40) in the rocky hills just south-west of the Stonevault trogg camp. You need 3 slabs and nearly every kill drops one. They hit hard but have no ranged attack: fight one at a time with Stoneskin Totem down and Lightning Shield up, and Healing Wave between pulls.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=41.0, y=79.0},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={1108}, names={"Indurium"}, text="Stonevault trogg camp. Only the Stonevault Bonesnappers and Shamans here drop the indurium flakes (about 60%); Earth Shock the Shamans' casts. Still short of jawbones, fangs or wings? The Feral Crag Coyotes and Buzzards around this camp drop those (these Buzzards rarely drop a gizzard).", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=50.5, y=68.0},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={709}, names={"Solution to Doom"}, text="Theldurin the Lost. The Tablet of Ryun'eh is in the tunnels before the dungeon portal.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=51.4, y=76.9, dg=12},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1108}, names={"Indurium"}, text="Martek", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.2, y=52.7},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1137}, names={"News for Fizzle"}, text="Martek. Keep it for Fizzle on the Shimmering Flats (segment 16).", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.2, y=52.7},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={703}, names={"Barbecued Buzzard Wings"}, text="Rigglefuzz", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.4, y=52.9},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={2418}, names={"Power Stones"}, text="Rigglefuzz. Power Stones drop from the Shadowforge dwarves in and around Uldaman.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=42.4, y=52.9, dg=12},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={711}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={712}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil. Keep it: the Greater Rock Elementals (42-44, far south-west) that drop the bracers wait for your second Badlands visit (segment 18).", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={2258}, names={"Badlands Reagent Run"}, text="Jarkal. Do not take Uldaman Reagent Run (2202): it is a dungeon quest.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.4, y=46.1, path={{25.6,47.8},{24.5,49.6},{21.1,49.9},{16.9,56.1},{12.9,59.4},{8.5,59.1},{6.7,56.1},{5.9,51.0}}},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1419}, names={"Coyote Thieves"}, text="Neeka Bloodscar", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=6.5, y=47.2},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={1420}, names={"Report to Helgrum"}, text="Neeka Bloodscar: her report for Helgrum the Swift, who stands by the wind rider master in Stonard. Keep it for segment 15. If she does not offer it, skip this step.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=6.5, y=47.2},
  {t="L", seg=14, lvl=39, text="Quest XP runs out here, and the Alterac quests next are level 40-42 with level 38-41 mobs. Grind the Rock Elementals (39-40) on the slopes north-east of Kargath; if they are thin, a bigger group sits in the south around 41,79, and the lesser rock elementals line the road east to Lotwil's camp. Stoneskin Totem, Lightning Shield, Healing Wave between pulls. The Stonevault troggs drop coins and cloth if you would rather save for the wolf.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=14.5, y=35.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=14, arg="Tarren Mill", text="Gorrik in Kargath", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=4.0, y=44.8},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Optional dungeon: Krol'dok Stronghold, levels 40-45", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is in the Riverglades, the new zone east of the Badlands: a fortress on a hill at about 48.6, 26.3 on the Riverglades map. Horde players fly to Rog'mar. No Horde quest givers are published yet: take any dungeon quests you are offered in Rog'mar and the addon logs them so these steps can be filled in.", dg=18, run=true},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={566}, names={"WANTED: Baron Vardus"}, text="The WANTED poster in Tarren Mill", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.6, y=20.8},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={1051}, names={"Vorrel's Revenge"}, text="Vorrel's Revenge: Monika Sengutz in the Tarren Mill inn.", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.7, y=18.9, dg=10},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={507}, names={"Lord Aliden Perenolde"}, text="Krusk. He only offers it if you freed Gol'dir and handed in Blackmoore's Legacy (506) in segment 11. If he has nothing for you, skip the 507 and 508 steps below.", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.2, y=20.7},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={566}, names={"WANTED: Baron Vardus"}, text="Ghost Wolf north out of Tarren Mill on the road past Strahnbrad, then up to the Uplands at the north edge of Alterac. Baron Vardus (40) stands among Syndicate Sentries (36-37): pull the sentries off him one at a time, then kill him and take his head. Keep away from the elite Crushridge ogres in the middle of the zone.", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=47.8, y=17.1},
  {t="C", seg=14, q={507}, names={"Lord Aliden Perenolde"}, text="Perenolde's manor lies west of the Uplands, on the shore of Lordamere Lake. Lord Aliden Perenolde (41) is inside, with Syndicate Assassins and Enforcers (38-40) around the manor. Clear them one pull at a time, drop Stoneclaw Totem if two come, Earthbind any runner, and fight him at full health and mana.", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=39.3, y=14.6, path={{47.6,18.4},{43.6,18.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={507}, names={"Lord Aliden Perenolde"}, text="Talk to Elysa, who stands right next to him", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=39.3, y=14.3},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={508}, names={"Taretha's Gift"}, text="Elysa gives you Taretha's pendant", zone="Alterac Mountains", map=1416, x=39.3, y=14.3},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={508}, names={"Taretha's Gift"}, text="Back in Tarren Mill: Krusk", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=63.2, y=20.7},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={566}, names={"WANTED: Baron Vardus"}, text="High Executor Darthalia, beside the poster", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=62.3, y=20.5},
  {t="FLY", seg=14, arg="Undercity", text="Zarise, Tarren Mill's bat handler", zone="Hillsbrad Foothills", map=1424, x=60.1, y=18.6},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={232}, names={"Errand for Apothecary Zinge"}, text="Apothecary Zinge in the Apothecarium. These errands need level 38.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=50.1, y=68.0},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={232}, names={"Errand for Apothecary Zinge"}, text="Alessandro Luca", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=58.6, y=54.7},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={238}, names={"Errand for Apothecary Zinge"}, text="Alessandro Luca", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=58.6, y=54.7},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={3341}, names={"Bring the End"}, text="Andrew Brownell in the Magic Quarter. Kill Amnennar the Coldbringer, the last boss. Needs level 37.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=74.0, y=33.3, dg=11},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={2342}, names={"Reclaimed Treasures"}, text="Patrick Garrett in the Trade Quarter. His family chest is in the South Common Hall, before the dungeon portal.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=62.3, y=48.6, dg=12},
  {t="T", seg=14, q={238}, names={"Errand for Apothecary Zinge"}, text="Back to Apothecary Zinge", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=50.1, y=68.0},
  {t="A", seg=14, q={243}, names={"Into the Field"}, text="Apothecary Zinge. Keep it: you hand it in at Gadgetzan (segment 16).", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=50.1, y=68.0},
  {t="N", seg=14, arg="Take the zeppelin to Grom'gol", text="Leave the Undercity and climb the zeppelin tower again. Two zeppelins stop there: Hin Denburg's goes to Grom'gol in Stranglethorn, the other one to Orgrimmar. Segment 15 starts at Grom'gol.", zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=61.8, y=59.2},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="You arrive at Grom'gol Base Camp on the zeppelin from the Undercity", text="Your hearthstone still points at Shadowprey Village: do not use it or Astral Recall until you bind in Booty Bay later in this segment. Keep saving for Wolf Riding and a wolf at 40 (roughly 90-100 gold)."},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1240}, names={"The Troll Witchdoctor"}, text="Kin'weelay", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.3, y=27.7},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1261}, names={"Marg Speaks"}, text="Click the Bubbling Cauldron beside Kin'weelay. Keep it: the Jeweled Pendant drops from the Muckshell crab-men in Dustwallow Marsh (segment 16).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.6},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={598}, names={"Split Bone Necklace"}, text="Kin'weelay. Keep it: the Skullsplitter trolls that drop the necklaces are level 40+ (segment 18).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.3, y=27.7},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={568}, names={"The Defense of Grom'gol"}, text="Commander Aggro'gosh", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=28.9},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={570}, names={"Mok'thardin's Enchantment"}, text="Far Seer Mok'thardin", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.1, y=29.2},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Take any new quests offered in Grom'gol; the logger records them", text="Forever adds a Horde naga quest here: Enemies in the Water (level 37), 10 Brinescale Tridents from the Brinescale Skirmishers around the sunken troll ruins in the sea west of the camp. Take it if you have log room: you do it on the way back from Zul'Kunda and hand it in here."},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={5763}, names={"Hunting in Stranglethorn"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary. Ghost Wolf north up the road from Grom'gol to the hunters' camp.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={187}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, text="Ajeck Rouack", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.6, y=10.6},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={192}, names={"Panther Mastery"}, text="Sir S. J. Erlgadin", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.5, y=10.6},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={195}, names={"Raptor Mastery"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={187}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, text="Elder Stranglethorn Tigers (34-35) on the slopes just south of the camp. Cats often come in pairs: drop Stoneclaw Totem to hold the second one while you kill the first.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=34.0, y=18.5},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={187}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, text="Ajeck Rouack", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.6, y=10.6},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={188}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, text="Ajeck Rouack", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.6, y=10.6},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={188}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, text="Sin'Dall, a named tigress (37) on the hill south-west of the camp. Clear the tigers around her first and fight her at full health and mana.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=17.4, path={{31.2,15.4},{31.2,17.2}}},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={568,195}, names={"The Defense of Grom'gol","Raptor Mastery"}, text="Lashtail Raptors (35-36) in the jungle south of Sin'Dall's hill, between the camp and Grom'gol. 15 for Aggro'gosh, 10 for Hemet: the same kills count for both. Earthbind Totem keeps a second raptor off you.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.0, y=23.0},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={577}, names={"Some Assembly Required"}, text="Snapjaw Crocolisks (35-36) in and around Lake Nazferiti, east of the raptors. About 1 in 3 drops a skin.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=40.0, y=22.0},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={1182}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Kill Foreman Cozzle (38) at the Venture Co. camp on the lake's north-east shore for his key, then open Cozzle's Footlocker in his house (43.3, 20.3). Pull the Venture Co. Geologists around him one at a time first.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=42.6, y=18.4},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={213}, names={"Hostile Takeover"}, text="Hostile Takeover: the Venture Co. Geologists (34-36) in the same camp and along the north shore of the lake carry Tumbled Crystals, about one in two. You need 8", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=42.6, y=18.4},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={192,570}, names={"Panther Mastery","Mok'thardin's Enchantment"}, text="Shadowmaw Panthers and Stranglethorn Tigresses (37-38) fill the jungle south of the lake, between the small ogre camp east of Grom'gol and the Crystalvein Mine. Head straight south-west from Cozzle's camp and do not drift east: the big Mosh'Ogg Mound (around 49,28) is full of elite ogres. Panthers drop the claws; only about 1 tigress in 7 drops the Pristine Tigress Fang. Panthers stalk unseen, so keep Lightning Shield up, and Stoneclaw Totem holds a second cat.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=39.0, y=37.0},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={188}, names={"Tiger Mastery"}, text="Ghost Wolf north past Grom'gol (its hand-ins come after Zul'Kunda) to Ajeck Rouack at Nesingwary's camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.6, y=10.6},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={192}, names={"Panther Mastery"}, text="Sir S. J. Erlgadin. Skip the next part (Bhag'thera, elite).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.5, y=10.6},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={195}, names={"Raptor Mastery"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary. Leave the next part (Jungle Stalkers, level 41) for a later visit.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Ruins of Zul'Kunda: if you skipped the NEW quests there in segment 11, take them now", text="Zeppelin crash debris east of the ruins and a caged goblin, Zimmix Sputterspark, inside. Do them together with the headhunters; they end in Booty Bay, your next stop. The logger records them."},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={582}, names={"Headhunting"}, text="Bloodscalp Headhunters (36-37) around the Ruins of Zul'Kunda, west of Nesingwary's camp near the coast. Most of them drop a head. Fight at the edge of the ruins so only one comes at a time, and Earth Shock the Mystics' and Witch Doctors' casts.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=23.0, y=10.0, path={{33.8,11.8},{28.0,9.1}}},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Enemies in the Water, if you took it", text="On the way back south, swim out to the Vile Reef, the sunken troll ruins off the coast north-west of Grom'gol (about 20-26, 19-32). The Brinescale Skirmishers are underwater: cast Water Breathing (one Shiny Fish Scale per cast) or come up for air between fights. Lesser Water Elementals (36-37) drift around the reef and elite Saltscale murlocs (35-37) may hold its middle (around 23-25, 23-26), so pull the naga one at a time from the north and south edges. Skip the elite Elder Saltwater Crocolisk by the north shore.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=22.5, y=21.5},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={568}, names={"The Defense of Grom'gol"}, text="Commander Aggro'gosh, back south in Grom'gol. Took Enemies in the Water? Hand it in now to whoever gave it to you here.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=28.9},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={569}, names={"The Defense of Grom'gol"}, zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=28.9},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={582}, names={"Headhunting"}, text="Nimboya", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.7},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={584}, names={"Bloodscalp Clan Heads"}, text="Keep it for segment 18 (Gan'zulah and Nezzliok, level 40-41)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.7},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={569}, names={"The Defense of Grom'gol"}, text="Mosh'Ogg Brutes and Witch Doctors (36-37) at the small ogre camp just east of Grom'gol. Earth Shock the Witch Doctors' casts and drop Stoneclaw Totem if two ogres come. Still missing the Pristine Tigress Fang? The tigresses you hunted earlier prowl the jungle just south of this camp.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=37.0, y=31.0},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={569}, names={"The Defense of Grom'gol"}, text="Commander Aggro'gosh", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=28.9},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={570}, names={"Mok'thardin's Enchantment"}, text="Far Seer Mok'thardin. Leave his next quest for a later visit (level 41).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.1, y=29.2},
  {t="FLY", seg=15, arg="Booty Bay", text="Thysta, Grom'gol's wind rider master"},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1182}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Baron Revilgaz, top floor of the inn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=76.9},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1183}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Keep the blueprints for Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats (segment 16)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=76.9},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={577}, names={"Some Assembly Required"}, text="Drizzlik. Skip Excelsior (628): the crocolisk is elite.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.3, y=77.6},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1115}, names={"The Rumormonger"}, text="Krazek", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1116}, names={"Dream Dust in the Swamp"}, text="Keep it for the Swamp of Sorrows", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={669}, names={"Sunken Treasure"}, text="Fleet Master Seahorn. Skip his next quest (670): it only sends you back to Faldir's Cove.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Optional dungeon: The Drowned City, levels 35-40", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is on Gillijim's Isle, in the sea south-west of Stranglethorn Vale; the portal is in a cave called Sunken Hollow, and no boat or flight path was known to go there. Horde quests for it are listed from Krazek in Booty Bay (Shady Saltseers, The Saltseer Captain), Commander Aggro'gosh and Kin'weelay in Grom'gol, and Mazu'kon in Mulgore. Take what they offer: the addon logs it so these steps can be filled in.", dg=17, run=true},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Hand in any Zul'Kunda NEW quests you did (the goblin escort ends at Wharfmaster Lozgil on the dock)"},
  {t="S", seg=15, arg="Booty Bay", text="Innkeeper Skindle. You hearth back here from the Swamp of Sorrows at the end of this segment."},
  {t="FLY", seg=15, arg="Grom'gol", text="Gringer, the Booty Bay wind rider master"},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Run from Grom'gol to the Swamp of Sorrows", text="Ghost Wolf north up the road past Nesingwary's camp into Duskwood, then east along the main road. Go round Darkshire (Alliance guards), take the road east through Deadwind Pass and follow it down into the swamp. Stay on the road in Deadwind Pass: the ogres and ghosts there are level 50+."},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={1116}, names={"Dream Dust in the Swamp"}, text="Dreaming and Adolescent Whelps (34-36) in the misty valley at the west end of the swamp, right by the road. About 1 whelp in 5 drops a speck and there are only about a dozen of them: kill them all once and move on. The rest of the dust comes from the green dragonkin east of Stonard at the end of the swamp loop, where you also grind to 40.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=14.0, y=61.0},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Optional: Amaryllis Webb", text="On the way east she may offer My Little Friends (new in Forever): catch three kinds of bugs with her kit. Where the bugs live is not known yet, so take it only if you have log room, and abandon it if they are not in this swamp. The logger records it.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=25.0, y=54.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1389}, names={"Draenethyst Crystals"}, text="Magtoor at the Harborage, the draenei village due north of Amaryllis in the north-west of the swamp. Taking it now saves running back here before Fallow Sanctuary.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.0, y=31.4},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Take any new quests offered at the Harborage; the logger records them", text="New Forever quests here are done at Fallow Sanctuary: Blood of My Blood (kill 10 Lost Ones) and Taking the Bait Back (a Lost One Fisherman on the banks east of the village has Pelluk's lure). Hand them in when you come back at the end of the swamp loop. Skip the draenethyst errand that sends you to Desolace to find a human named Azore (93464): it is 700 XP for a trip this route does not make.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.0, y=31.4},
  {t="F", seg=15, arg="Stonard", text="Breyk, the wind rider master in the orc town south-east of the Harborage", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=46.1, y=54.8},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1420}, names={"Report to Helgrum"}, text="Helgrum the Swift, next to Breyk: give him Neeka's report from Kargath (skip this step if she did not offer it). Do not take his Neeka Bloodscar (1418).", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=47.7, y=55.2},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=15, text="Haromm in Stonard, the only shaman trainer in the Eastern Kingdoms: learn your level 38 spells. Level 40 waits for Orgrimmar at the start of the next segment.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=48.2, y=57.9},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={698}, names={"Lack of Surplus"}, text="Dar. Keep it: Tok'Kar on the south-east coast takes the flanks in segment 18.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=44.7, y=57.2},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Take any new quests offered in Stonard; the logger records them", text="Dar may offer a new Forever quest about a lost shipment for the Harborage (Lost in Transit): if so, look for the courier's crate by the water along the road and bring it to the Harborage when you go back there at the end of the loop.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=44.7, y=57.2},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={1389}, names={"Draenethyst Crystals"}, text="Fallow Sanctuary, north-east of Stonard: the crystals sit among the Lost Ones' huts and campfires. Pull the Lost Ones from the edges and Earth Shock the Seers' and Riftseekers' casts. Kill every Sawtooth Crocolisk (38-39) you pass for Dar's flanks: about 1 in 4 drops one.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=62.4, y=22.7},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1393}, names={"Galen's Escape"}, text="Galen Goodward, just north-east of the crystals. Accepting starts the escort.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=65.5, y=18.2},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={1393}, names={"Galen's Escape"}, text="Keep Galen alive until he says he is safe. If something attacks him, drop Stoneclaw Totem to pull it off him and throw him a Healing Wave if he gets low. If he dies, abandon 1393 and take it again when he respawns.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=65.5, y=18.2},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1393}, names={"Galen's Escape"}, text="Open Galen's strongbox at his camp, north of Stonard", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=47.8, y=39.8},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1392}, names={"Noboru the Cudgel"}, text="Kill Noboru the Cudgel (39). He wanders the area roughly between here and 42,36. His cudgel starts the quest. Fight him at full health and mana with Stoneskin Totem down.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=55.7, y=34.4},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={698}, names={"Lack of Surplus"}, text="Finish the 8 sawtooth flanks on the Sawtooth Crocolisks (38-39) along the water between Galen's camp and Stonard. The small Young Sawtooth Crocolisks further west do not drop them. Keep the flanks for Tok'Kar (segment 18).", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=56.0, y=45.0},
  {t="C", seg=15, q={1116}, names={"Dream Dust in the Swamp"}, text="Finish the dream dust on the green dragonkin just east of the crocolisks: Green Scalebanes (42-43) around 60-65,37-43, plus a few Green Wyrmkin and Wyrmkin Dreamwalkers (41-43) south of them around 60-62,52-60. Each drops a speck about 1 time in 5. Pull them one at a time from the edge with Stoneskin Totem down and Healing Wave between fights; take on the Scalebane Captains (43-44) only at full health. Do not go east of about 66: Lord Captain Wyrmak, a level 45 rare elite, may stand at 69,39, and the Elder Dragonkin (45) further east are far too strong.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=62.5, y=40.5},
  {t="L", seg=15, lvl=40, text="Not 40 yet? Keep killing the dragonkin here or south of here (stay west of 66), or the Sawtooth Crocolisks by the water. The Harborage hand-ins next add about 5k XP (more with the new quests), so you can stop a little short. MacKinley's quest in Booty Bay needs 40.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=62.5, y=40.5},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1389,1392}, names={"Draenethyst Crystals","Noboru the Cudgel"}, text="Back to Magtoor at the Harborage. Hand in the new Harborage quests too.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=26.0, y=31.4},
  {t="H", seg=15, arg="Booty Bay", text="Hearthstone, or cast Astral Recall: both are bound to Booty Bay now"},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={213}, names={"Hostile Takeover"}, text="Kebok, in the inn: the 8 Tumbled Crystals", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=15, q={1116}, names={"Dream Dust in the Swamp"}, text="Krazek", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={1117}, names={"Rumors for Kravel"}, text="Krazek. Keep the rumors for Kravel Koalbeard on the Shimmering Flats (segment 16).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={2864}, names={"Tran'rek"}, text="Krazek in Booty Bay. It sends you to Tran'rek in Gadgetzan.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.2, dg=13},
  {t="A", seg=15, q={2872}, names={"Stoley's Debt"}, text="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley, near the inn. It needs level 40. Keep it for Stoley in Steamwheedle Port, Tanaris (segment 16).", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.8, y=77.1},
  {t="FLY", seg=15, arg="Grom'gol", text="Gringer"},
  {t="N", seg=15, arg="Take the zeppelin to Orgrimmar", text="The zeppelin tower is at Grom'gol's west edge. Squibby Overspeck's zeppelin goes to Orgrimmar; Nez'raz's goes to the Undercity. Segment 16 starts at the Orgrimmar tower, where you learn Wolf Riding.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=31.5, y=29.4},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="You arrive at the zeppelin tower outside Orgrimmar", text="Go in through the main gate. Your hearthstone still points at Booty Bay: leave it alone until you bind in Gadgetzan.", zone="Durotar", map=1411, x=50.8, y=13.5},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Learn Wolf Riding and buy a wolf", text="Valley of Honor, the north-east part of the city. Kildar teaches Wolf Riding and Ogunaro Wolfrunner (69.4, 12.2), right next to him, sells the wolves: about 90-100 gold for both. Short of gold? Buy them on the Orgrimmar stop of the next segment and keep using Ghost Wolf until then.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=69.4, y=13.1},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={2981}, names={"A Threat in Feralas"}, text="Belgrom Rockmaul, at the south end of the Valley of Honor. It only sends you to Rok Orhan at Camp Mojache, early in the next segment", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=75.2, y=34.2},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=16, text="Valley of Wisdom: learn your level 40 spells, and any level 38 ones you did not get from Haromm in Stonard", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=38.8, y=36.4},
  {t="FLY", seg=16, arg="Thunder Bluff", text="Doras, on the tower in the Valley of Strength", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=45.1, y=63.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1205}, names={"Deadmire"}, text="Melor Stonehoof on Hunter Rise (the south mesa). Deadmire is a crocolisk in Dustwallow Marsh; you bring the tooth back here later in this segment, when you come to train.", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=61.5, y=80.9},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1049}, names={"Compendium of the Fallen"}, zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=34.4, y=46.9, dg=10},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Optional dungeon: Razorfen Downs, levels 37-46", text="The entrance is at the southern tip of the Barrens, just east of the Great Lift down to Thousand Needles. Fly to Camp Taurajo or Freewind Post and ride. Myriam Moonsinger at the entrance gives A Host of Evil (the enemies it asks for are outside the portal); hand it back to her after the run. Inside: Belnistrasz gives a short quest and then an escort to the idol; Ambassador Malcin (outside the portal) can drop a Small Scroll that starts a quest for Varimathras in Undercity. Quests you picked up for it: Bring the End.", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=49.0, y=93.9, dg=11, run=true},
  {t="FLY", seg=16, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Tal, the wind rider master on the central mesa"},
  {t="S", seg=16, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Innkeeper Fizzgrimble at the inn"},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={243}, names={"Into the Field"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle, in the middle of town", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={379}, names={"Slake That Thirst"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle. Keep it for the Wastewander camps later.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1117}, names={"Rumors for Kravel"}, text="Ride north out of Gadgetzan into Thousand Needles to the Mirage Raceway. Kravel Koalbeard is on the gnome side of the track. Skip Back to Booty Bay, which he offers next: a log slot for very little XP.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.8, y=77.3},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1137}, names={"News for Fizzle"}, text="Fizzle Brassbolts, also on the gnome side", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1183}, names={"Goblin Sponsorship"}, text="Pozzik, on the goblin side of the track", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1186}, names={"The Eighteenth Pilot"}, text="Pozzik", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1186}, names={"The Eighteenth Pilot"}, text="Razzeric, right next to Pozzik", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.3, y=76.1},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1187}, names={"Razzeric's Tweaking"}, text="Razzeric. The booster is in a crashed zeppelin in Dustwallow Marsh.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.3, y=76.1},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1190}, names={"Keeping Pace"}, text="Pozzik", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Ask Zamek for his distraction", text="Zamek stands on the goblin side. Take Zamek's Distraction; while his explosion goes off, run straight to Rizzle's tent on the gnome side.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=79.8, y=77.0},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1190}, names={"Keeping Pace"}, text="Click Rizzle's Unguarded Plans in the tent while Rizzle is away", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.2, y=77.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1194}, names={"Rizzle's Schematics"}, text="From the same plans", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=77.2, y=77.4},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1194}, names={"Rizzle's Schematics"}, text="Pozzik", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.2, y=75.9},
  {t="FLY", seg=16, arg="Brackenwall Village", text="Ride back south to Gadgetzan and fly from Bulkrek Ragefist"},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1168}, names={"Army of the Black Dragon"}, text="Tharg", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=37.4, y=31.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1169}, names={"Identifying the Brood"}, text="Draz'Zilb. Skip Overlord Mok'Morokk's Concern (elite).", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=37.1, y=33.1},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={1205}, names={"Deadmire"}, text="Ride south down the road past Tabetha's hut. Deadmire (45) is a crocolisk in the water just east of the hut. He hits hard: pull him onto the shore, drop Stoneskin Totem, keep Lightning Shield up and Healing Wave once you fall below half. At 40-41 he is 4-5 levels above you: if your shocks keep missing or he takes half your health in a few hits, drop Earthbind Totem and leave, abandon Deadmire and skip its hand-in at Melor later in this segment.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=48.8, y=56.8},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={2846}, names={"Tiara of the Deep"}, text="Tabetha, in her hut in the marsh. The Tiara of the Deep drops from Hydromancer Velratha.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=46.1, y=57.1, dg=13},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={1187}, names={"Razzeric's Tweaking"}, text="The crashed zeppelin is a short way further east. Loot the Gizmorium Shipping Crate inside the wreck.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=54.1, y=56.5},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={1261}, names={"Marg Speaks"}, text="Marg's Jeweled Pendant: ride south-east from the wreck to the shore. Muckshell crab-men (39-43: Clackers, Pincers, Scrabblers) walk the beach around 54-57, 61-65. Each has about a 5% chance to drop it, so expect roughly 20 kills.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=55.8, y=63.0},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={1168,1169}, names={"Army of the Black Dragon","Identifying the Brood"}, text="Ride west along the south of the marsh into the Wyrmbog. Firemane Scouts and Ash Tails (41-43) are in the north-west part (around 42, 67); Firemane Scalebanes (43-44) and the Searing Hatchlings and Whelps are further south-east (around 47, 74). The tongues and hearts drop from the hatchlings and whelps. Single pulls: Earth Shock the Flamecallers' casts and drop Stoneclaw Totem if a second dragonkin joins. Stay away from the big Onyxia's Lair cave entrance.", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=41.2, y=66.7, path={{38.2,65.7}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1261}, names={"Marg Speaks"}, text="Back in Brackenwall: Nazeer Bloodpike", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.2, y=30.7},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1262}, names={"Report to Zor"}, text="Nazeer Bloodpike. Keep it for Zor Lonetree in Orgrimmar (next segment).", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=35.2, y=30.7},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1168}, names={"Army of the Black Dragon"}, text="Tharg", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=37.4, y=31.4},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1169}, names={"Identifying the Brood"}, text="Draz'Zilb", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=37.1, y=33.1},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1170}, names={"The Brood of Onyxia"}, text="Draz'Zilb", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=37.2, y=33.1},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1170}, names={"The Brood of Onyxia"}, text="Overlord Mok'Morokk", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.3, y=31.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1171}, names={"The Brood of Onyxia"}, text="Overlord Mok'Morokk", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=36.3, y=31.4},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1171}, names={"The Brood of Onyxia"}, text="Draz'Zilb. Skip the next part, The Brood of Onyxia (elite).", zone="Dustwallow Marsh", map=1445, x=37.2, y=33.1},
  {t="H", seg=16, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Hearthstone, or Astral Recall if it is on cooldown"},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1187}, names={"Razzeric's Tweaking"}, text="Ride north to the Mirage Raceway: Razzeric", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.3, y=76.1},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1188}, names={"Safety First"}, text="Razzeric", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.3, y=76.1},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1188}, names={"Safety First"}, text="Ride back to Gadgetzan: Shreev at the Gizmorium", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.0, y=27.2},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1189}, names={"Safety First"}, text="Shreev", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.0, y=27.2},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1189}, names={"Safety First"}, text="One more short ride north to Razzeric at the Raceway, then back to Gadgetzan", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=80.3, y=76.1},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={2770}, names={"Gahz'rilla"}, text="Wizzle Brassbolts at the Mirage Raceway. Gahz'rilla is summoned with the Mallet of Zul'Farrak, which takes its own trip to the Hinterlands; skip this one if your group does not have the mallet.", zone="Thousand Needles", map=1441, x=78.1, y=77.1, dg=13},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1690}, names={"Wastewander Justice"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle in Gadgetzan", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1707}, names={"Water Pouch Bounty"}, text="Spigot Operator Luglunket, next to Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.4},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={2781}, names={"WANTED: Caliph Scorpidsting"}, text="The Wanted poster in Gadgetzan", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.8, y=27.0},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={1690,1707,379}, names={"Wastewander Justice","Water Pouch Bounty","Slake That Thirst"}, text="The Wastewander Bandits and Thieves (40-42) camp east of Gadgetzan (around 59-65, 23-33). Any Wastewander can drop a Water Pouch; you need 10 in all (5 for each quest). Pull them one or two at a time; Stoneclaw Totem soaks the second one.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=62.5, y=29.0},
  {t="L", seg=16, lvl=41, text="Quest XP runs short in this segment, so most of the grinding happens in these two camps. Keep clearing the Bandits and Thieves here until level 41, then ride back to Gadgetzan for the hand-ins before the harder south camp. Loot every kill: the OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon (it starts a quest later in this segment) is a rare drop from almost any Tanaris mob, Wastewanders included, and the coin helps if you still owe the wolf.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=62.5, y=29.0},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1690}, names={"Wastewander Justice"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={1691}, names={"More Wastewander Justice"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1707}, names={"Water Pouch Bounty"}, text="Spigot Operator Luglunket", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.4},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={379}, names={"Slake That Thirst"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle. He gives you the Model 4711-FTZ Power Source. Do NOT right-click it yet: it starts a two-hour timer, so you use it after the level 43 grind.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={1691}, names={"More Wastewander Justice"}, text="The second Wastewander camp is south of the first (around 59-66, 33-41): Shadow Mages (41-43), Rogues (43-44) and Assassins (44-45). Earth Shock the Shadow Mages' casts. Leave Caliph Scorpidsting (46), in the middle of the camp, for after the grind.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=61.8, y=37.5},
  {t="L", seg=16, lvl=43, text="The long grind of this segment: keep killing the Shadow Mages, Rogues and Assassins in the south camp until level 43. Marvon's quest and the OOX robot later on both need 43. The camp respawns quickly, so work in a loop, keep looting for the beacon and top up with Healing Wave between pulls.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=61.8, y=37.0},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={2781}, names={"WANTED: Caliph Scorpidsting"}, text="Now kill Caliph Scorpidsting (46) in the middle of the camp and take his head: clear his guards first, then fight him at full health and mana with Stoneskin Totem down. Drop Stoneclaw Totem if a guard respawns into the fight.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=61.8, y=38.2},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={654}, names={"Tanaris Field Sampling"}, text="Now right-click the power source at the west edge of the camp. From here you have two hours to collect the samples and hand the kit in, so go straight on.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=58.5, y=35.0},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={654}, names={"Tanaris Field Sampling"}, text="Keep the Field Testing Kit in your bags. On the ride back west to Gadgetzan, kill Glasshide Basilisks, Starving Blisterpaws (the hyenas here) and Scorpid Hunters or Tail Lashers; all three roam the flats between the camp and town (about 48-60, 25-40). Loot each one for its sample. Not every sample passes the kit's test, so expect more than 8 kills of each.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=55.0, y=33.0},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1691,2781}, names={"More Wastewander Justice","WANTED: Caliph Scorpidsting"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={654}, names={"Tanaris Field Sampling"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={864}, names={"Return to Apothecary Zinge"}, text="Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle. Keep it for Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity (a later segment).", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.5, y=28.5},
  {t="FLY", seg=16, arg="Thunder Bluff", text="Bulkrek Ragefist, the Gadgetzan wind rider master"},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={1205}, names={"Deadmire"}, text="Melor Stonehoof on Hunter Rise", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=61.5, y=80.9},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=16, text="Shaman trainers in the Pools of Vision under Spirit Rise, beside Apothecary Zamah: learn your level 42 spells", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=22.8, y=21.1},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Cast Astral Recall (back to Gadgetzan)", text="Or use the hearthstone. If both are on cooldown, fly back to Gadgetzan."},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={992}, names={"Gadgetzan Water Survey"}, text="Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={992}, names={"Gadgetzan Water Survey"}, text="Ride west to Sandsorrow Watch. Use the Untapped Dowsing Widget beside the small pool just south of the Sandfury troll huts. The Sandfury trolls are elite (42-44) and stand just east and north-east of the pool, with two rare elites further north. Swing round and come in from the south-west, use the widget at the pool's west edge and leave at once.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=39.0, y=29.3},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={992}, names={"Gadgetzan Water Survey"}, text="Back in Gadgetzan: Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={82}, names={"Noxious Lair Investigation"}, text="Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={82}, names={"Noxious Lair Investigation"}, text="The Noxious Lair is south-west of Gadgetzan (around 33, 44). The bugs are level 47-50, well above you: pull single Tunnelers and Workers from the outer edge (they drop the parts about half the time; Wasps rarely), keep Stoneskin Totem down and Healing Wave between pulls. Do not go deep inside.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=33.5, y=44.5, path={{48.2,25.9},{44.0,29.5},{44.0,35.2},{36.8,48.1},{35.2,47.8}}},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={3161}, names={"Gahz'ridian"}, text="Ride east to Marvon Rivetseeker, who camps by the Broken Pillar in central Tanaris (52.7, 45.9). This one needs level 43.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.7, y=45.9},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={3161}, names={"Gahz'ridian"}, text="Put on the Gahz'ridian Detector (head slot) and ride through the desert south-west of Marvon (around 40-48, 60-72); it shows the buried Gahz'ridian mounds. Click a mound to dig up the ornaments. This area is above your level: basilisks, scorpids, hyenas and rocs of 45-49, and Dunemaul ogres (45-48) in small groups among the mounds, with their compound at the north-west end (around 41, 57). Ride from mound to mound without stopping for fights, dig and move on, and keep Stoneclaw Totem ready for an add. Swap your own helm back on afterwards.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=45.4, y=68.5, path={{52.8,51.6},{51.6,53.4},{52.2,59.4},{49.2,63.0},{48.8,67.8}}},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={3161}, names={"Gahz'ridian"}, text="Marvon Rivetseeker", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.7, y=45.9, path={{48.8,67.8},{49.2,63.0},{52.2,59.4},{51.6,53.4},{52.8,51.6}}},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={351}, names={"Find OOX-17/TN!"}, text="Right-click the OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon. Almost every Tanaris mob can drop it, but rarely (about 1 kill in 100 or fewer), so after the long Wastewander grind and the sample kills you most likely have it already. No beacon yet? Kill the Blisterpaw Hyenas, Glasshide Gazers, Scorpid Tail Lashers and Fire Rocs (43-46) on the ride south-east from Marvon for a while. Still nothing after a fair try? Press Skip on this step and the next three: the next segment's Tanaris block passes the robot again if the beacon drops later.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=60.2, y=64.7},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={351}, names={"Find OOX-17/TN!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-17/TN, at the edge of the Gaping Chasm (60.2, 64.7)", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=60.2, y=64.7},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={648}, names={"Rescue OOX-17/TN!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-17/TN", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=60.2, y=64.7},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={648}, names={"Rescue OOX-17/TN!"}, text="Escort the robot north to Steamwheedle Port. Ambushers come out of the sand in small groups (Wastewander Scofflaws 45, Scorpid Duneburrowers 46-47): drop Stoneclaw Totem to pull them off the robot, Earth Shock and kill them fast, and save your Healing Waves for yourself. If the robot dies, abandon the failed quest, wait for the robot to reappear at the Gaping Chasm and take the quest from it again.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.0, y=24.0, path={{60.0,59.4},{54.8,51.6},{54.8,45.4},{57.2,41.5},{58.4,41.5},{59.6,37.9},{64.6,31.0},{64.6,26.8}}},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={2872}, names={"Stoley's Debt"}, text="Stoley in Steamwheedle Port", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=24.0},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={2873}, names={"Stoley's Shipment"}, text="Stoley", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=24.0},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={2875}, names={"WANTED: Andre Firebeard"}, text="The Wanted poster in Steamwheedle Port", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=66.8, y=22.3},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={8366}, names={"Southsea Shakedown"}, text="Security Chief Bilgewhizzle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=23.9},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={8365}, names={"Pirate Hats Ahoy!"}, text="Haughty Modiste", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=66.6, y=22.3},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={3520}, names={"Screecher Spirits"}, text="Yeh'kinya, beside the Haughty Modiste. Keep it for the next segment: the vale screechers live in Feral Scar Vale in Feralas.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.0, y=22.4},
  {t="C", seg=16, q={2873,2875,8365,8366}, names={"Stoley's Shipment","WANTED: Andre Firebeard","Pirate Hats Ahoy!","Southsea Shakedown"}, text="Lost Rigger Cove, the walled pirate town south down the coast. Stoley's Shipment is the Stolen Cargo near the docks (72.2, 46.8); Andre Firebeard (45) stands at 73.4, 47.1. Every Southsea pirate (44-45) can drop a hat, but only about 1 kill in 10 does, so you stay well past the 40 Shakedown kills (good XP). Pull small groups from the edge of the walls: Stoneclaw Totem for the second pirate, Earthbind Totem for runners. Open every Pirate's Footlocker the pirates drop: if one holds a Ship Schedule, right-click it to start Ship Schedules and hand it to the Security Chief along with the others.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=73.5, y=46.5, path={{65.0,22.9},{65.0,39.7},{69.8,47.2}}},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={2873}, names={"Stoley's Shipment"}, text="Stoley", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=24.0, path={{69.8,47.2},{65.0,39.7},{64.6,26.8}}},
  {t="A", seg=16, q={2874}, names={"Deliver to MacKinley"}, text="Stoley. Keep it for \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley in Booty Bay (a later segment).", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=24.0},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={2875,8366}, names={"WANTED: Andre Firebeard","Southsea Shakedown"}, text="Security Chief Bilgewhizzle (and Ship Schedules, if you found one)", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.1, y=23.9},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={8365}, names={"Pirate Hats Ahoy!"}, text="Haughty Modiste", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=66.6, y=22.3},
  {t="T", seg=16, q={82}, names={"Noxious Lair Investigation"}, text="Ride back west along the road to Gadgetzan (or use the hearthstone or Astral Recall): Alchemist Pestlezugg", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.9, y=27.0, path={{65.0,22.9},{65.0,26.2},{63.8,28.0},{60.0,30.7},{58.8,30.7},{54.4,24.7},{51.2,24.7}}},
  {t="N", seg=16, arg="Keep these for later segments: 864 Return to Apothecary Zinge (Undercity), 648 Rescue OOX-17/TN and 2874 Deliver to MacKinley (Booty Bay), 1262 Report to Zor (Orgrimmar), 3520 Screecher Spirits (Feralas), 2981 A Threat in Feralas (Camp Mojache), plus 712, 584, 598 and 698 for the Eastern Kingdoms", text="Your hearthstone stays set to Gadgetzan. The next segment starts here with the flight to Freewind Post."},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2741}, names={"The Super Egg-O-Matic"}, text="You start in Gadgetzan. Before you fly, click the Super Egg-O-Matic machine next to Andi Lynn, a few steps south-east of the wind rider master, and take its quest. Its Hippogryph Egg lies in nests in southern Feralas, and the nests can only be looted while this quest is in your log.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.4, y=27.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=17, arg="Freewind Post", text="Take the wind rider to Freewind Post in Thousand Needles."},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="Ride west out of Freewind Post on the road into Feralas; it leads to Camp Mojache", text="About 5 minutes on your wolf. The camp sits on the hills in eastern Feralas."},
  {t="F", seg=17, arg="Camp Mojache", text="Shyn, the wind rider master", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.4, y=44.3},
  {t="S", seg=17, arg="Camp Mojache", text="Innkeeper Greul. You hearth back here from Orgrimmar later in this segment."},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2862}, names={"War on the Woodpaw"}, text="Hadoken Swiftstrider", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.9, y=42.5},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2822}, names={"The Mark of Quality"}, text="Jangdor Swiftstrider", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.4, y=42.9},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2973}, names={"A New Cloak's Sheen"}, text="Krueg Skullsplitter", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.9, y=42.7},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2981}, names={"A Threat in Feralas"}, text="Rok Orhan", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.8, y=43.6},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2975}, names={"The Ogres of Feralas"}, text="Rok Orhan", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.8, y=43.6},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2987}, names={"Gordunni Cobalt"}, text="Orwin Gizzmick", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.7, y=44.3},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={3121}, names={"A Strange Request"}, text="Witch Doctor Uzer'i. You hand the shrunken head in at Orgrimmar later in this segment.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.4, y=43.4},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="Keep any OOX-22/FE Distress Beacon that drops in Feralas", text="Almost every Feralas mob can drop it. It starts Find OOX-22/FE!, which you do on your second Feralas loop."},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2862,2973}, names={"War on the Woodpaw","A New Cloak's Sheen"}, text="The hills just west and south-west of Camp Mojache. Woodpaw Mongrels, Trappers and Brutes drop the manes; Sprite Darters flit over the same slopes and drop the wings.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=70.0, y=47.0},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2975,2987}, names={"The Ogres of Feralas","Gordunni Cobalt"}, text="Ride north to the Gordunni Outpost. Kill Gordunni Ogres, Ogre Mages and Brutes; click the Gordunni Dirt Mounds around the huts for the cobalt. Earth Shock the Ogre Mages when they start a cast, and drop Stoneclaw Totem when a second ogre joins.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=76.5, y=31.0, path={{71.0,40.0},{72.8,37.3},{75.7,37.3},{77.1,35.2},{77.3,32.2}}},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2978}, names={"The Gordunni Scroll"}, text="A Gordunni Scroll lies on the ground in the outpost (also at 75.1, 29.7 and 80.5, 34.3). Pick it up and read it.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.5, y=27.9},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2862}, names={"War on the Woodpaw"}, text="Back in Camp Mojache: Hadoken Swiftstrider. Leave his next quest, Alpha Strike, for now: it has a one-hour timer, so you take it after the horns.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.9, y=42.5},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2973}, names={"A New Cloak's Sheen"}, text="Krueg Skullsplitter", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.9, y=42.7},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2974}, names={"A Grim Discovery"}, text="Krueg Skullsplitter", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.9, y=42.7},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2975,2978}, names={"The Ogres of Feralas","The Gordunni Scroll"}, text="Rok Orhan", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.8, y=43.6},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2980,2979}, names={"The Ogres of Feralas","Dark Ceremony"}, text="Rok Orhan", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.8, y=43.6},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2987}, names={"Gordunni Cobalt"}, text="Orwin Gizzmick", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.7, y=44.3},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2974}, names={"A Grim Discovery"}, text="The Grimtotem Compound in the hills just west of the camp: Grimtotem Raiders, Naturalists and Shamans drop the horns. Interrupt the Shamans' heals with Earth Shock.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=68.0, y=42.0},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2974}, names={"A Grim Discovery"}, text="Back in Camp Mojache, a short ride east: Krueg Skullsplitter", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.9, y=42.7},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2976}, names={"A Grim Discovery"}, text="Krueg Skullsplitter. He gives you a crate of horns for Belgrom Rockmaul; you hand it in on the Orgrimmar stop below.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.9, y=42.7},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2863}, names={"Alpha Strike"}, text="Hadoken Swiftstrider. The one-hour timer starts now: ride straight south to the Woodpaw camps.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.9, y=42.5},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2863}, names={"Alpha Strike"}, text="The big Woodpaw camps south of Camp Mojache. Woodpaw Alphas walk among the Mystics and Reavers: pull from the edge, Stoneclaw Totem for the extra gnoll, Healing Wave between pulls.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=70.4, y=54.7, path={{72.4,43.3},{72.4,46.0},{70.4,50.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2863}, names={"Alpha Strike"}, text="Back in Camp Mojache: Hadoken Swiftstrider", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.9, y=42.5, path={{70.4,48.1},{72.8,42.7}}},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2902}, names={"Woodpaw Investigation"}, text="Hadoken Swiftstrider", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.9, y=42.5},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2902}, names={"Woodpaw Investigation"}, text="The Woodpaw Battle Map lies in the gnoll camp at 71.6, 55.9", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=71.6, y=55.9, path={{72.4,43.3},{72.4,46.0},{70.6,49.9},{70.6,54.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2903}, names={"The Battle Plans"}, text="From the same map", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=71.6, y=55.9},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2980,2979}, names={"The Ogres of Feralas","Dark Ceremony"}, text="Ride south-west to the Ruins of Isildien. Gordunni Maulers stand at the north edge; Shaman and Warlocks fill the ruins. The Gordunni Orb drops from the Gordunni Mage-Lords (45-46) in the southern part (around 60, 70). Most of them are casters: Earth Shock the cast, and pull them out of sight of the next group.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=60.5, y=66.0, path={{70.6,62.4},{68.2,68.1},{64.8,69.0},{62.4,65.4}}},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2741}, names={"The Super Egg-O-Matic"}, text="A short ride south of the ruins: take a Hippogryph Egg from one of the nests at the south end of the Frayfeather Highlands. Frayfeather Patriarchs (46-47) and Skystormers (45-46) walk around the nests: pull them away one at a time, with Stoneclaw Totem down. The egg goes into the machine in Gadgetzan at the end of this segment.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=57.3, y=77.4},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={3520}, names={"Screecher Spirits"}, text="Screecher Spirits, on the way north-west: Vale Screechers walk the slopes between the ruins and Feral Scar Vale (57-60, 55-62), and Rogue Vale Screechers roam around the vale and north of it (48-56, 47-59). Kill one, use Yeh'kinya's Bramble on the corpse, then click the spirit that appears. You need three.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=57.5, y=57.0},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2822}, names={"The Mark of Quality"}, text="Ride west to Feral Scar Vale. Feral Scar Yetis and their Enraged and Hulking kin drop the Thick Yeti Hides.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.5, y=57.0},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2903}, names={"The Battle Plans"}, text="Back in Camp Mojache: Hadoken Swiftstrider", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.9, y=42.5},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={7730,7731}, names={"Zukk'ash Infestation","Stinglasher"}, text="Hadoken Swiftstrider", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.9, y=42.5},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2980,2979}, names={"The Ogres of Feralas","Dark Ceremony"}, text="Rok Orhan", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.8, y=43.6},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={3002}, names={"The Gordunni Orb"}, text="Rok Orhan. The orb goes to Uthel'nay in Orgrimmar, on the Orgrimmar stop below.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.8, y=43.6},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2822}, names={"The Mark of Quality"}, text="Jangdor Swiftstrider. Leave his next quest, Improved Quality, until you are back from Orgrimmar.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.4, y=42.9},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={7730,7731}, names={"Zukk'ash Infestation","Stinglasher"}, text="The Writhing Deep, the silithid hive south of the Woodpaw camps. Every Zukk'ash bug drops carapaces. Stinglasher (47) is a big wasp that flies around the east side of the hive (around 77, 62): fight it alone, with Stoneclaw Totem down and Healing Wave ready.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.5, y=63.0, path={{72.4,43.6},{72.4,46.0},{70.6,49.9},{70.6,54.3}}},
  {t="L", seg=17, lvl=45, text="Quest XP runs short here. Keep killing Zukk'ash Workers, Wasps and Tunnelers in the hive until level 45. The next Feralas loop and Tanaris have level 47-50 mobs.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=75.5, y=63.0},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={7730,7731}, names={"Zukk'ash Infestation","Stinglasher"}, text="Hadoken Swiftstrider", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.9, y=42.5, path={{74.4,58.8},{74.4,52.8},{71.4,49.9},{72.4,43.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={7732}, names={"Zukk'ash Report"}, text="Hadoken Swiftstrider. The report goes to Zilzibin Drumlore in Orgrimmar, on the stop below.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.9, y=42.5},
  {t="FLY", seg=17, arg="Orgrimmar", text="Shyn, the Camp Mojache wind rider master. Your hearthstone stays set to Camp Mojache."},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={3121}, names={"A Strange Request"}, text="Neeru Fireblade in the Cleft of Shadow, the dark tunnel off the Valley of Strength", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=49.5, y=50.6},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={3122}, names={"Return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i"}, text="Neeru Fireblade", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=49.5, y=50.6},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={7732}, names={"Zukk'ash Report"}, text="Zilzibin Drumlore in the Drag (56.3, 46.7)", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=56.3, y=46.7},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={649}, names={"Ripple Recovery"}, text="Dran Droffers, further north in the Drag", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=59.6, y=36.5},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2283}, names={"Necklace Recovery"}, text="Dran Droffers in the Drag. The necklace is in a chest in the dig site before the dungeon portal. Needs level 37.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=59.5, y=36.6, dg=12},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={649}, names={"Ripple Recovery"}, text="Malton Droffers, right next to him", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=59.8, y=36.9},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={650}, names={"Ripple Recovery"}, text="Malton Droffers. You hand it in to Gilveradin Sunchaser in the Hinterlands (segment 19).", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=59.8, y=36.9},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2976}, names={"A Grim Discovery"}, text="Belgrom Rockmaul in the Valley of Honor. He also offers Betrayed: leave it.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=75.2, y=34.2},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="No wolf yet? Learn Wolf Riding from Kildar and buy a wolf from Ogunaro Wolfrunner next to him", text="North end of the Valley of Honor. Skip this if you bought them at 40.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=69.4, y=13.1},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1262}, names={"Report to Zor"}, text="Zor Lonetree in the Valley of Wisdom", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=38.9, y=38.4},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={7541}, names={"Service to the Horde"}, text="Zor Lonetree then offers Service to the Horde: it has no objectives", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=38.9, y=38.4},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={7541}, names={"Service to the Horde"}, text="Zor Lonetree. Pick either ring", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=38.9, y=38.4},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=17, text="Valley of Wisdom shaman trainers: learn your level 44 spells. Your level 46 ranks wait for Haromm in Stonard (next segment).", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=38.8, y=36.4},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={3002}, names={"The Gordunni Orb"}, text="Uthel'nay in the Darkbriar Lodge, Valley of Spirits (39.2, 86.3)", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=39.2, y=86.3},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={7068}, names={"Shadowshard Fragments"}, text="Uthel'nay in the Valley of Spirits. Shadowshard Fragments drop from the rumblers on the purple side, before the dungeon portal.", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=39.2, y=86.3, dg=14},
  {t="H", seg=17, arg="Camp Mojache"},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={3122}, names={"Return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i"}, text="Witch Doctor Uzer'i", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.4, y=43.4},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="Optional: Uzer'i now offers Testing the Vessel", text="Take it only if you plan the Camp Mojache detour in segment 20: its wildkin are in the Hinterlands (segment 19) and the rest of his chain waits until then. Skip it if your quest log is nearly full."},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={3063}, names={"Vengeance on the Northspring"}, text="Talo Thornhoof. Skip Dark Heart (elite) and The Strength of Corruption (Felwood).", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=76.2, y=43.8},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={7734}, names={"Improved Quality"}, text="Jangdor Swiftstrider", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.4, y=42.9},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2766}, names={"Find OOX-22/FE!"}, text="Ride west. Right-click the OOX-22/FE Distress Beacon: the robot is in a small cave at the edge of Feral Scar Vale. No beacon yet? Kill the Feral Scar yetis around the cave and the Vale Screechers on the slopes east of it until one drops: this robot pair and An OOX of Your Own (segment 19) are worth about 16,000 XP together.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.4, y=55.7, path={{53.0,56.1}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2766}, names={"Find OOX-22/FE!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-22/FE", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.4, y=55.7},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2767}, names={"Rescue OOX-22/FE!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-22/FE", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.4, y=55.7},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2767}, names={"Rescue OOX-22/FE!"}, text="Escort the robot west to the dock on the Forgotten Coast. Ambushers jump it on the way: Stoneclaw Totem pulls them off the robot, then kill them fast.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=45.0, y=43.0, path={{54.0,54.3},{53.0,52.8},{53.0,48.7},{49.6,42.1},{46.6,41.5}}},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={7003,7721}, names={"Zapped Giants","Fuel for the Zapping"}, text="Zorbin Fandazzle at the dock (44.8, 43.4)", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=44.8, y=43.4},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={7003,7721}, names={"Zapped Giants","Fuel for the Zapping"}, text="Along the coast: Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays drop the cores. Zap the Shore, Wave and Deep Striders (elite giants) with Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker first, then kill the small zapped giants for the residue. Never fight a giant that is not zapped.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=42.5, y=49.0},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={7003,7721}, names={"Zapped Giants","Fuel for the Zapping"}, text="Zorbin Fandazzle. Skip his repeat versions.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=44.8, y=43.4},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={3063}, names={"Vengeance on the Northspring"}, text="Ride north up the coast to the Northspring harpy nests. Kill 4 of each kind (48-50). Windcallers cast: Earth Shock them. Slayers hit hard: pull one at a time and heal between pulls. At 45 they are 3-5 levels above you: if one fight costs most of your health and mana, abandon Vengeance on the Northspring and skip its hand-in at Talo.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=39.5, y=13.5, path={{46.0,42.4},{46.0,35.2},{43.4,28.0},{43.4,24.4}}},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={7734}, names={"Improved Quality"}, text="Ride east to Rage Scar Hold. Rage Scar Yetis drop the hides. If a Perfect Yeti Hide drops, right-click it and hand it to Jangdor too.", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=53.5, y=31.5, path={{47.4,13.6},{50.8,18.4},{50.8,21.4},{52.8,24.7}}},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="Cast Astral Recall (back to Camp Mojache)", text="Or use your hearthstone if Astral Recall is on cooldown."},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={3063}, names={"Vengeance on the Northspring"}, text="Talo Thornhoof", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=76.2, y=43.8},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={7734}, names={"Improved Quality"}, text="Jangdor Swiftstrider", zone="Feralas", map=1444, x=74.4, y=42.9},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="Optional dungeon: Maraudon, levels 46-55", text="Maraudon is in the west of Desolace, north of Shadowprey Village (fly there from Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff or Camp Mojache). Inside the outer caves, before the portals, Cavindra gives Legends of Maraudon. Quests you picked up for it: Shadowshard Fragments. Not on your path, only if you want the detour: Vyletongue Corruption (Desolace 23, 70); Corruption of Earth and Seed (Desolace 27, 78); Twisted Evils (Desolace 62, 40); The Pariah's Instructions (Desolace 50, 87).", zone="Desolace", map=1443, x=29.1, y=62.5, dg=14, run=true},
  {t="FLY", seg=17, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Shyn, the wind rider master"},
  {t="S", seg=17, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Innkeeper Fizzgrimble. Your hearthstone stays here into the next segment."},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={2741}, names={"The Super Egg-O-Matic"}, text="Put the Hippogryph Egg in the Super Egg-O-Matic, next to Andi Lynn, a few steps from the wind rider master: do it now, before you ride out again", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.4, y=27.0},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={10}, names={"The Scrimshank Redemption"}, text="Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={5863}, names={"The Dunemaul Compound"}, text="Andi Lynn", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=52.8, y=27.4},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={2605}, names={"The Thirsty Goblin"}, text="Marin Noggenfogger", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.8, y=28.7},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={3362}, names={"Thistleshrub Valley"}, text="Tran'rek", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=26.8},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={10}, names={"The Scrimshank Redemption"}, text="Ride south to the Gaping Chasm. Scrimshank's Surveying Gear lies inside the silithid hive; clear the bugs at the entrance as you go in.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=56.0, y=71.2},
  {t="N", seg=17, arg="No OOX-17/TN robot in the last segment? If its Distress Beacon has dropped since, do the robot now", text="It sits at the edge of the Gaping Chasm, a short ride north-east of Scrimshank's gear. Right-click the beacon, hand it to the robot, take Rescue OOX-17/TN! and escort it north to Steamwheedle Port: stay off your mount and out of Ghost Wolf, and drop Stoneclaw Totem when ambushers jump it. Then ride back south-west to the Dunemaul Compound. Still no beacon? Skip it: Oglethorpe's hand-in for it in Booty Bay (next segment) then drops out too.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=60.2, y=64.7},
  {t="L", seg=17, lvl=46, text="Ride west to the Dunemaul Compound. Thistleshrub Valley and the Tooga escort after it are level 48-50, so kill Dunemaul Brutes and Enforcers (46-48) here until level 46; they count for The Dunemaul Compound. The ogres stand in twos and threes: Stoneclaw Totem for the second one, Earth Shock the Ogre Mages and Warlocks, Healing Wave between pulls.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=40.0, y=54.0, path={{60.0,60.0},{58.6,57.9},{53.2,57.6},{49.2,52.2},{42.4,52.2}}},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={5863}, names={"The Dunemaul Compound"}, text="Finish the 10 Dunemaul Brutes and 10 Enforcers, then kill Gor'marok the Ravager (49), who stands near the south-east side of the compound. Clear the ogres around him first and fight him on his own, with Stoneclaw Totem down.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=41.5, y=57.8},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={2605,3362}, names={"The Thirsty Goblin","Thistleshrub Valley"}, text="Thistleshrub Valley, the cactus garden south-west of the compound. Thistleshrub Dew Collectors drop the gland; Gnarled Thistleshrubs and Rootshapers (48-50) are the kill targets. Pull them one at a time.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=29.3, y=65.5, path={{41.4,60.3},{34.0,69.6},{32.0,69.3}}},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={1560}, names={"Tooga's Quest"}, text="Tooga the turtle sits at the south end of the valley (31.8, 74.1). Accept it only when the rest of the valley is done.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=31.8, y=74.1},
  {t="C", seg=17, q={1560}, names={"Tooga's Quest"}, text="30-minute timer: go straight to Torta, with no detours and no extra pulls. Lead Tooga north-east across the desert to his wife Torta, just south of Steamwheedle Port. He follows you: stay out of Ghost Wolf and off your mount, keep him close, kill anything that attacks him and heal him with Healing Wave if he gets low.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=66.6, y=25.7, path={{38.0,65.7},{39.8,65.7},{40.8,67.2},{48.8,67.8},{49.2,63.0},{55.2,56.1},{54.8,45.4},{57.2,41.5},{59.0,40.6},{59.6,37.9},{64.6,31.0},{64.6,26.8}}},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={1560}, names={"Tooga's Quest"}, text="Torta", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=66.6, y=25.7},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={3520}, names={"Screecher Spirits"}, text="Yeh'kinya in Steamwheedle Port, just north of Torta. Skip his next quest, The Prophecy of Mosh'aru: it needs Zul'Farrak.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.0, y=22.4},
  {t="A", seg=17, q={3527}, names={"The Prophecy of Mosh'aru"}, text="Yeh'kinya in Steamwheedle Port, after Screecher Spirits. The two tablets drop from Theka the Martyr and Hydromancer Velratha.", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=67.0, y=22.4, dg=13},
  {t="T", seg=17, q={10}, names={"The Scrimshank Redemption"}, text="Back in Gadgetzan (ride west along the road): Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.2, y=27.5},
