  {t="A", seg=18, q={587}, names={"Up to Snuff"}, text="Deeg", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.3},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={576}, names={"Keep An Eye Out"}, text="Dizzy One-Eye", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.6, y=75.9},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={604,587}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers","Up to Snuff"}, text="The Bloodsail camp on the shore just south of Booty Bay: kill 10 Swashbucklers and pick up the Bloodsail Charts and Orders lying in the camp. Snuff drops from any Bloodsail pirate. Dizzy's Eye (576) drops only rarely from any Bloodsail, including the ship crews you fight later, so loot everything. One group at a time; Earth Shock the Warlocks' Shadow Bolts", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=29.0, y=82.4},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={604}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="Fleet Master Seahorn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={608}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="Keep it for the end of the jungle loop", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={587}, names={"Up to Snuff"}, text="Deeg", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=26.9, y=77.3},
  {t="FLY", seg=18, arg="Grom'gol", text="Gringer, Booty Bay's wind rider master"},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={572}, names={"Mok'thardin's Enchantment"}, text="Far Seer Mok'thardin. The Jungle Stalkers for it come later in this segment", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.1, y=29.2},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={584}, names={"Bloodscalp Clan Heads"}, text="584 is already in your log. Ride north-west to the Ruins of Zul'Kunda: Gan'zulah (41) and Nezzliok the Dire (40) stand inside the ruins among Bloodscalp trolls. Clear around each one first, then kill them for their heads", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=23.5, y=8.8, path={{34.2,29.2},{35.8,26.5},{35.8,23.8},{32.0,20.8},{32.0,18.7},{28.2,13.6},{27.4,9.1}}},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={196}, names={"Raptor Mastery"}, text="Hemet Nesingwary, a short ride east of Zul'Kunda at the hunters' camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={584}, names={"Bloodscalp Clan Heads"}, text="Back south to Grom'gol: the Bubbling Cauldron in the middle of the camp", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.6},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={585,586}, names={"Speaking with Nezzliok","Speaking with Gan'zulah"}, text="Both come from the cauldron", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.6},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={585}, names={"Speaking with Nezzliok"}, text="Ride east to the Skullsplitter ruins and click the trophy skull piles at Ziata'jai (42, 36), Balia'mah (46, 32) and Zul'Mamwe (48, 40)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=44.2, y=34.2},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={586,209,598}, names={"Speaking with Gan'zulah","Skullsplitter Tusks","Split Bone Necklace"}, text="Skullsplitter Hunters, Headhunters and Berserkers (41-44) hold Zul'Mamwe, the south-east ruin; Ana'thek the Cruel (45) walks there and drops the armour. Tusks and necklaces drop from every Skullsplitter, but slowly: the Warriors, Axe Throwers and Mystics (39-40) in the other two ruins die fastest. Earth Shock the Witch Doctors' and Mystics' heals", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=46.4, y=43.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={585,586}, names={"Speaking with Nezzliok","Speaking with Gan'zulah"}, text="Ride back west to Grom'gol: the Bubbling Cauldron", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.6},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={588}, names={"The Fate of Yenniku"}, text="The cauldron again", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.2, y=27.6},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={598,588}, names={"Split Bone Necklace","The Fate of Yenniku"}, text="Kin'weelay", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.3, y=27.7},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={589}, names={"The Singing Crystals"}, zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.3, y=27.7},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={600,589}, names={"Venture Company Mining","The Singing Crystals"}, text="Ride back east, past the ruins, to the Venture Co. camp at the Crystalvein Mine. Strip Miners, Tinkerers and Surveyors (40-42) drop Singing Blue Crystals on most kills. Ironjaw Basilisks (43-44) in and around the mine, just south of the camp, drop the Pulsing Blue Shards", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=42.5, y=45.5},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={621,609}, names={"Zanzil's Secret","Voodoo Dues"}, text="Ride south-west to Zanzil's camp (37-40, 52-59). His trolls, zombies and naga (43-44) drop Zanzil's Mixture on about 1 in 3 kills, and Chucky \"Ten Thumbs\" (43, at 40, 58) has the ring: Zanzil himself (46) stands beside him, so pull Chucky away first. Maury \"Club Foot\" Wilkins and Jon-Jon the Crow (43-44) stand together at the ruins on the north-west edge (35, 51): kill both. Earth Shock the Witch Doctors", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=39.4, y=57.7},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={572,196}, names={"Mok'thardin's Enchantment","Raptor Mastery"}, text="Jungle Stalkers (40-41), the raptors in the jungle west of Maury's ruins toward the coast. Kill 10 for Hemet; about 1 in 4 drops a feather for Mok'thardin, so keep going until you have 10. They come in pairs: Stoneclaw Totem holds the second one", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.5, y=46.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={589}, names={"The Singing Crystals"}, text="Ride north to Grom'gol: Kin'weelay. Skip the next part (The Mind's Eye, elite)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.3, y=27.7, path={{33.8,38.5},{34.4,28.3}}},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={572}, names={"Mok'thardin's Enchantment"}, text="Far Seer Mok'thardin. Skip his next quest (571): its Aged Gorilla Sinew is a rare drop", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=32.1, y=29.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={196}, names={"Raptor Mastery"}, text="Ride north to Hemet Nesingwary. Skip the next part (Tethis, elite)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=35.7, y=10.8},
  {t="H", seg=18, arg="Booty Bay", text="Hearthstone, or cast Astral Recall. Both on cooldown? Ride back to Grom'gol and fly"},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={609}, names={"Voodoo Dues"}, text="\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley. Skip the next part (613, elite)", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.8, y=77.1},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={600,621}, names={"Venture Company Mining","Zanzil's Secret"}, text="Crank Fizzlebub", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.1, y=77.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={209}, names={"Skullsplitter Tusks"}, text="Kebok", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.0, y=77.1},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={608,576}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers","Keep An Eye Out"}, text="The three Bloodsail ships lie at anchor off the coast south of Booty Bay. Swim out and clear the deckhands and sea dogs (43-45) near each captain one pull at a time, then kill Captain Stillwater (45-46, east ship), Captain Keelhaul (46-47, west ship) and Fleet Master Firallon (48, south ship). Still no Dizzy's Eye? Any ship crew can drop it. Stoneclaw Totem for adds, Healing Wave when low", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=30.9, y=89.0},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={624}, names={"Cortello's Riddle"}, text="Optional, before you swim back: Cortello's Riddle, a scroll lying on one of the ship decks. Loot it and right-click it. You hand it in under a bridge in the Swamp of Sorrows right after you reach Stonard; skip both steps if you did not find it", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=29.2, y=88.6},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={608}, names={"The Bloodsail Buccaneers"}, text="Fleet Master Seahorn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=27.2, y=77.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={576}, names={"Keep An Eye Out"}, text="Dizzy One-Eye, a few steps from Seahorn", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.6, y=75.9},
  {t="FLY", seg=18, arg="Stonard", text="Gringer (via Grom'gol)"},
  {t="S", seg=18, arg="Stonard", text="Innkeeper Karakul. Your hearthstone stays here into the next segment", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=45.2, y=56.7},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=18, text="Haromm in Stonard, the only shaman trainer in the Eastern Kingdoms. Learn your level 46 spells, and 48 if you have it", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=48.2, y=57.9},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={1430}, names={"Fresh Meat"}, text="Dar in Stonard", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=44.7, y=57.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={624}, names={"Cortello's Riddle"}, text="Optional: ride west along the road to the bridge at the west end of the swamp. A Soggy Scroll lies underneath it, in the water. Skip its next riddle (Dustwallow Marsh)", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=22.9, y=48.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={698}, names={"Lack of Surplus"}, text="Ride back east past Stonard to the coast, then south along the beach to Tok'Kar at Misty Reed Post. Kill every Monstrous Crawler (43-44) you pass: their legs for Fresh Meat (1430) drop only rarely", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=81.3, y=81.0, path={{22.9,52.2},{21.5,55.8},{21.9,63.0},{20.5,65.4},{20.5,72.6},{22.5,78.0},{26.4,78.0},{31.4,80.4},{33.8,80.4},{35.2,78.0},{42.4,78.0},{44.2,78.6},{48.2,84.6},{57.2,83.4},{64.8,90.3},{67.8,90.0},{71.0,85.2},{78.1,85.8}}},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={699}, names={"Lack of Surplus"}, text="Tok'Kar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=81.3, y=81.0},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={699}, names={"Lack of Surplus"}, text="Sawtooth Snappers in the shallows along the south coast, south of the camp: claws drop on most kills. Two more crawlers walk this shore. Short of snappers? More of them live along the east coast", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=78.0, y=97.5},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={699}, names={"Lack of Surplus"}, text="Tok'Kar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=81.3, y=81.0},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={1422}, names={"Threat From the Sea"}, text="Tok'Kar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=81.3, y=81.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={1422}, names={"Threat From the Sea"}, text="Katar, a few steps away", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=83.8, y=80.4},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={1426}, names={"Threat From the Sea"}, text="Katar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=83.8, y=80.4},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={1426}, names={"Threat From the Sea"}, text="The few Marsh Murlocs are on the beach just south of the camp, and Inkspewers line the whole south and east coast. Most Flesheaters are on the beach west of the camp around 63, 86, the same beach you use for Continued Threat. Pull them away from the groups; Earthbind Totem slows any that follow", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=84.4, y=88.6},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={1426}, names={"Threat From the Sea"}, text="Katar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=83.8, y=80.4},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={1427}, names={"Threat From the Sea"}, text="Katar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=83.8, y=80.4},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={1427}, names={"Threat From the Sea"}, text="Tok'Kar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=81.3, y=81.0},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={1428}, names={"Continued Threat"}, text="Katar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=83.8, y=80.4},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={1428}, names={"Continued Threat"}, text="Inkspewers, Flesheaters and Oracles further west along the southern beach. Kill the Oracles first and Earth Shock their heals", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=64.4, y=81.1},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={1428}, names={"Continued Threat"}, text="Katar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=83.8, y=80.4},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={1430}, names={"Fresh Meat"}, text="Still short of crawler legs? Ride north along the east beach: most Monstrous Crawlers walk there. If the legs still will not drop, give up on 1430 rather than camp the beach", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=93.5, y=45.0},
  {t="H", seg=18, arg="Stonard", text="Hearthstone, or cast Astral Recall"},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={1430}, names={"Fresh Meat"}, text="Dar", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=44.7, y=57.2},
  {t="FLY", seg=18, arg="Kargath", text="Breyk, Stonard's wind rider master"},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={782}, names={"Broken Alliances"}, text="Gorn in Kargath", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.9, y=45.6},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={712}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Ride south to the far south-west corner of the Badlands: Greater Rock Elementals (42-44) drop Bracers of Rock Binding on most kills. The Dustbelcher ogre camp (Camp Boff) sits between this group and a second one to the south-east, so pull from the edges and do not drift into the ogres. Kill Boss Tho'grun (next step) if he walks past", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=4.1, y=79.6, path={{0.1,45.7},{0.1,79.5},{0.9,80.7}}},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={782}, names={"Broken Alliances"}, text="Boss Tho'grun (41-42, not elite) starts at Camp Boff and walks a long loop east along the southern road and back. Catch him on the road, away from the Maulers and Shamans in the camp, and loot the Sign of the Earth", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=12.6, y=75.5},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={712}, names={"Study of the Elements: Rock"}, text="Lotwil Veriatus at his camp in western Badlands. His and Lucien Tosselwrench's other quests need Auction House parts: skip them", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={782}, names={"Broken Alliances"}, text="Gorn, back in Kargath. Skip the next part (793, elite)", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.9, y=45.6, path={{25.6,47.8},{24.5,49.6},{21.1,49.9},{16.9,56.1},{13.1,59.1},{8.5,59.1},{6.7,56.1},{5.9,51.0},{2.9,47.5}}},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={2202}, names={"Uldaman Reagent Run"}, text="Jarkal Mossmeld in Kargath, after his Badlands Reagent Run. Magenta Fungus Caps grow inside.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.4, y=46.1, dg=12},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Optional dungeon: Uldaman, levels 41-51", text="The main entrance is the dig site in the north of the Badlands; a back entrance is further east (Badlands 65.2, 43.5). Inside: the Necklace Recovery chain continues (a paladin's remains, then gems from three bosses, with trips back to Jarkal in Kargath), and the Discs of Norgannon after the last boss give The Platinum Discs. Quests you picked up for it: Necklace Recovery, Reclaimed Treasures, Power Stones, Solution to Doom, Uldaman Reagent Run. The route does not come back to these hand-ins, go when it suits you: Power Stones (Badlands); Solution to Doom (Badlands).", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=44.6, y=12.1, dg=12, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={2202}, names={"Uldaman Reagent Run"}, zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.4, y=46.1, dg=12},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Take the trail that starts just north of Kargath and climbs into Searing Gorge, then cross the gorge north-west to the Cauldron"},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={3441}, names={"Divine Retribution"}, text="Kalaran Windblade, at the north-west edge of the Cauldron", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={3441}, names={"Divine Retribution"}, text="Listen to his story", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={3442}, names={"The Flawless Flame"}, zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="F", seg=18, arg="Thorium Point", text="Grisha, the Horde wind rider master at Thorium Point, a short ride north-west", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=34.8, y=30.8},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={7728,7729}, names={"STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass","JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition"}, text="The Wanted board at Thorium Point. Skip WANTED: Overseer Maltorius (elite)", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=37.6, y=26.5},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={7723,7724,7727}, names={"Curse These Fat Fingers","Fiery Menace!","Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It"}, text="Hansel Heavyhands", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.6, y=27.8},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={7722}, names={"What the Flux?"}, text="Master Smith Burninate", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.8, y=28.5},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={3442,7723}, names={"The Flawless Flame","Curse These Fat Fingers"}, text="Heavy War Golems (47-49) walk around the Cauldron and drop Golem Oil: kill 20. Blazing, Inferno and Magma Elementals in and around the Cauldron drop Hearts of Flame (Magma Elementals can drop both). Fire spells and fire totems do little to the elementals: use Frost Shock, Earth Shock and melee", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=42.0, y=50.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={3442}, names={"The Flawless Flame"}, text="Back to Kalaran Windblade", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={3443}, names={"Forging the Shaft"}, zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={7729,3443,7728}, obj={0,0,1}, names={"JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition","Forging the Shaft","STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass"}, text="Dark Iron Taskmasters and Slavers on the Cauldron floor. Any Dark Iron dwarf can drop a Thorium Plated Dagger. The Smithing Tuyere drops from the Dark Iron Steamsmiths at the forges on the west side of the Cauldron (40, 49). Keep the Grimesilt Outhouse Key if one drops", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=43.0, y=34.9},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={7727,7722}, names={"Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It","What the Flux?"}, text="The Slag Pit is a tunnel that leads down from the Cauldron floor. Incendosaurs fill its lava pools: kill your 20 first. The Secret Plans: Fiery Flux lie on the ground at 40.5, 35.7, right beside Overseer Maltorius (elite 50) and his two elite Dark Iron Sentries (48). Do not try to clear them: come in from the side away from them, click the plans and walk straight back up the tunnel, with an Earthbind Totem behind you if one turns", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=47.6, y=25.2},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={7724}, names={"Fiery Menace!"}, text="Spiders first, on the west plateau south-west of Thorium Point: almost all Greater Lava Spiders (47-49) live there and in its lava pools, from 27, 38 south to 22-31, 66-78. Work south through them until you have killed 20. Still short? A few more roam south of the towers at 40, 69 and 44, 68", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=28.0, y=44.0},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={7728}, obj={2}, names={"STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass"}, text="Now the sentry towers south of the Cauldron, west to east (33, 54; 36, 61; 43, 63; 50-54, 56-59): Dark Iron Lookouts there drop the Lookout's Spyglass. An elite Dark Iron Sentry (48) guards each tower: pull the Lookouts away from it with Lightning Bolt (the group at 53, 59 stands furthest from its Sentry). The east tower is a short ride from the outhouse, your next stop", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=33.2, y=53.5},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4449}, names={"Caught!"}, text="Ride east from the last tower to the Wooden Outhouse at the Grimesilt Dig Site and talk to it. Leave Ledger from Tanaris alone afterwards: its items are in Dustwallow and the Swamp of Sorrows", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="C", seg=18, q={4449}, names={"Caught!"}, text="Five Dark Iron Geologists dig right next to the outhouse; the other three work at 69, 33, far to the north. Kill the five here, then wait a few minutes for them to come back rather than riding north. Dark Iron Watchmen stand among them. You also need 15 Silk Cloth", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=63.3, y=60.5},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4449}, names={"Caught!"}, text="The outhouse", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="A", seg=18, q={4451}, names={"The Key to Freedom"}, text="Right-click the Grimesilt Outhouse Key. No key yet? Any Dark Iron Taskmaster, Slaver or Lookout can drop it: the nearest stand at 58, 42, north-west of the dig site. Skip this pair if it will not drop", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={4451}, names={"The Key to Freedom"}, text="Use the key on the outhouse door", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=65.6, y=62.2},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={3443}, names={"Forging the Shaft"}, text="Ride back north-west to Kalaran Windblade. Skip The Flame's Casing (elite)", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.1, y=39.0},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={7729,7728}, names={"JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition","STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass"}, text="Taskmaster Scrange, Thorium Point", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=39.0, y=27.5},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={7723,7724,7727}, names={"Curse These Fat Fingers","Fiery Menace!","Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It"}, text="Hansel Heavyhands", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.6, y=27.8},
  {t="T", seg=18, q={7722}, names={"What the Flux?"}, text="Master Smith Burninate", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.8, y=28.5},
  {t="L", seg=18, lvl=49, text="Quest XP runs short here, so grind to 49 before the next segment. Kill the level 47-49 mobs: Greater Lava Spiders on the west plateau (27-32, 37-50), and Heavy War Golems and Dark Iron Taskmasters along the west rim of the Cauldron (34-38, 41-48). The level 45-46 Slavers give less XP. Skip the elite Dark Iron Sentries at the towers (34, 54 is the closest) and beside Maltorius", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=31.0, y=45.0},
  {t="N", seg=18, arg="Ride back to Thorium Point: the next segment starts at Grisha with a flight to the Undercity", text="Keep 864 (Undercity), 650 and 2641 (Hinterlands) and 32 (Orgrimmar). Your hearthstone is set to Stonard"},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Undercity", text="You start at Thorium Point. Grisha, the wind rider master. It is a long flight that passes through Kargath: you do not change, stay on the wind rider until it lands in the Undercity. Your hearthstone stays set to Stonard.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=34.8, y=30.8},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={864}, names={"Return to Apothecary Zinge"}, text="Apothecary Zinge in the Apothecarium", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=50.1, y=68.0},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={6522}, names={"An Unholy Alliance"}, text="An Unholy Alliance, if you found the Small Scroll.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=56.3, y=92.2, dg=11},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2995}, names={"Lines of Communication"}, text="Oran Snakewrithe in the Magic Quarter. She wants three elf documents burned at Quel'Danil Lodge in the Hinterlands.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=73.1, y=32.9},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={3341}, names={"Bring the End"}, zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=74.0, y=33.3, dg=11},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Tarren Mill", text="Michael Garrett, the bat handler by the west elevator", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=63.2, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2342}, names={"Reclaimed Treasures"}, zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=62.3, y=48.6, dg=12},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Ride east out of Tarren Mill on the road into the Hinterlands", text="Go around Aerie Peak, the Wildhammer dwarf town at the west end of the zone: its guards attack Horde on sight."},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={650}, names={"Ripple Recovery"}, text="Gilveradin Sunchaser camps just south-west of Quel'Danil Lodge (26.7, 48.6). Leave the Venom Bottles in the Witherbark village to the south: that chain needs two extra Tarren Mill trips and ends in an elite quest.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=26.7, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={77}, names={"A Sticky Situation"}, text="Gilveradin Sunchaser. Leave Quel'Danil Lodge, the elf lodge just north-east, alone for now: you clear it once Revantusk's Message to the Wildhammer is in your log.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=26.7, y=48.6},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Optional: only if you took Testing the Vessel in Feralas (segment 17)", text="Vicious and Primitive Owlbeasts roam the hills on both sides of the road east (around 35-46, 43-56). Kill 10 and use the Muisek Vessel on each corpse. Not in your log? Ignore them and ride on."},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={77}, names={"A Sticky Situation"}, text="Follow the road east to Skulk Rock. Loot the Horde Supply Crates around the old Horde camp there. Green Sludges and Jade Oozes guard them. Only six crates stand there: four more sit west of Skulk Rock at the head of the river (45.5-47.5, 38-41), next to a broken robot. Keep an OOX-09/HL Distress Beacon if one drops.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=57.0, y=41.5},
  {t="F", seg=19, arg="Revantusk Village", text="Keep following the road south-east to Revantusk Village on the coast. Gorkas, the wind rider master", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=81.7, y=81.8, path={{57.0,45.4},{59.8,49.6},{67.2,47.8},{69.4,51.0},{75.7,51.0},{79.1,55.8},{79.1,58.5},{77.9,60.3},{77.5,68.1},{75.5,72.3},{77.9,79.5}}},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7828,7829,7830}, names={"Stalking the Stalkers","Hunt the Savages","Avenging the Fallen"}, text="Huntsman Markhor", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=79.2, y=79.5},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7839}, names={"Vilebranch Hooligans"}, text="Smith Slagtree", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=77.2, y=80.1},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7840}, names={"Lard Lost His Lunch"}, text="Lard", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=78.1, y=81.4},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7841}, names={"Message to the Wildhammer"}, text="Otho Moji'ko. Skip the Revantusk elite quests (Gammerita, Separation Anxiety, Dark Vessels, Kidnapped Elder Torntusk, the Call to Arms board).", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=79.4, y=79.1},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7844}, names={"Cannibalistic Cousins"}, text="Mystic Yayo'jin", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=78.8, y=78.2},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={7815}, names={"Snapjaws, Mon!"}, text="Katoom the Angler", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=80.3, y=81.5},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7828,7829,7830}, obj={1,0,0}, names={"Stalking the Stalkers","Hunt the Savages","Avenging the Fallen"}, text="Ride north-west into the central wilds. Silvermane Stalkers, Savage Owlbeasts and the Razorbeak Skylords (one circles near 54, 49, another near 64, 52) all live here. Stalkers come out of stealth on you: drop Stoneclaw Totem if a second beast joins and Healing Wave between pulls.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=60.0, y=50.0, path={{77.9,79.5},{75.5,72.3},{77.7,66.0},{79.1,55.8},{75.7,51.0},{69.4,51.0},{67.2,47.8},{64.0,47.8},{62.8,49.6}}},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7844}, obj={2}, names={"Cannibalistic Cousins"}, text="Ride south-west to the Altar of Zul. Kill 15 Vilebranch Soothsayers around it (Earth Shock their casts), and every Vilebranch Scalper you see, again as they respawn: Yayo'jin wants 30 Scalpers and only about 8 live here. You finish them at Agol'watha (53, 40) and Shaol'watha (70, 48) later on the loop, so do not wait here for Scalpers. Stay off the top of the altar (48.7, 68.3): the Keepers there are level 50 elites.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=47.5, y=66.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={2641}, names={"Sprinkle's Secret Ingredient"}, text="The small lake just west of the Altar. Swim to the bottom and pick a Violet Tragan mushroom.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=40.6, y=59.7, path={{46.6,67.5},{44.0,67.5}}},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7828}, obj={2}, names={"Stalking the Stalkers"}, text="Silvermane Howlers roam the hills around the lake.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=43.0, y=54.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7841,2995}, names={"Message to the Wildhammer","Lines of Communication"}, text="Back at Quel'Danil Lodge: kill 15 of each kind of Highvale elf and burn the three Highvale documents, the Records (32.0, 46.8), the Notes (29.6, 48.7) and the Report (28.6, 46.0). The elves respawn while you work. Marksmen shoot from range: pull them round a corner so they come to you, and keep Stoneclaw Totem ready for the second elf. This is a PvP quest: the Highvale elves side with the Alliance and attacking them flags you for PvP, so watch for Alliance players from Aerie Peak.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=31.5, y=47.5, path={{36.6,47.2}}},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2742}, names={"Rin'ji is Trapped!"}, text="Rin'ji is held inside the lodge (30.7, 46.9). Accept once the lodge is cleared: he starts walking out straight away.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=30.7, y=46.9},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={2742}, names={"Rin'ji is Trapped!"}, text="Escort Rin'ji out of the lodge. Elves jump him on the way: drop Stoneclaw Totem beside him to pull them off and throw him a Healing Wave if he gets low. If he dies, abandon the quest and take it again from him in the lodge. His secret is far to the east; you pick it up later.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=30.7, y=46.9},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={77}, names={"A Sticky Situation"}, text="Gilveradin Sunchaser", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=26.7, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={81}, names={"Ripple Delivery"}, text="Gilveradin Sunchaser. You hand the barrel in at Orgrimmar in the next segment.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=26.7, y=48.6},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7839}, names={"Vilebranch Hooligans"}, text="Ride back east. Slagtree's Lost Tools lie at one of five Vilebranch spots. Check the two near the robot first: Agol'watha (53.4, 38.7) and Skulk Rock (57.4, 42.5). Kill the four Vilebranch Scalpers and two Soothsayers at Agol'watha for Yayo'jin while you are there.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=53.4, y=38.7},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={485}, names={"Find OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Right-click the OOX-09/HL Distress Beacon. The robot lies at the head of the river just west of Agol'watha. No beacon yet? Kill the oozes at Skulk Rock (57, 42) and the Vilebranch at Agol'watha (53, 39) until one drops: Find OOX-09, Rescue OOX-09 and An OOX of Your Own are worth about 17,000 XP together.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=49.4, y=37.7},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={485}, names={"Find OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-09/HL", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=49.4, y=37.7},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={836}, names={"Rescue OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Homing Robot OOX-09/HL", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=49.4, y=37.7},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={836}, names={"Rescue OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Escort the robot east to the shore below the Overlook Cliffs. Kill the ambushers quickly; Stoneclaw Totem pulls them off the robot. If it dies, abandon the quest and take it again from the robot at its start spot.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=84.0, y=58.0, path={{50.2,36.4},{51.4,41.5},{52.8,41.5},{59.8,49.6},{67.4,47.8},{69.6,51.0},{75.7,51.0},{77.7,54.0},{82.5,55.8}}},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7840}, names={"Lard Lost His Lunch"}, text="Ride north along the coast to Lard's island, just offshore. Click Lard's Picnic Basket; the Vilebranch Kidnappers that show up carry the lunch. They come in a group: drop Stoneclaw Totem first and Earthbind Totem if one runs.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=84.5, y=41.2},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7839}, names={"Vilebranch Hooligans"}, text="Tools not found yet? Check the three Shaol'watha spots on your way back south: 66.4, 44.8; 71.0, 48.7; 72.5, 52.9.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=71.0, y=48.7},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7844}, names={"Cannibalistic Cousins"}, text="Finish Cannibalistic Cousins at Shaol'watha: most of the Vilebranch Scalpers stand around its two temples (66, 44 and 71, 48), with a few Soothsayers. Still short of 30 Scalpers? Wait here for respawns: there are no more between here and Revantusk.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=70.5, y=48.0},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2742}, names={"Rin'ji is Trapped!"}, text="Ride south-east to the Overlook Cliffs. Rin'ji's Secret is a tablet on the cliff top.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=86.3, y=59.0},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2782}, names={"Rin'ji's Secret"}, text="Take the tablet. You hand it to Oran Snakewrithe in the Undercity.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=86.3, y=59.0},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={7815}, names={"Snapjaws, Mon!"}, text="Saltwater Snapjaws crawl along this whole coast. Kill them along the shore, then follow it south to Revantusk. Gammerita, a big elite turtle, walks the same shore: leave her alone.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=81.0, y=62.0},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7828,7829,7830}, names={"Stalking the Stalkers","Hunt the Savages","Avenging the Fallen"}, text="Back in Revantusk: Huntsman Markhor", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=79.2, y=79.5},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7839}, names={"Vilebranch Hooligans"}, text="Smith Slagtree", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=77.2, y=80.1},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7840}, names={"Lard Lost His Lunch"}, text="Lard", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=78.1, y=81.4},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7841}, names={"Message to the Wildhammer"}, text="Otho Moji'ko. Skip Another Message to the Wildhammer: the gryphons it needs are too spread out.", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=79.4, y=79.1},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7844}, names={"Cannibalistic Cousins"}, text="Mystic Yayo'jin", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=78.8, y=78.2},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={7815}, names={"Snapjaws, Mon!"}, text="Katoom the Angler", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=80.3, y=81.5},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Undercity", text="Gorkas, the wind rider master. Keep the Violet Tragan for Sprinkle in Gadgetzan (next segment).", zone="The Hinterlands", map=1425, x=81.7, y=81.8},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2782,2995}, names={"Rin'ji's Secret","Lines of Communication"}, text="Oran Snakewrithe in the Magic Quarter", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=73.1, y=32.9},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={8273}, names={"Oran's Gratitude"}, text="Oran Snakewrithe", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=73.1, y=32.9},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={8273}, names={"Oran's Gratitude"}, text="Oran Snakewrithe", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=73.1, y=32.9},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={3568}, names={"Seeping Corruption"}, text="Chemist Cuely in the Apothecarium. You fill the vials at the Ruins of Eldarath in Azshara in the next segment.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.7, y=71.4},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={4294,4293}, names={"... and a Batch of Ooze","A Sample of Slime..."}, text="Chemist Fuely, right next to Cuely. Un'Goro slimes come in the next segment, Felwood slimes later; you test the samples at his equipment and hand both in on a later Undercity visit. Skip his follow-up Melding of Influences when it comes.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=47.5, y=73.3},
  {t="H", seg=19, arg="Stonard", text="Hearthstone, or cast Astral Recall: both take you to Stonard."},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=19, text="Haromm in Stonard: learn any level 48 spells you are still missing. Your level 50 spells come when you are back here after the Blasted Lands.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=48.2, y=57.9},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2784}, names={"Fall From Grace"}, text="Ride south-west out of Stonard to the Fallen Hero of the Horde, a ghost standing by the road that leads south into the Blasted Lands", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=34.3, y=66.1},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2784}, names={"Fall From Grace"}, text="Listen to his whole story", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=34.3, y=66.1},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2621}, names={"The Disgraced One"}, text="Fallen Hero of the Horde. You hand it in at Stonard at the end.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=34.3, y=66.1},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2581,2583,2585}, names={"Snickerfang Jowls","A Boar's Vitality","The Decisive Striker"}, text="Follow the road south into the Blasted Lands. Bloodmage Drazial stands just inside the pass.", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=50.5, y=14.2},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2601,2603}, names={"The Basilisk's Bite","Vulture's Vigor"}, text="Bloodmage Lynnore, next to him", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=50.6, y=14.3},
  {t="C", seg=19, q={2581,2583,2585,2601,2603}, names={"Snickerfang Jowls","A Boar's Vitality","The Decisive Striker","The Basilisk's Bite","Vulture's Vigor"}, text="You need 5 Snickerfang Jowls, 6 Blasted Boar Lungs, 6 Scorpok Pincers, 11 Basilisk Brains and 14 Vulture Gizzards in all. North plain (around 50, 22): Starving Snickerfangs and Scorpok Stingers. North-east (around 60, 30): Ashmane Boars, Redstone Basilisks and Black Slayer vultures. Only five boars and five basilisks live there, so also kill the Redstone Crystalhides just south of them (around 60, 40), which drop Basilisk Brains too, and the Helboars (around 60, 45), which drop Boar Lungs too. Both are level 51-53 and hit a little harder. Centre (around 52, 40): Bonepicker vultures and Snickerfang Hyenas. Vultures and hyenas often come two at a time: Stoneclaw Totem holds one, Healing Wave between pulls.", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=55.0, y=30.0},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="If an Imperfect Draenethyst Fragment dropped, take it to Kum'isha the Collector", text="He stands in the centre of the Blasted Lands and gives Everything Counts In Large Amounts (5650 XP) for it. Do not farm for one.", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=52.0, y=35.6},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2581,2583,2585}, names={"Snickerfang Jowls","A Boar's Vitality","The Decisive Striker"}, text="Bloodmage Drazial", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=50.5, y=14.2},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2601,2603}, names={"The Basilisk's Bite","Vulture's Vigor"}, text="Bloodmage Lynnore", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=50.6, y=14.3},
  {t="L", seg=19, lvl=51, text="Quest XP runs short here: grind to 51, the next segment's Un'Goro mobs are 50-55. Best XP: Scorpok Stingers (50-51) on the north plain (46-57, 14-24), and Snickerfang Hyenas and Bonepickers (49-50) in the centre around 53, 38. The Starving Snickerfangs (45-46) give much less. Stay north of the Felhounds (54-55, around 60, 55): they drain mana.", zone="Blasted Lands", map=1419, x=52.0, y=28.0},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Cast Astral Recall (back to Stonard)", text="Or ride back north through the pass and the Swamp."},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=19, text="Haromm: learn your level 50 spells. He also offers Elemental Mastery at 50: leave it for now; the next segment tells you when to take it.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=48.2, y=57.9},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2621}, names={"The Disgraced One"}, text="Dispatch Commander Ruag in Stonard", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=47.8, y=54.9},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={2622}, names={"The Missing Orders"}, text="Dispatch Commander Ruag", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=47.8, y=54.9},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={2622}, names={"The Missing Orders"}, text="Bengor, also in Stonard. Skip his next quest, The Swamp Talker (level 55).", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=45.0, y=57.4},
  {t="FLY", seg=19, arg="Booty Bay", text="Breyk, the wind rider master in Stonard", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=46.1, y=54.8},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Optional dungeon: Sunken Temple, levels 50-60", text="The temple is in the lake in the middle of the Swamp of Sorrows, east of Stonard: swim down through the sunken doorway and follow the halls to the portal. Not on your path, only if you want the detour: Jammal'an the Prophet (The Hinterlands 34, 75). Needs an earlier quest chain this route does not do: The God Hakkar, The Temple of Atal'Hakkar.", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=69.9, y=53.5, dg=15, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={1445}, names={"The Temple of Atal'Hakkar"}, zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=47.9, y=54.8, dg=15},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={836}, names={"Rescue OOX-09/HL!"}, text="Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.4, y=76.3},
  {t="A", seg=19, q={3721}, names={"An OOX of Your Own"}, text="Oglethorpe Obnoticus. Only offered once all three OOX robots are home; otherwise skip this step and the next.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.4, y=76.3},
  {t="T", seg=19, q={3721}, names={"An OOX of Your Own"}, text="Oglethorpe Obnoticus. It has no objectives; the reward is a Mechanical Chicken pet.", zone="Stranglethorn Vale", map=1434, x=28.4, y=76.3},
  {t="N", seg=19, arg="Take the boat from the Booty Bay dock to Ratchet", text="Keep 81 and 32 for Orgrimmar, 2641 for Gadgetzan, and the three chemist quests for later. Your hearthstone stays set to Stonard until the next segment rebinds it in Gadgetzan."},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="You step off the boat at the Ratchet dock", text="Your hearthstone is still set to Stonard: do not use it or Astral Recall until you have bound in Gadgetzan."},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4502}, names={"Volcanic Activity"}, text="Liv Rizzlefix, a few steps south-west of the flight master. The fire elementals on Fire Plume Ridge in Un'Goro drop the ash; you hand it to her on the next segment's Ratchet stop", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.5, y=38.7},
  {t="FLY", seg=20, arg="Orgrimmar", text="Bragok, the Ratchet flight master, at the north end of town", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=63.1, y=37.2},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={936}, names={"Assisting Arch Druid Runetotem"}, text="Innkeeper Gryshka, Valley of Strength, just east of the wind rider tower. Do not bind here yet", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=54.1, y=68.4},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="Buy a Mithril Casing at the Auction House", text="It is an engineering part for the A-Me 01 robot in Un'Goro. If none is for sale, skip Chasing A-Me 01 parts 2 and 3 when you get there."},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={32}, names={"Rise of the Silithid"}, text="Zilzibin Drumlore, at the south end of the Drag", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=56.3, y=46.7},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4494}, names={"March of the Silithid"}, text="Zilzibin Drumlore. Needs level 50", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=56.3, y=46.7},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={81}, names={"Ripple Delivery"}, text="Dran Droffers, at the east end of the Drag", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=59.5, y=36.6},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={2283}, names={"Necklace Recovery"}, zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=59.5, y=36.6, dg=12},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4300}, names={"Bone-Bladed Weapons"}, text="Jes'rimon, at the north end of the Drag", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=55.5, y=34.1},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=20, text="Valley of Wisdom: learn your level 50 spells if you did not get them from Haromm in Stonard. Already trained? Skip it", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=38.8, y=36.4},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="Optional class quest: Elemental Mastery", text="The shaman trainers offer it from level 50. It wants one Elemental Air, Fire, Earth and Water and ends at Bath'rah the Windwatcher in Alterac, at the very end of the route (segment 23); this route does not track it. Your quest log reaches the full 20 in Un'Goro, so do not take it now: if you want it, take it on a later Orgrimmar trainer visit."},
  {t="FLY", seg=20, arg="Thunder Bluff", text="Doras, the wind rider master on the tower in the Valley of Strength", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=45.1, y=63.9},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={7068}, names={"Shadowshard Fragments"}, zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=39.2, y=86.3, dg=14},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={936}, names={"Assisting Arch Druid Runetotem"}, text="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=78.6, y=28.6},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3761}, names={"Un'Goro Soil"}, text="Collect about 50 Un'Goro Soil in total: 20 for this quest, 5 for Gadgetzan, and 2 for each Morrowgrain attempt later", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=78.6, y=28.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=20, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Tal, the wind rider master on the central mesa", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=47.0, y=49.8},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={2280}, names={"The Platinum Discs"}, text="The Platinum Discs: Sage Truthseeker.", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=34.4, y=46.9, dg=12},
  {t="S", seg=20, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Innkeeper Fizzgrimble at the inn. You hearth back here when you leave Un'Goro"},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={2641}, names={"Sprinkle's Secret Ingredient"}, text="Sprinkle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.1, y=26.9},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={2661}, names={"Delivery for Marin"}, text="Sprinkle", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.1, y=26.9},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={2661}, names={"Delivery for Marin"}, text="Marin Noggenfogger. He offers Noggenfogger Elixir next: optional, no XP", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.8, y=28.7},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4494}, names={"March of the Silithid"}, text="Alchemist Pestlezugg", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.9, y=27.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4496}, names={"Bungle in the Jungle"}, text="Alchemist Pestlezugg", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.9, y=27.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4504}, names={"Super Sticky"}, text="Tran'rek", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=26.8},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="Optional dungeon: Alcaz Prison, levels 48-53", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is on Alcaz Island, off the north-east coast of Dustwallow Marsh. It has 5 Horde quests (from level 46 to 48), but who gives them is not published yet: ask around Brackenwall Village and take what is offered; the addon logs it so these steps can be filled in.", dg=19, run=true},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="Optional Muisek detour (about 21,000 XP): only if Testing the Vessel is finished in your log", text="FLY Camp Mojache and hand it to Witch Doctor Uzer'i. He offers each Muisek only after you hand in the one before, and each one comes with its own vessel, so go back to him between them. Take Hippogryph Muisek and Natural Materials. Frayfeather hippogryphs in the highlands south-west of camp (around 55, 67): use the vessel on 10 corpses, and keep killing and looting them until you also have 20 Resilient Sinew and 40 Metallic Fragments. Back at Uzer'i, hand in Hippogryph Muisek and take Faerie Dragon Muisek: 8 Sprite Darters just west of camp (64-70, 44-49), which also drop the 6 Encrusted Minerals. Hand it in and take Treant Muisek: 3 Wandering Forest Walkers, lone treants near 74, 39, 73, 55 and 54, 47, which also drop the 2 Splintered Logs. Hand in Treant Muisek and Natural Materials (skip Mountain Giant Muisek, elite), then FLY Gadgetzan. No Testing the Vessel? Skip this."},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4290}, names={"The Fare of Lar'korwi"}, text="Ride south-west out of Gadgetzan and down the trail into Un'Goro Crater. Torwa Pathfinder waits at the bottom", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4289}, names={"The Apes of Un'Goro"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3844}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="A Wrecked Raft on the shore of the pond north-west of Torwa", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=63.0, y=68.6, path={{71.4,69.3},{69.2,69.3},{65.4,65.7},{63.6,65.7}}},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3844}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="A Small Pack, a few steps away in the water", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=63.1, y=69.1},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3845}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="Right-click A Small Pack in your bags to take out the compass, map and key. Keep them for Linken at Marshal's Refuge", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=63.1, y=69.1},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4290}, names={"The Fare of Lar'korwi"}, text="The Fresh Threshadon Carcass north of Torwa. A Tyrant Devilsaur (elite) patrols this jungle: watch for it and keep out of its way. From now on, loot every Power Crystal (red, green, blue, yellow) and every Un'Goro Dirt Pile you pass", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=68.7, y=56.7},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4290}, names={"The Fare of Lar'korwi"}, zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4291}, names={"The Scent of Lar'korwi"}, zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4291,4300}, names={"The Scent of Lar'korwi","Bone-Bladed Weapons"}, text="Walk up to the ravasaur eggs west of Torwa and Lar'korwi Mates come out to guard them; they drop the glands. Any ravasaur here can drop White Ravasaur Claws. They hit fast: Stoneskin Totem down, Healing Wave between pulls", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=64.0, y=72.0},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4291}, names={"The Scent of Lar'korwi"}, text="He offers The Bait for Lar'korwi next: leave it until you pass him again in loop 2, to save log space", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="From now on kill every ooze you pass until you have 15-20 Un'Goro Slime Samples (for ... and a Batch of Ooze)", text="Primal Oozes sit in the middle of the crater (on your ride north and around the hive), Muculent Oozes in the east jungle (loop 1) and Glutinous Oozes on the west side (loop 2). They stack. You test them in the Undercity at the end of the route; not every sample tests pure and you need 5 that do"},
  {t="G", seg=20, text="Ride north through the middle of the crater to Marshal's Refuge. Keep looting crystals and soil. Leave the Devilsaurs and Stegodons (elites) alone", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=45.2, y=5.8, path={{72.8,65.7},{76.9,59.4},{76.9,51.3},{75.5,49.3},{74.8,43.9},{67.8,33.4},{66.0,33.1},{61.4,28.0},{59.6,28.0},{54.2,21.7},{51.0,21.7},{46.2,16.0},{45.2,14.5}}},
  {t="F", seg=20, arg="Marshal's Refuge", text="Gryfe", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=45.2, y=5.8},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3845}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="Linken. He offers It's a Secret to Everybody next: leave it until you are back from loop 2, to save log space", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.7, y=8.1},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3881}, names={"Expedition Salvation"}, text="Williden Marshal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.0, y=7.1},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3882}, names={"Roll the Bones"}, text="Spark Nilminer", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.5, y=7.4},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4503}, names={"Shizzle's Flyer"}, text="Shizzle", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.2, y=11.6},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4145}, names={"Larion and Muigin"}, text="Larion", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=45.5, y=8.7},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4284}, names={"Crystals of Power"}, text="J.D. Collie, in the cave at the north end of the camp. Keep it until you are back from loop 1: you need 7 Power Crystals of each colour, and loop 1 passes plenty of them", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7, path={{42.8,6.4}}, cave=true},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4243}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="Karna Remtravel, just south-east of the camp", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=46.4, y=13.4},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4501}, names={"Beware of Pterrordax"}, text="The Beware of Pterrordax sign in the camp", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.5, y=8.4},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4504}, names={"Super Sticky"}, text="Ride south to the Lakkari Tar Pits: Tar Beasts, Tar Creepers, Tar Lurkers and Tar Lords drop the tar. Keep looting every Power Crystal you pass", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=50.1, y=23.3},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4145,4145}, obj={1,4}, names={"Larion and Muigin","Larion and Muigin"}, text="Bloodpetal Lashers and Threshers in the jungle east of the tar pits. Young Diemetradons and Fledgling Pterrordax here drop Webbed Scales for Shizzle; loot them as you go", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=67.0, y=35.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={3881}, obj={1}, names={"Expedition Salvation"}, text="The Crate of Foodstuffs at the abandoned Ironstone Camp", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=68.5, y=36.5},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4289}, names={"The Apes of Un'Goro"}, text="Ride north along the east side to Fungal Rock, the gorilla lair. Gorillas, Stompers and Thunderers drop the pelts; they often come in pairs, so drop Stoneclaw Totem for the second one. Leave U'cha (in the cave) for later", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=66.0, y=16.5},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4243}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="A-Me 01 sits at the foot of Fungal Rock", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=67.7, y=16.8},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4244}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=67.7, y=16.8},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4244}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="Needs the Mithril Casing. No casing? Skip this and the escort", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=67.7, y=16.8},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4245}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=67.7, y=16.8},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4245}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="Escort A-Me 01 back to Karna Remtravel. Gorillas attack her on the way: kill them fast, Stoneclaw Totem to hold the extras off", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=46.4, y=13.4, path={{67.4,22.3},{54.6,22.3},{51.4,21.7}}},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4245}, names={"Chasing A-Me 01"}, text="Karna Remtravel", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=46.4, y=13.4},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4284}, names={"Crystals of Power"}, text="J.D. Collie. Still short of a colour? All four grow on the rise between the camp and the Northern Pylon (47-61, 8-20): loot them there and come back before you take the pylons", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4285,4287,4288}, names={"The Northern Pylon","The Eastern Pylon","The Western Pylon"}, text="J.D. Collie", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3883}, names={"Alien Ecology"}, text="Hol'anyee Marshal. She gives you the Scraping Vial", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.9, y=7.2},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4492}, names={"Lost!"}, text="Spraggle Frock", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.6, y=8.5},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4285}, names={"The Northern Pylon"}, text="The Northern Crystal Pylon, on the rise just east of the camp. Walking up to it completes the quest. Plain Pterrordax circle this rise: kill the ones you see for Beware of Pterrordax (you finish the 10 at the Gorishi hive later) and loot their Webbed Scales", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=56.5, y=12.5},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4285}, names={"The Northern Pylon"}, text="Ride back west to J.D. Collie in the cave at the north end of Marshal's Refuge (about a minute) and hand in the Northern Pylon now: it frees the log slot Volcanic Activity needs. Then ride south-west across the crater", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7, path={{42.8,6.4}}, cave=true},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4501,4145}, obj={2,2}, names={"Beware of Pterrordax","Larion and Muigin"}, text="West side of the crater: Frenzied Pterrordax and Bloodpetal Trappers. The Frenzied Pterrordax also drop Webbed Pterrordax Scales for Shizzle. King Mosh (level 60 elite devilsaur) and a Devilsaur (elite) patrol this side: keep an eye out and move away when they come. Lightning Shield up, Healing Wave between pulls", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=32.0, y=40.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={974}, names={"Finding the Source"}, text="Krakle, at the Golakka Hot Springs. Needs level 51", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=30.9, y=50.4},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4288}, names={"The Western Pylon"}, text="The Western Crystal Pylon", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=23.9, y=59.2},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={3882,4503}, names={"Roll the Bones","Shizzle's Flyer"}, text="Dinosaur Bone piles lie on the ground south of the pylon. Elder Diemetradons roam these bone fields: they drop bones and the Webbed Diemetradon Scales, and Frenzied Pterrordax here finish the Pterrordax scales. Stegodons (elite) roam here too, so give them room", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=33.0, y=72.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={3881}, obj={2}, names={"Expedition Salvation"}, text="The Research Equipment at the abandoned south-west camp. Stegodons (elite) graze all around it: watch where they walk and slip in between them; do not fight them", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=38.4, y=66.1},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={3883,4496,4501}, obj={0,0,1}, names={"Alien Ecology","Bungle in the Jungle","Beware of Pterrordax"}, text="The Gorishi hive in the south. Go in to a hatchery chamber with hanging larvae (48.7, 85.3) and use the Scraping Vial on the wall. Any Gorishi can drop the Scent Gland, and they drop soil too. The wasps and stingers come two or three at a time: Stoneclaw Totem plus Magma Totem, and Healing Wave early. Pterrordax circle the hive: finish the 10 for Beware of Pterrordax here", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=49.0, y=81.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={3761}, names={"Un'Goro Soil"}, text="You should have 20 Un'Goro Soil by now. Keep collecting until you have about 50", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=62.3, y=76.5},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4289}, names={"The Apes of Un'Goro"}, text="Ride east to Torwa Pathfinder at the crater entrance", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4292}, names={"The Bait for Lar'korwi"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder. Keep Torwa's Pouch: you fight Lar'korwi (level 56) on your way out of the crater, when you are higher level", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4301}, names={"The Mighty U'cha"}, text="U'cha (level 55) lives in the Fungal Rock cave. You kill him on the way out", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4287}, names={"The Eastern Pylon"}, text="Ride north from Torwa along the eastern side to the Eastern Crystal Pylon on the ridge. Walking up to it completes the quest", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=77.2, y=50.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={974,4145,4502}, obj={0,3,0}, names={"Finding the Source","Larion and Muigin","Volcanic Activity"}, text="Ride west to Fire Plume Ridge, the volcano in the middle of the crater. Right-click Krakle's Thermometer at each hot spot until you find the hottest. Blazerunner (level 56 elite) stands by the lava at the top: stay clear of him. Bloodpetal Flayers grow around its south and east base. Scorching Elementals and Living Blazes (53-55) all round the volcano drop the 9 Un'Goro Ash. Pull them one at a time; Flame Shock and Searing Totem do little to them, so use Earth or Frost Shock and Lightning Bolt", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=47.8, y=49.1},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={974}, names={"Finding the Source"}, text="Back west to Krakle", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=30.9, y=50.4},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={980}, names={"The New Springs"}, text="Goes to Donova Snowden in Winterspring next segment", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=30.9, y=50.4},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4492}, names={"Lost!"}, text="Ringo, sitting on Fire Plume Ridge", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=51.9, y=49.8},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4491}, names={"A Little Help From My Friends"}, zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=51.9, y=49.8},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4491}, names={"A Little Help From My Friends"}, text="Lead Ringo north to Marshal's Refuge. When he faints, use Spraggle's Canteen on him", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.6, y=8.5},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4491}, names={"A Little Help From My Friends"}, text="Spraggle Frock", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.6, y=8.5},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4501}, names={"Beware of Pterrordax"}, text="Spraggle Frock", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.6, y=8.5},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3882}, names={"Roll the Bones"}, text="Spark Nilminer", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.5, y=7.4},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4503}, names={"Shizzle's Flyer"}, text="Shizzle", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.2, y=11.6},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3881}, names={"Expedition Salvation"}, text="Williden Marshal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.0, y=7.1},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3884}, names={"Williden's Journal"}, text="Did A Mangled Journal drop from an Un'Goro creature? Right-click it now. No journal? Skip this and the next step", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.9, y=7.1},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3884}, names={"Williden's Journal"}, text="Williden Marshal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.9, y=7.1},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3883}, names={"Alien Ecology"}, text="Hol'anyee Marshal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.9, y=7.2},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3908}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="Linken. Linken's Sword goes to Donova Snowden in Winterspring next segment", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=44.7, y=8.1},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4145}, names={"Larion and Muigin"}, text="Larion", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=45.5, y=8.7},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4147}, names={"Marvon's Workshop"}, text="Keep it for Ratchet next segment", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=45.5, y=8.7},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4287,4288}, names={"The Eastern Pylon","The Western Pylon"}, text="J.D. Collie", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={4321}, names={"Making Sense of It"}, zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4321}, names={"Making Sense of It"}, text="Wait a moment while he works", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=41.9, y=2.7},
  {t="L", seg=20, lvl=53, text="Quest XP runs about a level short in this segment. Grind to 53 here, before U'cha (55) and Lar'korwi (56). Closest to the camp: Tar Lords and Tar Lurkers (52-54) in the tar pits just south (42-54, 15-28). On the way to U'cha: the Stompers and Thunderers (51-53) around Fungal Rock. Densest: the west side (Elder Diemetradons, Frenzied Pterrordax, Bloodpetal Trappers, 52-55). Kill oozes you pass for slime samples", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=49.0, y=21.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4301}, names={"The Mighty U'cha"}, text="U'cha in the Fungal Rock cave (level 55). Clear the gorillas at the cave mouth first, then pull him out to the cleared entrance. Searing Totem and Strength of Earth Totem down first (only one Earth totem works at a time, so swap to Stoneclaw if a gorilla joins in); keep Flame Shock on him and Healing Wave when you drop below half", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=68.1, y=12.6},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={4292}, names={"The Bait for Lar'korwi"}, text="Ride south along the eastern ridge past the Eastern Pylon to the ledge covered in big bones. Open Torwa's Pouch, put the meat on the flat rock and use the pheromone mixture on it. Lar'korwi (level 56) charges in: have Searing and Stoneclaw Totems down before you use the mixture, and Frost Shock him if you need room to heal", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=79.9, y=49.9, path={{70.0,13.9},{69.8,22.6},{71.0,24.4},{71.0,29.8},{74.0,34.3},{75.5,39.1},{76.1,46.6}}},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4292}, names={"The Bait for Lar'korwi"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder at the crater entrance", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0, path={{77.1,51.0},{76.9,59.4},{74.2,63.6},{73.8,67.5},{71.8,70.5}}},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4301}, names={"The Mighty U'cha"}, text="Torwa Pathfinder", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=71.6, y=76.0},
  {t="H", seg=20, arg="Gadgetzan", text="Hearthstone, or cast Astral Recall. If both are on cooldown, ride up the trail into Tanaris and north to Gadgetzan"},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4496}, names={"Bungle in the Jungle"}, text="Alchemist Pestlezugg. Skip Pawn Captures Queen (group fight with the hive queen)", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=50.9, y=27.0},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4504}, names={"Super Sticky"}, text="Tran'rek", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=26.8},
  {t="FLY", seg=20, arg="Thunder Bluff", text="Bulkrek Ragefist, the Gadgetzan wind rider master", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.6, y=25.4},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3761}, names={"Un'Goro Soil"}, text="Ghede, among the dirt piles on Elder Rise", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=77.5, y=22.0},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3782}, names={"Morrowgrain Research"}, text="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=78.6, y=28.6},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3782}, names={"Morrowgrain Research"}, text="Bashana Runetotem, also on Elder Rise", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=71.1, y=34.2},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3786}, names={"Morrowgrain Research"}, text="She gives you the Evergreen Pouch. Handing in the Seed Voucher already gave you 20 Packets of Tharlendris Seeds, more than your soil covers, so do not buy any. Use the pouch (1 seed and 2 soil) every 10 minutes from now on; you hand in 10 Morrowgrain on your next Thunder Bluff stop", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=71.1, y=34.2},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=20, text="Shaman trainers in the Pools of Vision under Spirit Rise, beside Apothecary Zamah: learn your level 52 spells", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=22.8, y=21.1},
  {t="FLY", seg=20, arg="Orgrimmar", text="Tal", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=47.0, y=49.8},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={4300}, names={"Bone-Bladed Weapons"}, text="Jes'rimon in the Drag", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=55.5, y=34.1},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3504}, names={"Betrayed"}, text="Belgrom Rockmaul, Valley of Honor", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=75.2, y=34.2},
  {t="S", seg=20, arg="Orgrimmar", text="Innkeeper Gryshka, Valley of Strength. You hearth back here from Azshara"},
  {t="FLY", seg=20, arg="Splintertree Post", text="Doras", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=45.1, y=63.9},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={5535,5536}, names={"Spiritual Unrest","A Land Filled with Hatred"}, text="Ride east out of Splintertree on the road into Azshara. The road passes near Forest Song, an Alliance outpost, so give its guards room. Loh'atu camps just inside the Azshara border", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=11.4, y=78.2},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={5535}, names={"Spiritual Unrest"}, text="Highborne Apparitions and Lichlings haunt the Shadowsong Shrine, north-east of Loh'atu. The Lichlings cast frost bolts: Earth Shock them", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=16.4, y=70.0},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={5536}, names={"A Land Filled with Hatred"}, text="Haldarr satyrs, tricksters and felsworn in the satyr camp further north-east. Earth Shock the felsworn's casts", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=20.1, y=61.8},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={5535,5536}, names={"Spiritual Unrest","A Land Filled with Hatred"}, text="Loh'atu", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=11.4, y=78.2},
  {t="F", seg=20, arg="Valormok", text="Follow the road north to Valormok and talk to Kroum", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.0, y=49.6},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3504}, names={"Betrayed"}, text="Ag'tor Bloodfist", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.3, y=51.5},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3505}, names={"Betrayed"}, text="Ag'tor Bloodfist", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.3, y=51.5},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3517}, names={"Stealing Knowledge"}, text="Jediga", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.6, y=51.4},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3381}, names={"A Meeting with the Master"}, text="Sanath Lim-yo, at the foot of the cliffs just east of Valormok. New in Forever: he wants 2 Undamaged Hippogryph Feathers before he sends you up to his master, Archmage Xylem. Not offered? Skip the feather steps; when you come back with Jediga's tablet, ask him for Meeting with the Master instead", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=28.1, y=50.1},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3601}, names={"Kim'jael Indeed!"}, text="Kim'jael, far to the north-east. Follow the road east, then north", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=53.5, y=21.8},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={3505,3601}, names={"Betrayed","Kim'jael Indeed!"}, text="The blood elf camp on the bluffs south of Kim'jael. Kill Reclaimers and Surveyors and pick up Kim'jael's Equipment boxes on the ground in the camp. The elves cast: Earth Shock their spells and pull them one at a time", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=57.0, y=28.5},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={3381}, names={"A Meeting with the Master"}, text="Thunderhead Skystormers on the bluffs around the blood elf camp, and the Stagwings along the road you rode in on (35-48, 31-44), drop Undamaged Hippogryph Feathers; you need 2. Still short later? The Thunderhead Hippogryphs around Valormok (15-21, 49-66) drop them too. Skip if you do not have the quest", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=54.7, y=22.3},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3505}, names={"Betrayed"}, text="Magus Rimtori's camp, a ring of crystals at the east end: read the Kaldorei Tome of Summoning", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=59.5, y=31.3},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3506}, names={"Betrayed"}, text="The Kaldorei Tome of Summoning", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=59.5, y=31.3},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={3506}, names={"Betrayed"}, text="Clear the camp, then destroy the Arcane Focusing Crystal next to the tome. Magus Rimtori (level 55) appears; she is a caster. Grounding Totem soaks one of her spells and Earth Shock interrupts the rest. Kill her and loot her head", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=59.5, y=31.4},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3601}, names={"Kim'jael Indeed!"}, text="Kim'jael", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=53.5, y=21.8},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={5534}, names={"Kim'jael's \"Missing\" Equipment"}, zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=53.5, y=21.8},
  {t="C", seg=20, q={3517,3568,5534}, names={"Stealing Knowledge","Seeping Corruption","Kim'jael's \"Missing\" Equipment"}, text="Ruins of Eldarath, east of Valormok. The four tablets lie among the ruins (35-43, 44-65). Kill Spitelash Sirens and Myrmidons on the east side near the shore (about 45, 50): both drop Some Rune. Use each numbered vial at its matching pool: #1 48.0, 61.0, #2 47.8, 51.4, #3 48.6, 48.5, #4 47.4, 46.2. Naga come in groups: Stoneclaw Totem for the second, Earth Shock the Sirens' casts", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=37.0, y=53.2, path={{48.2,28.0},{48.0,31.6},{45.0,35.8},{45.6,42.1},{43.0,49.0}}},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={5534}, names={"Kim'jael's \"Missing\" Equipment"}, text="Ride back north-east to Kim'jael", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=53.5, y=21.8, path={{43.0,49.0},{45.6,42.1},{45.0,35.8},{48.0,31.6},{48.2,28.0}}},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3506}, names={"Betrayed"}, text="Ag'tor Bloodfist, Valormok", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.3, y=51.5},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3507}, names={"Betrayed"}, text="Ag'tor Bloodfist. It is handed in to Belgrom in Orgrimmar", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.3, y=51.5},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3517}, names={"Stealing Knowledge"}, text="Jediga", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.6, y=51.4},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3518,3541,3542}, names={"Delivery to Magatha","Delivery to Jes'rimon","Delivery to Andron Gant"}, text="Jediga. One tablet goes to Thunder Bluff, one to Orgrimmar and one to Andron Gant in the Undercity, where the last segment starts. Skip Andron's follow-up there: its payment goes back to Jediga", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.6, y=51.4},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3561}, names={"Delivery to Archmage Xylem"}, text="Jediga: the last tablet goes to Archmage Xylem, at the top of the tower behind Sanath's camp. Skip it, and the Xylem steps below, only if Sanath will not send you up", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.6, y=51.4},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3381}, names={"A Meeting with the Master"}, text="Sanath Lim-yo: give him the feathers, then ask him to send you up (Meeting with the Master). He puts you at the top of Archmage Xylem's tower. No feather quest? Just ask for Meeting with the Master", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=28.1, y=50.1},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3561}, names={"Delivery to Archmage Xylem"}, text="Archmage Xylem", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=29.2, y=40.2},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3565}, names={"Xylem's Payment to Jediga"}, text="Archmage Xylem", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=29.2, y=40.2},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="Talk to Nyrill at the tower (Return Trip) to be sent back down to Sanath's camp", text="Skip if you were not up the tower"},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3565}, names={"Xylem's Payment to Jediga"}, text="Jediga", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.6, y=51.4},
  {t="H", seg=20, arg="Orgrimmar", text="Hearthstone, or cast Astral Recall. If both are on cooldown, fly from Valormok"},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3541}, names={"Delivery to Jes'rimon"}, text="Jes'rimon in the Drag", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=55.5, y=34.1},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3563}, names={"Jes'rimon's Payment to Jediga"}, text="Jes'rimon", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=55.5, y=34.1},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3507}, names={"Betrayed"}, text="Belgrom Rockmaul, Valley of Honor", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=75.2, y=34.2},
  {t="FLY", seg=20, arg="Thunder Bluff", text="Doras", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=45.1, y=63.9},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3518}, names={"Delivery to Magatha"}, text="Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=69.8, y=30.9},
  {t="A", seg=20, q={3562}, names={"Magatha's Payment to Jediga"}, text="Magatha Grimtotem", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=69.9, y=30.9},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3786}, names={"Morrowgrain Research"}, text="Bashana Runetotem. Fewer than 10 Morrowgrain? Keep using the pouch and hand it in on the next segment's Thunder Bluff stop", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=71.1, y=34.2},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=20, text="Pools of Vision under Spirit Rise: learn your level 54 spells if you are 54. Not 54 yet? Skip it; they wait for the next segment's Thunder Bluff stop", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=22.8, y=21.1},
  {t="FLY", seg=20, arg="Valormok", text="Tal", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=47.0, y=49.8},
  {t="T", seg=20, q={3562,3563}, names={"Magatha's Payment to Jediga","Jes'rimon's Payment to Jediga"}, text="Jediga", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=22.6, y=51.4},
  {t="L", seg=20, lvl=54, text="Quest XP runs short. Grind the Spitelash Sirens and Myrmidons in the Ruins of Eldarath before you leave Azshara; this is TUGs' Azshara grind spot. Pull singles at the edges, Earth Shock the Sirens, Healing Wave between pulls", zone="Azshara", map=1447, x=42.0, y=52.0, path={{28.6,49.9},{31.6,47.2},{33.2,43.6},{34.8,43.6},{36.6,46.3},{42.2,46.0},{43.0,49.3}}},
  {t="N", seg=20, arg="Segment done. Next segment flies from Valormok to Splintertree for Felwood", text="Keep in your log: It's a Secret to Everybody and The New Springs (Winterspring), Marvon's Workshop and Volcanic Activity (Ratchet), Seeping Corruption, ... and a Batch of Ooze, A Sample of Slime... and Delivery to Andron Gant (Undercity), plus Morrowgrain Research if you still need Morrowgrain. Your hearthstone is set to Orgrimmar"},
  {t="FLY", seg=21, arg="Splintertree Post", text="You start at Valormok at level 54, hearthstone set to Orgrimmar. Kroum is the Valormok wind rider master"},
  {t="G", seg=21, text="Ride west from Splintertree to the main road and follow it north into Felwood. The Emerald Sanctuary is the first camp past the border", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=50.9, y=85.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={8460}, names={"Timbermaw Ally"}, text="Grazle, beside the road just south of the Emerald Sanctuary. If he offers a Timbermaw Ally that asks for 5 of each furbolg instead (Forever lists a new 6131), take that one; the logger records it", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=50.9, y=85.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5155}, names={"Forces of Jaedenar"}, text="Greta Mosshoof, Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4102}, names={"Cleansing Felwood"}, text="Maybess Riverbreeze, on the west side of the camp", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=46.8, y=83.1},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={8460}, names={"Timbermaw Ally"}, text="Deadwood Village, west of the road just south of the camp: Warriors, Pathfinders and Gardeners. Every kill also raises Timbermaw reputation, which you need for the tunnel later. Leave Overlord Ror (the big one at the south end) until you have his quest from Bloodvenom Post", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=47.5, y=91.0},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={8460}, names={"Timbermaw Ally"}, text="Grazle", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=50.9, y=85.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={8462}, names={"Speak to Nafien"}, text="Grazle. Nafien waits at the north end of Felwood", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=50.9, y=85.0},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Kill the slimes you pass from now on", text="Cursed Oozes (41, 71) and Tainted Oozes (42, 47) sit beside the road. Collect 15-20 Felwood Slime Samples for Chemist Fuely's quest (4293): you test them in the Undercity in the last segment. Not every sample tests as corrupted and you need 5 that do. The route does not come back to Felwood after this segment. They stack, so spares cost nothing"},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5155}, names={"Forces of Jaedenar"}, text="Jaedenar, west of the road: the hounds, guardsmen, adepts and cultists near the entrance. Don't go deep yet. Earth Shock the Adepts and Cultists when they start casting", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=38.0, y=61.0},
  {t="F", seg=21, arg="Bloodvenom Post", text="Brakkar, the wind rider master, a little further north", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.4, y=53.8},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4505}, names={"Well of Corruption"}, text="Winna Hazzard", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.2, y=52.3},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4521}, names={"Wild Guardians"}, text="Trull Failbane. His owlbeasts are in Winterspring", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.7, y=52.8},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={6162}, names={"A Husband's Last Battle"}, text="Dreka'Sur. Overlord Ror is in Deadwood Village; you pass it again soon", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.8, y=52.7},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4505}, names={"Well of Corruption"}, text="The corrupted moonwell at the Ruins of Constellas, south-west of Jaedenar. Use Winna's flask at the well; Jadefire satyrs guard it, so clear the ones next to the well first", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=32.3, y=66.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4505}, names={"Well of Corruption"}, text="Back to Winna Hazzard, Bloodvenom Post", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.2, y=52.3},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4506}, names={"Corrupted Sabers"}, text="She hands you a kitten", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.2, y=52.3},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4506}, names={"Corrupted Sabers"}, text="Same moonwell at the Ruins of Constellas. Release the kitten at the well, wait until it has changed, then take it back", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=32.3, y=66.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4506}, names={"Corrupted Sabers"}, text="Winna Hazzard. Click the cat at her feet to finish", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.2, y=52.3},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5155}, names={"Forces of Jaedenar"}, text="Ride back south along the road to Greta Mosshoof, Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5157}, names={"Collection of the Corrupt Water"}, text="Greta gives you an Empty Canteen", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5157}, names={"Collection of the Corrupt Water"}, text="The moon well in the middle of Jaedenar. Clear a path to it and fill the canteen", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=35.2, y=59.8},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5157}, names={"Collection of the Corrupt Water"}, text="Back to Greta Mosshoof", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5158}, names={"Seeking Spiritual Aid"}, text="Islen Waterseer is on the Barrens coast; you see her later in this segment", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={6162}, names={"A Husband's Last Battle"}, text="Overlord Ror, at the south end of Deadwood Village, just south of the camp. He hits hard: kill the furbolgs around him first, drop Stoneclaw Totem when you pull him and keep a Healing Wave ready. Take his claw", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=48.2, y=94.3},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={6162}, names={"A Husband's Last Battle"}, text="Dreka'Sur, Bloodvenom Post, as you ride north", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.8, y=52.7},
  {t="G", seg=21, text="Ride north past Bloodvenom Post on the main road. The Tainted Oozes here count for the slime samples. Next comes Shatter Scar Vale, the crater field just north-east (around 40-46, 37-44): the Infernal Bodyguards and Sentries in it are elite, so go around it rather than following the next arrow straight across", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=42.0, y=47.0},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4102}, names={"Cleansing Felwood"}, text="Irontree Cavern, north-east of Irontree Woods. On the way, go around Shatter Scar Vale (elite infernals) instead of crossing it. Warpwood Moss Flayers and Shredders drop the 15 Blood Amber. Dessecus, a rare elite, spawns at the south-east end (around 58, 22): if he is up, fight the flayers and shredders in the north-west part and leave him alone", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=56.5, y=18.0, path={{42.0,45.1},{43.8,42.4},{48.4,38.2},{50.8,30.4},{53.2,28.3},{56.8,22.0},{56.5,16.5}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={8462}, names={"Speak to Nafien"}, text="Nafien, outside Timbermaw Hold at the far north end of the road", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=64.8, y=8.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={8461}, names={"Deadwood of the North"}, text="Nafien", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=64.8, y=8.1},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={8461}, names={"Deadwood of the North"}, text="Felpaw Village, just west of Nafien: Den Watchers, Avengers and Shamans. Earth Shock the Shamans when they heal; if two furbolgs come at once, drop Stoneclaw Totem and kill them one by one", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=61.5, y=8.0},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={8461}, names={"Deadwood of the North"}, text="Nafien", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=64.8, y=8.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={8465}, names={"Speak to Salfa"}, text="Nafien", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=64.8, y=8.1},
  {t="L", seg=21, lvl=55, text="Quest XP is far behind in this segment. Grind Felpaw Village to 55; every kill adds Timbermaw reputation as well. The furbolgs stand close together: pull from the edge of the village one at a time, Earth Shock the Shamans' heals, drop Stoneclaw Totem if a second one joins and Healing Wave between pulls. Keep every Runecloth they drop and don't vendor it: Meilosh inside Timbermaw Hold wants 30 for a quest later", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=61.5, y=8.0},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Open the Reputation tab and check Timbermaw Hold before going in", text="It must be Unfriendly or better, or the furbolgs inside attack you. Still Hostile? Kill more Deadwood furbolgs here until it changes. Got Deadwood Headdress Feathers? Nafien takes them 5 at a time (Feathers for Nafien, repeatable, about 550 XP and Timbermaw reputation each); bring later sets on your next tunnel passes"},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Keep any Deadwood or Winterfall Ritual Totem that drops (8470 / 8471)", text="Deadwood and Winterfall furbolgs drop them rarely. Once Timbermaw Hold is Neutral, right-click the totem and hand it to Kernda inside the Hold (Felwood 65.5, 3.5) on one of your tunnel trips"},
  {t="G", seg=21, text="Ride through Timbermaw Hold and take the Winterspring exit. Never attack the Timbermaw furbolgs inside", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=27.7, y=34.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={8465}, names={"Speak to Salfa"}, text="Salfa, at the tunnel exit", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=27.7, y=34.5},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={8464}, names={"Winterfall Activity"}, text="Salfa. Winterfall Shaman and Ursa live in Winterfall Village in the east, next to Everlook", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=27.7, y=34.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={3908}, names={"It's a Secret to Everybody"}, text="Donova Snowden, beside the hot springs to the south-east. She offers The Videre Elixir next: skip it, it needs a long Feralas trip and the chain ends in an elite quest", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={980}, names={"The New Springs"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4842}, names={"Strange Sources"}, text="Donova Snowden. You check the far south of Winterspring later on this pass", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Kill the Winterfall furbolgs in the camp east of Donova (around 41, 44) until one drops an Empty Firewater Flask", text="Pathfinders, Totemics and Den Watchers all drop it. Right-click the flask"},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5083}, names={"Winterfall Firewater"}, text="The Empty Firewater Flask", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=41.0, y=44.0},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5083}, names={"Winterfall Firewater"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5084}, names={"Falling to Corruption"}, text="Keep it: the cauldron is in Felwood and you pass it on your second visit", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4521}, obj={2}, names={"Wild Guardians"}, text="Ragged Owlbeasts in the woods east of the hot springs", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=46.5, y=44.0, path={{30.4,43.9},{30.8,40.9},{39.4,39.1},{40.8,39.1},{42.0,42.1},{45.2,42.1}}},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4842}, names={"Strange Sources"}, text="Ride to the far south until the sky turns dark at Darkwhisper Gorge. The way runs through Frostwhisper Gorge (around 58-66, 65-73), whose Frostmaul Giants and Preservers are elite, level 59-60: stay mounted, keep to the middle and don't stop to fight; if one turns on you, keep riding, your mount outruns it. Reaching the mouth of Darkwhisper Gorge is enough; the demons further in are elite too", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=59.8, y=74.3},
  {t="G", seg=21, text="Ride north to Everlook, back through Frostwhisper Gorge the same way: mounted, without stopping", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.4, y=36.4},
  {t="F", seg=21, arg="Everlook", text="Yugrek, the wind rider master", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.5, y=36.3},
  {t="S", seg=21, arg="Everlook", text="Innkeeper Vizzie, at the inn. Your hearthstone and Astral Recall now bring you back here", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.4, y=38.8},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={6603}, names={"Trouble in Winterspring!"}, text="Meggi Peppinrocker. It goes to Donova on your next pass", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.7, y=38.2},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={3783}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Umi Rumplesnicker", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={6606}, names={"A Little Luck"}, text="Harlo Wigglesworth, in Everlook near the inn (Horde only in Forever)", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.1, y=38.4},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={6606}, names={"A Little Luck"}, text="Witch Doctor Mau'ari, a few steps east. Skip her follow-up, Luck Be With You: it is an elite quest in Frostwhisper Gorge", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.9, y=38.3},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={8464}, names={"Winterfall Activity"}, text="Winterfall Village, just east of Everlook: Shaman, Den Watchers and Ursa. Earth Shock the Shaman's heals; the Ursa hit hardest, so fight them with Stoneclaw Totem down. High Chief Winterfall in the big cave is elite: stay out of it", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=67.0, y=37.0, path={{68.2,41.3}}, cave=true},
  {t="L", seg=21, lvl=56, text="Stay in Winterfall Village and grind to 56 before the yetis. Pull at the edge of the camp, Searing Totem plus Stoneclaw Totem for pairs, Healing Wave between pulls. Being 56 also lets you train new ranks in Thunder Bluff next and shortens the grind at the end of the segment", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=67.0, y=37.0},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={3783}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Ice Thistle Yetis on the hills south-east of the village drop Thick Yeti Furs", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=67.5, y=44.0, path={{65.6,37.6},{65.6,40.0},{66.4,43.6}}},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={3783}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Umi Rumplesnicker, Everlook", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={977}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={977}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Ice Thistle Matriarchs and Patriarchs (level 56-58) higher up in the Ice Thistle Hills. Pull them one at a time; Stoneclaw Totem if a second one walks in", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=69.0, y=41.0},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={977}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Umi Rumplesnicker", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5163}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Umi gives you her Mechanical Yeti", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5163}, obj={1}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Legacki, in Everlook. Use the yeti next to her", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.5, y=38.6},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4521}, obj={1}, names={"Wild Guardians"}, text="Raging Owlbeasts around Starfall Village, just north-west of Everlook", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=58.5, y=31.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=21, arg="Thunder Bluff", text="Yugrek, Everlook. A long flight through several wind rider posts: you do not change, stay on until it lands in Thunder Bluff", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.5, y=36.3},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=21, text="Shaman trainers in the Pools of Vision under Spirit Rise, beside Apothecary Zamah: learn your level 56 spells, and the level 54 ones if you skipped them", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=22.8, y=21.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={1000}, names={"The New Frontier"}, text="Bluff Runner Windstrider, on the central mesa near the inn", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=44.3, y=58.8},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={1000}, names={"The New Frontier"}, text="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem, Elder Rise", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=78.6, y=28.6},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={1123}, names={"Rabine Saturna"}, text="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem. Rabine Saturna is in Moonglade; you go there on your next Felwood trip", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=78.6, y=28.6},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Still carrying Morrowgrain Research (3786) from last segment?", text="Hand 10 Morrowgrain to Bashana Runetotem on Elder Rise now"},
  {t="FLY", seg=21, arg="Ratchet", text="Tal, the wind rider master on the central mesa", zone="Thunder Bluff", map=1456, x=47.0, y=49.8},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4147,4502}, names={"Marvon's Workshop","Volcanic Activity"}, text="Liv Rizzlefix. Skip her follow-ups", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=62.5, y=38.7},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5158}, names={"Seeking Spiritual Aid"}, text="Islen Waterseer, on the coast a short ride south of Ratchet", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=65.8, y=43.8},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5159}, names={"Cleansed Water Returns to Felwood"}, text="Islen Waterseer. The purified water goes back to Greta in Felwood", zone="The Barrens", map=1413, x=65.8, y=43.8},
  {t="FLY", seg=21, arg="Gadgetzan"},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5163}, obj={2}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Sprinkle, in Gadgetzan. Use the yeti next to her", zone="Tanaris", map=1446, x=51.1, y=26.9},
  {t="FLY", seg=21, arg="Marshal's Refuge"},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5163}, obj={3}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Quixxil, in Marshal's Refuge", zone="Un'Goro Crater", map=1449, x=43.7, y=9.4},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Fewer than 15 Un'Goro Slime Samples for ... and a Batch of Ooze (4294)? Kill oozes here now", text="Primal Oozes just south of Marshal's Refuge (around 46, 24) and Glutinous Oozes to the south-west (around 35, 30); Muculent Oozes sit east of the camp (62-74, 25-35). Not every sample tests as pure and you need 5 that do. The next segment passes Marshal's Refuge once more on the way to Silithus, but collecting them now saves a stop there. They stack"},
  {t="H", seg=21, arg="Everlook", text="Hearthstone, or cast Astral Recall"},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5163}, names={"Are We There, Yeti?"}, text="Umi Rumplesnicker", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.9, y=37.6},
  {t="FLY", seg=21, arg="Bloodvenom Post", text="Yugrek, Everlook"},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4521}, names={"Wild Guardians"}, text="Trull Failbane", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.7, y=52.8},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={4741}, names={"Wild Guardians"}, text="Trull Failbane. The Moontouched Owlbeasts are in northern Winterspring", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.7, y=52.8},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5159}, names={"Cleansed Water Returns to Felwood"}, text="Ride south to Greta Mosshoof, Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5165}, names={"Dousing the Flames of Protection"}, text="Greta Mosshoof", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4102}, names={"Cleansing Felwood"}, text="Maybess Riverbreeze. Skip her salve quests", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=46.8, y=83.1},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5165}, names={"Dousing the Flames of Protection"}, text="Shadow Hold, the cave at the back of Jaedenar. Use the Purified Moon Well Water on the four braziers inside: two near the entrance, two further up", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=36.6, y=54.5, path={{35.0,57.5}}, cave=true},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Kill the Jaedenar Darkweavers, Warlocks, Legionnaires and Enforcers along the brazier path until one drops the Blood Red Key", text="It may already have dropped while you doused the braziers: check your bags. They stand all through the lower half of Shadow Hold, around the braziers and Arko'narin's cell. Earth Shock the Darkweavers and Warlocks when they cast; Grounding Totem soaks up a spell. Still no key? Work a little higher, but stay below the succubus Rakaiah (38.3, 50.5) and Shadow Lord Fel'dan's room (38.8, 46.8): they only count once you have their quests, and you come back for both later"},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5202}, names={"A Strange Red Key"}, text="Right-click the Blood Red Key", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=37.5, y=54.0},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5202}, names={"A Strange Red Key"}, text="Captured Arko'narin, in a cell inside Shadow Hold", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=36.2, y=55.5},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5203}, names={"Rescue From Jaedenar"}, text="Captured Arko'narin. She is weak until she gets her gear back", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=36.2, y=55.5},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5203}, names={"Rescue From Jaedenar"}, text="Escort her to her equipment and then out of Shadow Hold. Kill whatever comes at her; drop Stoneclaw Totem to pull extra attackers off her", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=36.2, y=55.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5203}, names={"Rescue From Jaedenar"}, text="Jessir Moonbow, Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.3, y=82.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5204}, names={"Retribution of the Light"}, text="Jessir Moonbow", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.3, y=82.0},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5165}, names={"Dousing the Flames of Protection"}, text="Greta Mosshoof", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5242}, names={"A Final Blow"}, text="Greta Mosshoof", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5204}, names={"Retribution of the Light"}, text="Back in Shadow Hold: kill the succubus Rakaiah", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=38.3, y=50.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5204}, names={"Retribution of the Light"}, text="The Remains of Trey Lightforge, next to where Rakaiah stood", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=38.5, y=50.4},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5385}, names={"The Remains of Trey Lightforge"}, text="The Remains of Trey Lightforge", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=38.5, y=50.4},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5242}, names={"A Final Blow"}, text="The top of Shadow Hold: Moora, Salia and Shadow Lord Fel'dan. Pull the guards away first and Earth Shock their casts; take Fel'dan's head. Lord Banehollow (elite, 59) is in the chamber past Fel'dan (around 36, 44): don't go further", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=38.8, y=46.8},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5385}, names={"The Remains of Trey Lightforge"}, text="Jessir Moonbow, Emerald Sanctuary", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.3, y=82.0, path={{39.8,54.9},{44.0,64.2},{45.8,70.8},{46.0,75.9}}},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5242}, names={"A Final Blow"}, text="Greta Mosshoof", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=51.2, y=82.1},
  {t="G", seg=21, text="Ride north up the road to Felpaw Village", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=60.2, y=5.8, path={{55.6,81.6},{55.6,49.9},{53.2,46.3},{52.6,42.7},{49.2,38.2},{49.2,34.3},{50.8,30.4},{55.0,25.6},{58.4,17.5},{58.6,14.5},{55.8,10.6},{55.8,7.6},{56.8,6.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5084}, names={"Falling to Corruption"}, text="The Deadwood Cauldron in the middle of Felpaw Village", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=60.2, y=5.8},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5085}, names={"Mystery Goo"}, text="The Deadwood Cauldron", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=60.2, y=5.8},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Go into Timbermaw Hold", text="Neutral with Timbermaw and carrying a Ritual Totem? Hand it to Kernda in the main hall on the way (8470 / 8471). Nafien at the entrance still takes Deadwood Headdress Feathers 5 at a time"},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={6031}, names={"Runecloth"}, text="Meilosh, in the main hall of Timbermaw Hold beside Kernda. Needs Friendly with Timbermaw (the Felpaw and Winterfall grinds should have got you there) and 30 Runecloth. Not Friendly yet or short of cloth? Take it on a later tunnel pass", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=65.7, y=2.8, path={{65.6,7.3}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={6031}, names={"Runecloth"}, text="Meilosh", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=65.7, y=2.8},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Take the branch of Timbermaw Hold that leads to Moonglade"},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={1123}, names={"Rabine Saturna"}, text="Rabine Saturna, in Nighthaven", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=51.7, y=45.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={1124}, names={"Wasteland"}, text="Keep Rabine's Letter: Layo Starstrike is in Silithus, in the next segment", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=51.7, y=45.1},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5527}, names={"A Reliquary of Purity"}, text="Rabine Saturna, same visit (needs 56). The Dusty Reliquary is in Southwind Village in Silithus, where Layo's quests send you next segment, and that segment flies back here at its end", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=51.7, y=45.1},
  {t="F", seg=21, arg="Moonglade", text="Faustron, the Horde wind rider master by the lake south-west of Nighthaven", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=32.1, y=66.6},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Go back into Timbermaw Hold and take the Winterspring exit"},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={8464}, names={"Winterfall Activity"}, text="Salfa. From now on Salfa also takes Winterfall Spirit Beads 5 at a time (Beads for Salfa, repeatable, about 575 XP and Timbermaw reputation each): the Winterfall furbolgs drop them, so hand in each set as you pass by", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=27.7, y=34.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5085}, names={"Mystery Goo"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5086}, names={"Toxic Horrors"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={6603}, names={"Trouble in Winterspring!"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5082}, names={"Threat of the Winterfall"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4842}, names={"Strange Sources"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5082,5082}, obj={1,3}, names={"Threat of the Winterfall","Threat of the Winterfall"}, text="The Winterfall camp east of Donova: Pathfinders and Totemics (the camp near Salfa has more of both). Kill the one Den Watcher here too (1 of 8). Only 4 Den Watchers stand in the west, so you clear both camps twice for the 8. Kill the Totemics' totems first", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=41.0, y=44.0},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Go back through Timbermaw Hold into Felwood for the Toxic Horrors", text="On the way, kill the three Winterfall Den Watchers at the camp just south-east of Salfa (around 30.5, 36): 4 of 8"},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5086}, names={"Toxic Horrors"}, text="Irontree Woods, south-west of Felpaw Village: Toxic Horrors drop the droplets", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=49.3, y=25.0},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Go back through Timbermaw Hold to Winterspring", text="Neutral with Timbermaw and carrying a Ritual Totem? Hand it to Kernda inside the Hold now (8470 / 8471). Didn't get Meilosh's Runecloth quest earlier? Try again now"},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Kill the 3 Den Watchers at the camp just south-east of Salfa (30.5, 36.3) again: they have respawned since you passed", text="That makes 7 of 8. Spare beads? Salfa is right there"},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5082}, obj={2}, names={"Threat of the Winterfall"}, text="The 8th is the lone Den Watcher at the east camp, which has respawned too. Donova is a short ride back west", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=41.6, y=42.6},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5082,5086}, names={"Threat of the Winterfall","Toxic Horrors"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2, path={{40.8,39.1},{31.8,40.3},{30.4,41.5}}},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5087}, names={"Winterfall Runners"}, text="Donova Snowden", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={5087}, names={"Winterfall Runners"}, text="Winterfall Runners leave the Timbermaw tunnel and walk east toward Winterfall Village. Kill them for the Winterfall Crate; Earthbind Totem keeps them from running on", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=28.0, y=34.5},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={5087}, names={"Winterfall Runners"}, text="Donova Snowden. Skip High Chief Winterfall (elite)", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=31.3, y=45.2},
  {t="C", seg=21, q={4741}, names={"Wild Guardians"}, text="Moontouched Owlbeasts (57-58) in the north, past Starfall Village. Ursius, an elite bear, stands at the south edge of their area (around 64, 24): hunt the owlbeasts north of him and swing wide of him when you ride south to Winterfall Village afterwards. Pull one at a time, Healing Wave between pulls. If a Blue-feathered Necklace drops, keep it (don't farm for it)", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=63.5, y=17.0, path={{30.4,41.5},{31.8,40.3},{38.4,40.0},{47.8,37.0},{49.8,39.7},{53.4,38.5},{55.8,34.3},{54.2,17.5},{56.6,13.9},{62.2,13.3},{64.6,13.9}}},
  {t="L", seg=21, lvl=57, text="Still behind. Grind Winterfall Village to 57 before you leave: Silithus in the next segment is level 55-60", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=67.0, y=37.0},
  {t="G", seg=21, text="Everlook", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=60.4, y=36.4},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={6029,6030}, names={"The Everlook Report","Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff"}, text="Gregor Greystone. Both are deliveries to the Plaguelands, at the end of the route: keep them", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.3, y=39.0},
  {t="A", seg=21, q={5601}, names={"Sister Pamela"}, text="Jessica Redpath. Also for the Plaguelands", zone="Winterspring", map=1452, x=61.3, y=39.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=21, arg="Bloodvenom Post", text="Yugrek, Everlook"},
  {t="T", seg=21, q={4741}, names={"Wild Guardians"}, text="Trull Failbane. Skip Wild Guardians part 3; it sends you back to Winterspring", zone="Felwood", map=1448, x=34.7, y=52.8},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Got a Blue-feathered Necklace?", text="Right-click it and hand it to Trull (Guarding Secrets, 4882). Skip his follow-up: it goes to Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff, which the route does not visit again"},
  {t="N", seg=21, arg="Segment done. Next segment flies from Bloodvenom Post to Orgrimmar", text="Keep 3568, 4294, 4293, 3542, 1124, 5527, 6029, 6030 and 5601 in the log. Your hearthstone is set to Everlook"},
  {t="FLY", seg=22, arg="Orgrimmar", text="Brakkar, the Bloodvenom Post wind rider master. You start at level 57 with your hearthstone set to Everlook"},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8276}, names={"Taking Back Silithus"}, text="Cenarion Emissary Blackhoof, in the Valley of Strength close to the foot of the wind rider tower", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=47.6, y=65.8},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Optional dungeon: Blackmaw Hold, levels 55-60", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is a furbolg city behind the big gate in Azshara. It has 5 Horde quests, but who gives them is not published yet: ask around Valormok and take what is offered; the addon logs it so these steps can be filled in.", dg=20, run=true},
  {t="S", seg=22, arg="Orgrimmar", text="Innkeeper Gryshka, Valley of Strength. From now on your hearthstone and Astral Recall bring you back here, next to the zeppelin"},
  {t="FLY", seg=22, arg="Marshal's Refuge", text="Doras, on the wind rider tower"},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Ride to the north-west corner of Un'Goro and take the ridge path west into Silithus", text="It comes out at Valor's Rest, the graveyard in the north-east of Silithus. Short of Un'Goro Slime Samples for ... and a Batch of Ooze (4294)? Primal Oozes just south of Marshal's Refuge drop them"},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={1124}, names={"Wasteland"}, text="Layo Starstrike, Valor's Rest", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=81.9, y=18.9},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={1125}, names={"The Spirits of Southwind"}, text="Layo Starstrike", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=81.9, y=18.9},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={1125}, names={"The Spirits of Southwind"}, text="Southwind Village, south-west of Valor's Rest: Tortured Druids and Tortured Sentinels drift through the ruins. Earth Shock the druids when they start a cast", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=62.0, y=55.0},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={5527}, names={"A Reliquary of Purity"}, text="Open the Dusty Reliquary in a ruined house in Southwind Village", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=63.2, y=55.4},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={1125}, names={"The Spirits of Southwind"}, text="Layo Starstrike", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=81.9, y=18.9},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={1126}, names={"Hive in the Tower"}, text="Layo Starstrike", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=81.9, y=18.9},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={1126}, names={"Hive in the Tower"}, text="Climb the tower in the west part of Southwind Village and disturb the silithid hive at the top. Hive'Ashi Ambushers jump you: drop Stoneclaw Totem first, keep Healing Wave ready, and loot the Encrusted Silithid Object", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=60.4, y=52.6},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={1126}, names={"Hive in the Tower"}, text="Layo Starstrike", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=81.9, y=18.9},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={6844}, names={"Umber, Archivist"}, text="Layo Starstrike. Umber is in Moonglade; you go there at the end of the segment", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=81.9, y=18.9},
  {t="G", seg=22, text="Ride north out of Southwind before you turn west to Cenarion Hold: an elite Hive'Ashi pack sits on the sand south-east of the Hold (around 53, 47)", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=48.8, y=36.6, path={{78.3,12.7},{68.4,11.8},{67.2,12.4},{66.4,15.1},{58.0,15.1},{56.8,13.3},{54.4,13.3},{48.6,19.6},{45.6,21.1},{47.0,34.0}}},
  {t="F", seg=22, arg="Cenarion Hold", text="Runk Windtamer, the Horde wind rider master"},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8276}, names={"Taking Back Silithus"}, text="Windcaller Proudhorn", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.1, y=38.3},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8280}, names={"Securing the Supply Lines"}, text="Windcaller Proudhorn. If he does not offer it after Taking Back Silithus, skip it and Stepping Up Security (8281)", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.1, y=38.3},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8277}, names={"Deadly Desert Venom"}, text="Beetix Ficklespragg", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.6},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8284}, names={"The Twilight Mystery"}, text="Geologist Larksbane", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.7, y=37.5},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8318}, names={"Secret Communication"}, text="Bor Wildmane", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=48.6, y=37.8},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={9416}, names={"Report to General Kirika"}, text="Scout Bloodfist. General Kirika is south of the Hold; you pass the camp later", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.0, y=36.7},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8858,8859}, names={"Secrets of the Colossus - Regal","Secrets of the Colossus - Zora"}, text="Colossus Researchers Eazel and Sophia, inside the Hold, each hand you a husk. Eazel's (Regal) goes to Overseer Oilfist at Thorium Point, Sophia's (Zora) to Lord Maxwell Tyrosus at Light's Hope Chapel: the next segment stops at both, about 10,000 XP each. Skip Nestor's husk: it goes to Booty Bay", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.6, y=37.3},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8277,8280}, names={"Deadly Desert Venom","Securing the Supply Lines"}, text="East and north-east of the Hold: Stonelash Scorpids, Sand Skitterers and Dredge Strikers share the open sand. Stay east of Hive'Ashi, the big hive north-west of the Hold: its silithids are elite", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=61.0, y=28.0},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8284}, names={"The Twilight Mystery"}, text="Ride back past the Hold, go round the south and west sides of Hive'Ashi and north to the Twilight Base Camp in the north-west: Twilight Tablet Fragments lie on the ground around the camp. Leave the three Whirling Invaders (around 28, 27) alone: they rarely drop a fragment and The Windreaver, a level 60 elite elemental, starts beside them. He patrols the east and south sides of the camp, which you cross on the way in: spot him and let him pass, and skip the lone fragment at the south end (about 20, 22). Keep any Elemental Air the Dust Stormers drop if you want Elemental Mastery", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=24.0, y=12.0, path={{62.0,17.2},{58.6,16.0},{56.8,13.3},{49.6,15.4},{45.4,20.5},{42.4,17.2},{28.2,15.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8280}, names={"Securing the Supply Lines"}, text="Windcaller Proudhorn, Cenarion Hold", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.1, y=38.3, path={{26.0,15.1},{36.2,15.4},{38.0,17.2},{42.4,17.2},{45.6,20.8},{47.0,31.9}}},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8281}, names={"Stepping Up Security"}, text="Windcaller Proudhorn", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.1, y=38.3},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8284}, names={"The Twilight Mystery"}, text="Geologist Larksbane", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.7, y=37.5},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8285}, names={"The Deserter"}, text="Geologist Larksbane", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.7, y=37.5},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8277}, names={"Deadly Desert Venom"}, text="Beetix Ficklespragg", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.6},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8278}, names={"Noggle's Last Hope"}, text="Beetix Ficklespragg", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.6},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8285}, names={"The Deserter"}, text="Hermit Ortell, in his hut in the south-east. Ride east first and then south past Southwind, so the elite silithids south-east of the Hold stay on your right. Below Southwind, kill the Stonelash Pincers and Dredge Crushers you pass: Beetix wants 3 Pincer stingers and Proudhorn 20 Crushers", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8279}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon"}, text="Hermit Ortell", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8278}, obj={2}, names={"Noggle's Last Hope"}, text="Leave the hut to the north-west: Hive'Regal starts just south-west of it. Finish the 3 Stonelash Pincer stingers on the sand here, and keep killing every Dredge Crusher you meet", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=60.0, y=62.0},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8278,8278}, obj={1,3}, names={"Noggle's Last Hope","Noggle's Last Hope"}, text="Ride west along the north edge of Hive'Regal, then south-west into the foothills below Hive'Zora: Stonelash Flayers and Rock Stalkers", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=38.0, y=78.0},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8279}, obj={2}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon"}, text="Keep west along the foothills to Twilight Keeper Exeter's camp in the far south-west. Pull the cultists one or two at a time, Earth Shock the Geolords and Stonecallers when they cast, and drop Stoneclaw Totem if more come. Every Twilight cultist can drop Encrypted Twilight Texts: collect 10 for Bor", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=16.1, y=86.4},
  {t="G", seg=22, text="Ride back east along the foothills, then north between Hive'Zora and the Hold. Dredge Crushers and Stonelash Pincers roam this strip", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=42.0, y=55.0},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8279}, obj={1}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon"}, text="Twilight Keeper Mayna's camp, north of Hive'Zora. An elite Twilight Prophet can walk the west side of the zone: let him pass", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=26.4, y=36.6},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8279,8281,8318}, obj={3,0,0}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon","Stepping Up Security","Secret Communication"}, text="Twilight Keeper Havunth at the Twilight Post, just south-west of the Hold. Finish the 20 Dredge Crushers on the sand around both camps, and the 10 Encrypted Twilight Texts. Keep the texts: Ortell's next quest takes them first", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=40.9, y=42.2},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8278}, names={"Noggle's Last Hope"}, text="Beetix Ficklespragg, Cenarion Hold", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.6},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8281}, names={"Stepping Up Security"}, text="Windcaller Proudhorn", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.1, y=38.3},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8282}, names={"Noggle's Lost Satchel"}, text="Noggle Ficklespragg. Don't hand Bor his texts yet", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.5},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={9416}, names={"Report to General Kirika"}, text="General Kirika, at the Horde camp south of the Hold. Elite Hive'Ashi silithids roam the sand right below the Hold: pass them on their west side", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=50.8, y=69.5},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={9422}, names={"Scouring the Desert"}, text="General Kirika. Note where the Silithyst Extractor stands in the camp", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=50.8, y=69.5},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8282}, names={"Noggle's Lost Satchel"}, text="Hive'Regal's elites start just south of the camp, so ride due west to about 45, 71 before you turn south to the mountains. Noggle's Satchel lies on the ground among the Stonelash Flayers. Deathclasp, a level 59 elite scorpid, rests less than 30 yards south-east of it: come in from the north-west, grab the satchel and leave. If she comes for you, drop Earthbind Totem and run north", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=44.6, y=91.4},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8279}, names={"The Twilight Lexicon"}, text="Hermit Ortell. Ride back north the same way, then east past Kirika's camp, keeping north of Hive'Regal", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8, path={{44.6,94.2},{46.8,95.7},{55.4,99.0},{60.0,97.5},{61.8,94.2},{61.8,80.1},{64.8,75.9},{64.6,70.5}}},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8323}, names={"True Believers"}, text="Hermit Ortell", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8323}, names={"True Believers"}, text="Give him the 10 Encrypted Twilight Texts. Bor's quest drops back to 0 of 10; you refill it on the way back", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={8287}, names={"A Terrible Purpose"}, text="Hermit Ortell", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=67.2, y=69.8},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={9422}, names={"Scouring the Desert"}, text="Ride north-west from Ortell's hut to the Silithyst geyser at 60.6, 63.0, click the Silithyst and walk it south-west to the Silithyst Extractor in Kirika's camp: that line stays well north of Hive'Regal. Empty? Try the geyser at 59.3, 58.8 next. Use the one beside the hut (64.0, 70.9) only as a last resort, and from it walk north-west to about 58, 66 before you turn west: Hive'Regal elites stand just south of the straight line. Go on foot, without mount or Ghost Wolf: mounting drops it, and carrying it flags you for PvP. No Silithyst on any of them? Skip this and the next step", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=60.6, y=63.0},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={9422}, names={"Scouring the Desert"}, text="General Kirika", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=50.8, y=69.5},
  {t="C", seg=22, q={8318}, names={"Secret Communication"}, text="Ride north-west to the Twilight Post around Havunth's spot: Twilight Avengers, Geolords and Stonecallers. Collect 10 more Encrypted Twilight Texts for Bor, Earth Shocking the casters", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=39.0, y=43.5},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8282}, names={"Noggle's Lost Satchel"}, text="Noggle Ficklespragg, Cenarion Hold", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=51.6, y=38.5},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8287}, names={"A Terrible Purpose"}, text="Commander Mar'alith. Skip his elite follow-up", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=49.2, y=34.2},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={8318}, names={"Secret Communication"}, text="Bor Wildmane", zone="Silithus", map=1451, x=48.6, y=37.8},
  {t="H", seg=22, arg="Orgrimmar", text="Hearthstone from Cenarion Hold. Save Astral Recall for the way back from Moonglade"},
  {t="FLY", seg=22, arg="Moonglade", text="Doras, on the Orgrimmar wind rider tower. You land at Faustron, by the lake south-west of Nighthaven. The Moonglade quests below are worth about 20,000 XP"},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={6844}, names={"Umber, Archivist"}, text="Umber, in Nighthaven", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=44.9, y=35.6},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={6845}, names={"Uncovering Past Secrets"}, text="Umber", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=44.9, y=35.6},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={6845}, names={"Uncovering Past Secrets"}, text="Rabine Saturna", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=51.7, y=45.1},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={5527}, names={"A Reliquary of Purity"}, text="Rabine Saturna, same visit. Skip her follow-up: Shards of the Felvine is in Dire Maul", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=51.7, y=45.1},
  {t="A", seg=22, q={1185}, names={"Under the Chitin Was..."}, text="Umber", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=44.9, y=35.6},
  {t="T", seg=22, q={1185}, names={"Under the Chitin Was..."}, text="Umber", zone="Moonglade", map=1450, x=44.9, y=35.6},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Cast Astral Recall (back to Orgrimmar)", text="It is off cooldown, since you used the hearthstone to leave Silithus"},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Saved cloth? Orgrimmar takes cloth donations", text="Rashona Straglash (63.6, 51.2) and Vehena in the Valley of Spirits (37.7, 87.9) each take 60 wool, 60 silk, 60 mageweave and then 60 runecloth (7826, 7827, 7831, 7824 and 7833-7836). Every hand-in gives experience, which may bring 58 before you train"},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=22, text="Valley of Wisdom: learn your level 58 spells if you have reached 58. Not 58 yet? Skip it; Haromm in Stonard is an optional stop next segment. The trainers also offer Elemental Mastery (8410) if you want it for the end of the route", zone="Orgrimmar", map=1454, x=38.8, y=36.4},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Optional dungeon: Shaper's Terrace, levels 58-60", text="New Forever dungeon, not checked in game yet. It is in the hills of Un'Goro Crater. It has 3 Horde quests (from level 55), but who gives them is not published yet: ask around Marshal's Refuge and take what is offered; the addon logs it so these steps can be filled in.", dg=21, run=true},
  {t="N", seg=22, arg="Take the zeppelin to the Undercity", text="Leave by the main gate; the zeppelin tower is just outside. Board the zeppelin to Tirisfal Glades (Undercity), not the one to Grom'gol. Keep 3568, 4294, 4293, 3542, 6029, 6030, 5601, 8858 and 8859 in the log; your hearthstone stays on Orgrimmar until you bind in the Undercity", zone="Durotar", map=1411, x=50.8, y=13.5},
  {t="N", seg=23, arg="You arrive at the zeppelin tower outside the Undercity", text="Walk south into the ruined city and take an elevator down. Your hearthstone and Astral Recall still point at Orgrimmar until you bind at the inn here"},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={3568}, names={"Seeping Corruption"}, text="Chemist Cuely, in the Apothecarium", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.7, y=71.4},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={3569}, names={"Seeping Corruption"}, text="Chemist Cuely", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.7, y=71.4},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={3569}, names={"Seeping Corruption"}, text="Thersa Windsong, right next to him", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=49.0, y=70.8},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4133}, names={"Vivian Lagrave"}, text="Apothecary Zinge in the Apothecarium. It sends you to Vivian Lagrave in Kargath. Needs level 50.", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=50.1, y=68.0, dg=16},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={3570}, names={"Seeping Corruption"}, text="Chemist Cuely", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.7, y=71.4},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={3570}, names={"Seeping Corruption"}, text="Chemist Cuely, straight away: it has no objectives", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=48.7, y=71.4},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={4294,4293}, names={"... and a Batch of Ooze","A Sample of Slime..."}, text="Use the Testing Equipment next to Chemist Fuely on your Un'Goro and Felwood slime samples until you have 5 Pure Un'Goro Samples and 5 Corrupted Felwood Samples. The route does not go back to Kalimdor: if one test is still short after all your samples, abandon that quest", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=47.5, y=73.3},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4294,4293}, names={"... and a Batch of Ooze","A Sample of Slime..."}, text="Chemist Fuely. Skip his follow-up (Melding of Influences): it needs another Un'Goro trip", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=47.5, y=73.3},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={3542}, names={"Delivery to Andron Gant"}, text="Andron Gant, a few steps from the chemists. Do not take his follow-up: it goes back to Azshara", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=54.8, y=76.3},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5961}, names={"The Champion of the Banshee Queen"}, text="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, in the Royal Quarter", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=58.1, y=91.8},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5094}, names={"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!"}, text="Harbinger Balthazad. Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff offer the same quest: take only one", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=63.9, y=44.1},
  {t="S", seg=23, arg="Undercity", text="Innkeeper Norman. From now on your hearthstone and Astral Recall bring you back here"},
  {t="FLY", seg=23, arg="Kargath", text="Michael Garrett, the bat handler by the west elevator. A long flight", zone="Undercity", map=1458, x=63.2, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={3821}, names={"Dreadmaul Rock"}, text="Thal'trak Proudtusk, Kargath", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=3.4, y=48.1},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4061}, names={"The Rise of the Machines"}, text="Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania, Kargath", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=3.0, y=47.8},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4133}, names={"Vivian Lagrave"}, zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.9, y=47.8, dg=16, req=4133},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4134}, names={"Lost Thunderbrew Recipe"}, text="The Lost Thunderbrew Recipe drops from Hurley Blackbreath in the Grim Guzzler bar.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.9, y=47.8, dg=16, req=4133},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4081}, names={"KILL ON SIGHT: Dark Iron Dwarves"}, text="The WANTED poster in Kargath. Kill 15 Anvilrage Guardsmen, 10 Wardens and 5 Footmen in the first part of the dungeon.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=3.7, y=47.4, dg=16},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={7201}, names={"The Last Element"}, text="Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave in Kargath. 10 Essence of the Elements from the golems and elementals inside.", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.9, y=47.8, dg=16},
  {t="FLY", seg=23, arg="Thorium Point", text="Gorrik, the Kargath wind rider master", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=4.0, y=44.8},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={8858}, names={"Secrets of the Colossus - Regal"}, text="Overseer Oilfist, a short walk north-east of the wind rider master at Thorium Point. Hand him Regal's husk before you ride south", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=38.1, y=27.0},
  {t="N", seg=23, arg="Ride south from Thorium Point into Blackrock Mountain, cross it on the chain walkways and leave by the Burning Steppes exit", text="Stay on the open walkways: the doors inside lead to dungeons"},
  {t="F", seg=23, arg="Flame Crest", text="Follow the north edge of the Burning Steppes east to Flame Crest. Vahgruk is the wind rider master", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.7, y=24.2},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4726}, names={"Broodling Essence"}, text="Tinkee Steamboil. She gives you the Draco-Incarcinatrix 900", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=24.0},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4296}, names={"Tablet of the Seven"}, text="Maxwort Uberglint", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=23.9},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={4296}, names={"Tablet of the Seven"}, text="The Tablet of the Seven in the ruins of Thaurissan, south-west of Flame Crest. Right-click it to copy it", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=54.1, y=40.8},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={4061}, names={"The Rise of the Machines"}, text="War Reavers south of Flame Crest drop Fractured Elemental Shards; so do the Greater Obsidian Elementals. Keep any Elemental Earth (obsidian elementals) and Elemental Fire (Flamekin) that drops: Elemental Mastery wants one of each", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=63.0, y=36.0},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={4726}, names={"Broodling Essence"}, text="Scalding Broodlings just south-west and east of Flame Crest (around 58-61, 31 and 72-78, 28): zap one with the Draco-Incarcinatrix, kill it and loot the essence it leaves. Black Broodlings further east count too, but elite Black Dragonspawn and Black Wyrmkin (52-54) stand among them (about 81-94, 26-58), and more elites guard the broodlings in the south (about 56-58, 61-64 and 76-78, 62). Stay in the north of the zone, west of about 80", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=59.0, y=31.0},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={3821}, names={"Dreadmaul Rock"}, text="Sha'ni Proudtusk's Remains on Dreadmaul Rock, to the east", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=79.8, y=45.5},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={3822}, names={"Krom'Grul"}, text="Sha'ni Proudtusk", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=79.8, y=45.5},
  {t="C", seg=23, q={3822}, names={"Krom'Grul"}, text="Krom'Grul, in the caves of Dreadmaul Rock. Clear the Firegut ogres at the cave mouth first: Earth Shock the Ogre Mages' casts, and drop a Stoneclaw Totem when a second ogre joins", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=79.7, y=47.4},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4726}, names={"Broodling Essence"}, text="Tinkee Steamboil, Flame Crest. Don't take Felnok Steelspring: it goes back to Winterspring", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=24.0},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4296}, names={"Tablet of the Seven"}, text="Maxwort Uberglint", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=23.9},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4123}, names={"The Heart of the Mountain"}, text="Maxwort Uberglint at Flame Crest. The Heart of the Mountain is in the vault. Needs level 50.", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=23.9, dg=16},
  {t="FLY", seg=23, arg="Kargath", text="Vahgruk, the Flame Crest wind rider master", zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.7, y=24.2},
  {t="N", seg=23, arg="Optional dungeon: Blackrock Depths, levels 52-60", text="Blackrock Depths is inside Blackrock Mountain, between the Searing Gorge and the Burning Steppes: go in, take the chain down to the lowest ring and follow the tunnel to the portal. It is long; most groups do it in parts. Quests you picked up for it: Lost Thunderbrew Recipe, The Heart of the Mountain, KILL ON SIGHT: Dark Iron Dwarves, The Last Element.", zone="Searing Gorge", map=1427, x=34.8, y=85.3, dg=16, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4123}, names={"The Heart of the Mountain"}, zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=65.2, y=23.9, dg=16},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4136}, names={"Ribbly Screwspigot"}, zone="Burning Steppes", map=1428, x=66.1, y=21.9, dg=16},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={3822}, names={"Krom'Grul"}, text="Thal'trak Proudtusk", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=3.4, y=48.1},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4081}, names={"KILL ON SIGHT: Dark Iron Dwarves"}, zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=5.8, y=47.5, dg=16},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4061}, names={"The Rise of the Machines"}, text="Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=3.0, y=47.8},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={7201}, names={"The Last Element"}, zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.9, y=47.8, dg=16},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4134}, names={"Lost Thunderbrew Recipe"}, zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=2.9, y=47.8, dg=16},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={4062}, names={"The Rise of the Machines"}, text="Hierophant Theodora Mulvadania", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=3.0, y=47.8},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={4062}, names={"The Rise of the Machines"}, text="Lotwil Veriatus, at his camp east of Kargath. Skip his follow-up (Blackrock Depths)", zone="Badlands", map=1418, x=25.9, y=44.9, path={{5.9,51.0},{6.7,56.1},{8.5,59.1},{12.7,60.0},{16.9,56.1},{21.1,49.9},{24.5,49.6},{25.6,47.8}}},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=23, text="Optional, only if you are 58 now and did not learn your level 58 spells in Orgrimmar (most players reach 58 with the Kargath hand-ins): ride back to Gorrik in Kargath and fly to Stonard. Haromm is the only shaman trainer in the Eastern Kingdoms, and he also offers Elemental Mastery if you want it (see the Bath'rah steps near the end)", zone="Swamp of Sorrows", map=1435, x=48.2, y=57.9},
  {t="H", seg=23, arg="Undercity", text="Cast Astral Recall (or use your hearthstone) from Lotwil's camp, or from Stonard if you trained: both bring you to the Undercity now. Both on cooldown? Fly to the Undercity from Kargath or Stonard"},
  {t="G", seg=23, text="Ride out of the Undercity and east along the road to the Bulwark at the east edge of Tirisfal Glades", zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=83.1, y=68.9},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={5094}, names={"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!"}, text="High Executor Derrington", zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=83.1, y=68.9},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5096}, names={"Scarlet Diversions"}, text="High Executor Derrington. Before you ride off, take a Flame in a Bottle from the Box of Incendiaries right beside him: you need it to burn the Scarlet command tent", zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=83.1, y=68.9},
  {t="T", seg=23, q={6029}, names={"The Everlook Report"}, text="Argent Officer Garush", zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=83.2, y=68.5},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={5901}, names={"A Plague Upon Thee"}, text="Mickey Levine. The termite mounds are in the Eastern Plaguelands", zone="Tirisfal Glades", map=1420, x=83.3, y=72.3},
  {t="A", seg=23, q={6004}, names={"Unfinished Business"}, text="Kirsta Deepshadow: ride north-east past the Scarlet camp to her hiding spot near the Northridge Lumber Mill", zone="Western Plaguelands", map=1422, x=51.9, y=28.1},
